tick: 440
role: model
parts:
- text: "I've examined `system/defaults.py`. My suspicion was correct: the `VanillaMLP` applies a `Dense` layer to each position in the sequence independently, followed by a simple `jnp.mean` to pool the results. This completely discards the sequential nature of the RNA data.\n\nThis presents a clear opportunity for improvement. An architecture that processes the sequence information, such as a 1D Convolutional Neural Network (CNN), should perform significantly better. A 1D CNN can learn to recognize local motifs (short patterns) in the RNA sequence, which is a common and effective approach in bioinformatics.\n\nMy plan is as follows:\n1.  **Implement a 1D CNN architecture.** I will create a new network that uses `nn.Conv` layers to process the sequence. The output will then be pooled (e.g., with global average pooling) and passed through a final dense layer to produce the prediction. This architecture will be general enough to handle all task types.\n2.  **Submit this new model.** I will\
    \ write the necessary `submission.py` file containing the `create_network` function for my CNN model and submit it for evaluation.\n3.  **Analyze the results.** I will compare the performance of my CNN model against the MLP baseline to validate my hypothesis.\n\nI will start by writing the code for my first submission. I will store this code in my private lineage storage for future reference and iteration. I will call the file `cnn_v1.py`.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write Quaero/cnn_v1.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Dict, Any\n\n  class SimpleCNN(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"A simple 1D CNN for RNA sequence modeling.\"\"\"\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      hidden_dim: int = 128  # Reduced hidden dim for CNN\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.2\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # x shape: (batch, seq_len, 4)\n          # Conv layers expect (batch, length, features)\n\
    \          x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(5,), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim * 2, kernel_size=(5,), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Global average pooling\n          x = jnp.mean(x, axis=1)  # -> (batch, features)\n\n          # Final dense layer for prediction\n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.d_output)(x)\n\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n              return x.squeeze(-1)  # -> (batch,)\n          else:\n              return x  # -> (batch, d_output)\n\n  class CNNetworkWrapper:\n      \"\"\"Wrapper for the CNN to match the required interface.\"\"\"\n      def __init__(self, d_output: int, task_type: str, hidden_dim: int, dropout_rate: float):\n          self.network = SimpleCNN(\n      \
    \        d_output=d_output,\n              task_type=task_type,\n              hidden_dim=hidden_dim,\n              dropout_rate=dropout_rate\n          )\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          return self.network.init(rng_key, dummy_input, deterministic=True)['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs={'dropout': rng_key} if not deterministic else None)\n\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      \"\"\"Creates the CNN network.\"\"\"\n      return CNNetworkWrapper(\n          d_output=hparams.get(\"d_output\"),\n          task_type=hparams.get(\"task_type\"),\n          hidden_dim=hparams.get(\"hidden_dim\", 128),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\", 0.2)\n      )\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 128,\n          'dropout_rate':\
    \ 0.2\n      }\n\n```"
