parts:
- text: "I have saved the code for my new Multi-Kernel CNN model. Now, I will submit it for evaluation. My hypothesis is that by capturing features at multiple scales (using kernel sizes 3, 5, and 7), this model will build a richer representation of the RNA sequences and further improve performance over my single-kernel CNN.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Multi-Kernel 1D CNN for Sequence Modeling\"\ntags: \"cnn, 1d cnn, multi-kernel\"\nabstract: |\n  This model enhances the previous 1D CNN by incorporating multiple parallel convolutional layers with different kernel sizes (3, 5, and 7). The feature maps from each kernel are concatenated, allowing the network to simultaneously learn and integrate local motifs of various lengths. This multi-scale approach aims to create a more robust sequence representation and improve performance across the diverse RNA modeling tasks.\ncontent: |\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import random\n  from typing\
    \ import Dict, Any, Sequence\n\n  class MultiKernelCNN(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"A 1D CNN with multiple kernel sizes for RNA sequence modeling.\"\"\"\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      num_filters: int = 128\n      kernel_sizes: Sequence[int] = (3, 5, 7)\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.25\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # x shape: (batch, seq_len, 4)\n          \n          conv_outputs = []\n          for kernel_size in self.kernel_sizes:\n              conv_out = nn.Conv(\n                  features=self.num_filters,\n                  kernel_size=(kernel_size,),\n                  padding='SAME'\n              )(x)\n              conv_outputs.append(conv_out)\n          \n          x = jnp.concatenate(conv_outputs, axis=-1)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          x = jnp.mean(x, axis=1)\n\n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.d_output)(x)\n\
    \n          if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n              return x.squeeze(-1)\n          else:\n              return x\n\n  class CNNetworkWrapper:\n      \"\"\"Wrapper for the CNN to match the required interface.\"\"\"\n      def __init__(self, d_output: int, task_type: str, num_filters: int, kernel_sizes: Sequence[int], dropout_rate: float):\n          self.network = MultiKernelCNN(\n              d_output=d_output,\n              task_type=task_type,\n              num_filters=num_filters,\n              kernel_sizes=kernel_sizes,\n              dropout_rate=dropout_rate\n          )\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                                       dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if not deterministic\
    \ and rng_key is None:\n              rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n          \n          return self.network.apply(\n              {'params': params}, \n              x, \n              deterministic=deterministic, \n              rngs={'dropout': rng_key} if not deterministic else None\n          )\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      \"\"\"Creates the Multi-Kernel CNN network.\"\"\"\n      return CNNetworkWrapper(\n          d_output=hparams.get(\"d_output\"),\n          task_type=hparams.get(\"task_type\"),\n          num_filters=hparams.get(\"num_filters\"),\n          kernel_sizes=hparams.get(\"kernel_sizes\"),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\")\n      )\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'num_filters': 128,\n          'kernel_sizes': [3, 5, 7],\n          'dropout_rate': 0.25\n      }\n```"
