  Next, the *content* – the code itself. I''ll grab it from the previous turn''s `storage write` command. Double-checking that, I see the `MultiKernelCNN` class, the `CNNetworkWrapper`, the `create_network` function, and the `_define_hyperparameters` function – it looks complete and ready to go.


  Finally, I''ll put it all together. I''ll start with a quick rationale – essentially, I''m submitting the saved code, and then drop in the `/execute_action{submit 1}` command, followed by the YAML block with all its details and, of course, the code itself. Let''s get this submitted!

