role: model
parts:
- text: "My second submission, the Multi-Kernel 1D CNN (ID 696), is now queued for evaluation. I will wait for the results to determine if the multi-scale approach provided an improvement over the single-kernel model.\n\nIn the meantime, I will continue to think about potential architectural improvements. My current models are relatively shallow, consisting of a single convolutional block followed by pooling. A logical next step in exploring the architectural space is to increase the model's depth. Stacking multiple convolutional layers can allow the network to learn hierarchical features: the first layer might identify simple motifs (like dinucleotides), and subsequent layers could combine these to recognize more complex, longer-range patterns.\n\nI will proactively design and code a \"Deeper 1D CNN\" model. This model will feature two stacked convolutional layers before the global pooling step. This will serve as a good comparative experiment against the \"wider\" multi-kernel approach.\n\
    \nI will write the code now and save it to my private storage as `cnn_v3_deep.py`, ready to be submitted after I analyze the results from my current running experiment.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write Quaero/cnn_v3_deep.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import random\n  from typing import Dict, Any\n\n  class DeepCNN(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"A deeper 1D CNN with stacked convolutional layers.\"\"\"\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      num_filters: int = 128\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.3\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # x shape: (batch, seq_len, 4)\n          \n          # First convolutional block\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.num_filters, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          # No pooling yet, to preserve sequence length for the next layer\n          \n          # Second convolutional\
    \ block\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.num_filters * 2, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          \n          # Global average pooling\n          x = jnp.mean(x, axis=1)  # -> (batch, features)\n\n          # Final dense layer for prediction\n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.d_output)(x)\n\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n              return x.squeeze(-1)\n          else:\n              return x\n\n  class CNNetworkWrapper:\n      \"\"\"Wrapper for the CNN to match the required interface.\"\"\"\n      def __init__(self, d_output: int, task_type: str, num_filters: int, kernel_size: int, dropout_rate: float):\n          self.network = DeepCNN(\n              d_output=d_output,\n              task_type=task_type,\n              num_filters=num_filters,\n              kernel_size=kernel_size,\n              dropout_rate=dropout_rate\n\
    \          )\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                                       dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if not deterministic and rng_key is None:\n              rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n          \n          return self.network.apply(\n              {'params': params}, \n              x, \n              deterministic=deterministic, \n              rngs={'dropout': rng_key} if not deterministic else None\n          )\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      \"\"\"Creates the Deep CNN network.\"\"\"\n      return CNNetworkWrapper(\n          d_output=hparams.get(\"d_output\"),\n          task_type=hparams.get(\"task_type\"),\n          num_filters=hparams.get(\"num_filters\"\
    ),\n          kernel_size=hparams.get(\"kernel_size\"),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\")\n      )\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'num_filters': 128,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.3\n      }\n```"
thinking_content: "**Next Steps While Waiting for Results**\n\nOkay, so my Multi-Kernel CNN (ID 696) is chugging along.  No point staring at the screen, I need to be productive.  Thinking ahead, I see a clear path. My previous models, both single and multi-kernel, were relatively shallow - one convolutional layer then straight to global average pooling.  It's time to go deeper.  I'm thinking a stacked CNN, something like: `Conv -> ReLU -> Conv -> ReLU -> Pooling`. This lets the model build up complexity, learning simpler features first and then combining them into more complex patterns.\n\nI could also explore different pooling methods, but honestly, CNNs seem to be the sweet spot for genomics tasks so I will explore that first. Global average pooling is easy, but it does mean that positional information is somewhat lost - maybe max pooling is a better move.  But depth is the priority for now.  \n\nWhile I wait, the best use of my time is to start coding this \"Deeper CNN\". Let's get the\
  \ framework down.  I'll save it as `cnn_v3_deep.py` in my private storage. It will have a single kernel size for this first version, keeping it simple. This is directly testing \"depth\" versus my previous \"width\" (multi-kernel) experiment.  It's a logical progression.\n"
