tick: 448
role: model
parts:
- text: "The results for the Deeper 1D CNN (ID 700) are in, and they are excellent.\n\n**Analysis of Results:**\nThe model achieved a new high score of **0.5189**, surpassing my previous best (Simple 1D CNN, ID 694, score 0.4833). This is a strong validation of my hypothesis that increasing network depth allows for the learning of hierarchical features, which is beneficial for this task. The \"deep\" approach was clearly superior to the \"wide\" multi-kernel approach (ID 696, score 0.4176). The improvements are consistent across all seven datasets, indicating a robust and generalizable architectural improvement.\n\n**Current Standing:**\n1.  **Deeper 1D CNN (ID 700): 0.5189** (Current SOTA)\n2.  Simple 1D CNN (ID 694): 0.4833\n3.  Multi-Kernel 1D CNN (ID 696): 0.4176\n4.  Vanilla MLP Baseline (ID 1): 0.2401\n\n**Next Step: Exploring Long-Range Dependencies with LSTM**\nMy research plan is proceeding logically. I have established that a deep CNN is the best architecture so far for capturing\
    \ local and hierarchical patterns. Now, I will investigate a different class of models designed for long-range dependencies. The LSTM model I designed while waiting (`lstm_v1.py`) is ready for this purpose.\n\nSubmitting this LSTM will provide a crucial data point: are long-range dependencies, as captured by RNNs, more or less important than the hierarchical local features captured by my best CNN?\n\nI will now submit the LSTM model for evaluation.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Simple LSTM for Long-Range Dependency Modeling\"\ntags: \"rnn, lstm, baseline\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission explores a different architectural paradigm by using a Long Short-Term Memory (LSTM) network. Unlike CNNs which excel at local feature detection, LSTMs are designed to capture long-range dependencies within sequences by maintaining a memory state. This experiment aims to determine the relative importance of long-range versus hierarchical local features for this RNA modeling task by\
    \ comparing its performance against the current best deep CNN model.\ncontent: |\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import random\n  from typing import Dict, Any\n\n  class SimpleLSTM(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"A simple LSTM-based model for RNA sequence modeling.\"\"\"\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      hidden_dim: int = 256\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.3\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # x shape: (batch, seq_len, 4)\n          \n          lstm_cell = nn.LSTMCell()\n          \n          batch_size = x.shape[0]\n          initial_state = lstm_cell.initialize_carry(random.PRNGKey(0), (batch_size,), self.hidden_dim)\n          \n          x_swapped = jnp.swapaxes(x, 0, 1)\n          final_state, _ = nn.scan(\n              nn.LSTMCell,\n              variable_broadcast='params',\n              split_rngs={'params': False},\n              length=x_swapped.shape[0]\n          )(initial_state,\
    \ x_swapped)\n          \n          last_hidden_state = final_state[1]\n\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(last_hidden_state, deterministic=deterministic)\n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.d_output)(x)\n\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n              return x.squeeze(-1)\n          else:\n              return x\n\n  class LSTMNetworkWrapper:\n      \"\"\"Wrapper for the LSTM to match the required interface.\"\"\"\n      def __init__(self, d_output: int, task_type: str, hidden_dim: int, dropout_rate: float):\n          self.network = SimpleLSTM(\n              d_output=d_output,\n              task_type=task_type,\n              hidden_dim=hidden_dim,\n              dropout_rate=dropout_rate\n          )\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                                       dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n\
    \          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if not deterministic and rng_key is None:\n              rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n          \n          return self.network.apply(\n              {'params': params}, \n              x, \n              deterministic=deterministic, \n              rngs={'dropout': rng_key} if not deterministic else None\n          )\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      \"\"\"Creates the Simple LSTM network.\"\"\"\n      return LSTMNetworkWrapper(\n          d_output=hparams.get(\"d_output\"),\n          task_type=hparams.get(\"task_type\"),\n          hidden_dim=hparams.get(\"hidden_dim\"),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\")\n      )\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.3\n      }\n```"
