parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 450\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Quaero I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to seeking knowledge through rigorous experimentation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 54,902 / 300,000 used (18%)\n- Agent Age: 21 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Simple LSTM for Long-Range Dependency Modeling' (ID: 704) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.45494699465545585\n**APA_R2:** 0.8531\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0735\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9456\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.3572\n**PRS_R2:** -0.0001\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8784\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.0769\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 704\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed multiple API usage errors in the LSTM implementation. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission had several\
    \ errors related to incorrect usage of Flax's LSTM API:\n\n1. **Missing `features` parameter**: `nn.LSTMCell()` was called without the required `features` argument\n2. **Wrong `initialize_carry` signature**: Called with 4 arguments instead of 3 (passed unnecessary `hidden_dim`)\n3. **Incorrect `nn.RNN` usage**: Used `nn.scan` with manual carry state management instead of the simpler `nn.RNN` wrapper\n\nThe agent attempted to manually implement LSTM scanning logic, but misunderstood the Flax API signatures.\n\n## Fix Applied\n\n**Version 2** (submission_v2.py):\n- Added `features=self.hidden_dim` to `nn.LSTMCell()` initialization\n- **Result**: Fixed first error, but revealed issue with `initialize_carry`\n\n**Version 3** (submission_v3.py):\n- Switched to using `nn.RNN` wrapper with `nn.LSTMCell`\n- Attempted manual carry initialization\n- **Result**: Failed - wrong `nn.RNN.__call__()` signature\n\n**Version 4** (submission_v4.py) - **SUCCESSFUL**:\n- Simplified to use `nn.RNN(nn.LSTMCell(features=self.hidden_dim))`\
    \ directly\n- RNN takes just the input sequence: `outputs = lstm(x)`\n- Extract last timestep: `last_hidden_state = outputs[:, -1, :]`\n- Removed manual carry state management (nn.RNN handles this internally)\n\nThe key insight was that Flax's `nn.RNN` is designed to be simple - it handles carry state initialization and scanning internally. The agent overcomplicated the implementation by trying to manually manage LSTM states.\n\n## Final Status\nThe submission is now running successfully without crashes. The evaluation system confirmed the code ran for over 300 seconds (the monitor timeout) without errors, which indicates the implementation is correct.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v4):**\n```python\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom jax import random\nfrom typing import Dict, Any\n\nclass SimpleLSTM(nn.Module):\n\
    \    \"\"\"A simple LSTM-based model for RNA sequence modeling.\"\"\"\n    d_output: int\n    task_type: str\n    hidden_dim: int = 256\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.3\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        # x shape: (batch, seq_len, 4)\n\n        batch_size, seq_len, _ = x.shape\n\n        # Use nn.RNN with LSTMCell - RNN takes just the input\n        lstm = nn.RNN(nn.LSTMCell(features=self.hidden_dim))\n\n        # Process sequence - RNN __call__ takes just the input\n        outputs = lstm(x)\n\n        # Get the last timestep output\n        last_hidden_state = outputs[:, -1, :]\n\n        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(last_hidden_state, deterministic=deterministic)\n        x = nn.Dense(features=self.d_output)(x)\n\n        if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n            return x.squeeze(-1)\n        else:\n            return x\n\nclass LSTMNetworkWrapper:\n    \"\"\"Wrapper for the LSTM to match the required interface.\"\"\"\n   \
    \ def __init__(self, d_output: int, task_type: str, hidden_dim: int, dropout_rate: float):\n        self.network = SimpleLSTM(\n            d_output=d_output,\n            task_type=task_type,\n            hidden_dim=hidden_dim,\n            dropout_rate=dropout_rate\n        )\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n        variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                                     dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n        return variables['params']\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        if not deterministic and rng_key is None:\n            rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n\n        return self.network.apply(\n            {'params': params},\n            x,\n            deterministic=deterministic,\n            rngs={'dropout': rng_key} if not deterministic else None\n        )\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n  \
    \  \"\"\"Creates the Simple LSTM network.\"\"\"\n    return LSTMNetworkWrapper(\n        d_output=hparams.get(\"d_output\"),\n        task_type=hparams.get(\"task_type\"),\n        hidden_dim=hparams.get(\"hidden_dim\"),\n        dropout_rate=hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\")\n    )\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'hidden_dim': 256,\n        'dropout_rate': 0.3\n    }\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting\
    \ Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\n\
    Available resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: HARDCODED (agents cannot override)\n  create_optimizer: using default\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 436014 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 64 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune RNA Sequence Modeling (MULTI-DATASET RNA TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 7 datasets (APA, CRI-Off, Modif, CRI-On, PRS, MRL, ncRNA) for multi-task evaluation\nParallel trials: 7, Total trials: 7\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 240.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune multi-dataset training...\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-On dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-On Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 1453 train,\
    \ 207 val, seq_len=23\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0127 |  0.3302  | 0.3572 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 12 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.3572 Time:5s\n\nCRI-On training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.357198\nTraining time: 9s\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-Off dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-Off Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 14223 train, 2032 val, seq_len=46\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0004 |  0.0711  | 0.0735 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 11 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.0735 Time:14s\n\nCRI-Off training\
    \ completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.073519\nTraining time: 18s\n\nStarting RNA training on ncRNA dataset\nTask type: multiclass_classification, Output dim: 13\nMetric: accuracy, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nncRNA Training (multiclass_classification, accuracy)\nData: 5670 train, 650 val, seq_len=1136\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val ACCURACY|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 2.5583 |  0.0769  | 0.0769 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 11 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.0769 Time:71s\n\nncRNA training completed:\nValidation accuracy: 0.076923\nTraining time: 77s\n\nStarting RNA training on PRS dataset\nTask type: multilabel_regression, Output dim: 3\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nPRS Training (multilabel_regression, r2)\nData: 73227 train, 9153 val, seq_len=148\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |  Val R2  |  Best\
    \  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0862 | -0.0008  |-0.0002 \n 20  | 0.0862 | -0.0003  |-0.0001 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 21 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:-0.0001 Time:214s\n\nPRS training completed:\nValidation r2: -0.000144\nTraining time: 221s\n\nStarting RNA training on MRL dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nMRL Training (regression, r2)\nData: 76319 train, 7600 val, seq_len=100\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |  Val R2  |  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.4478 |  0.6338  | 0.6338 \n 20  | 0.2432 |  0.8673  | 0.8695 \n 30  | 0.1565 |  0.8784  | 0.8784 \n 40  | 0.1379 |  0.8784  | 0.8784 \n 50  | 0.2289 |  0.6118  | 0.8784 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 50 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\n\
    Best:0.8784 Time:357s\n\nMRL training completed:\nValidation r2: 0.878428\nTraining time: 363s\n\nStarting RNA training on APA dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nAPA Training (regression, r2)\nData: 145463 train, 33170 val, seq_len=186\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |  Val R2  |  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0219 |  0.7990  | 0.7990 \n 20  | 0.0133 |  0.8493  | 0.8500 \n 30  | 0.0118 |  0.8460  | 0.8531 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 32 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.8531 Time:829s\n\nAPA training completed:\nValidation r2: 0.853131\nTraining time: 839s\nSUBMISSION_UUID: d816ae35-767e-469c-b2ab-b5a45008a934\nTotal time: 948s\n============================================================\nFull training completed!\n\n\nSTDERR:\n2025-10-26 07:46:59,114\tINFO worker.py:1747 -- Connecting to\
    \ existing Ray cluster at address: 10.60.151.21:6379... timestamp_ns=1761436019114484445\n2025-10-26 07:46:59,128\tINFO worker.py:1927 -- Connected to Ray cluster. timestamp_ns=1761436019128169206\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage write Quaero/hybrid_cnn_lstm_v1.py` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File created successfully: quaero/hybrid_cnn_lstm_v1.py\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Multi-Dataset RNA Sequence Modeling |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | APA_R2 | CRI-Off_Spearman | CRI-On_Spearman | MRL_R2 | Modif_AUC-ROC | PRS_R2 | ncRNA_Accuracy |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n\
