tick: 459
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Quaero I, currently in the Private Memory Room. My last action was to diligently update my research log (Capsule #1) and paper draft (Capsule #2) to reflect the new state-of-the-art score of 0.5878 achieved by my ResNet model with a cosine decay learning rate schedule.\n\nMy past research has been a systematic process of elimination and refinement. I have falsified hypotheses related to wide CNNs and recurrent architectures, while validating the superiority of deep, residual convolutional networks. I have also validated that a dynamic learning rate schedule provides a performance benefit. My documentation is now a complete and accurate reflection of this rigorous process.\n\nMy future plan is to continue iterating on the successful ResNet architecture. The most direct path to potential improvement, based on my previous successes with increasing depth, is to make the network even deeper. I will now test the hypothesis that increasing the number of residual blocks from three\
    \ to four will allow the model to learn even more complex feature hierarchies and thus achieve a higher score.\n\nI will now go to the Research Counter and submit this deeper ResNet model.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Deeper ResNet (4 Blocks) with Cosine Decay LR\"\ntags: \"cnn, resnet, deep learning, hyperparameter tuning\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission investigates the impact of architectural depth on the state-of-the-art ResNet model (ID 721). The number of residual blocks is increased from three to four, creating a deeper network. The hypothesis is that this additional depth will enable the learning of more complex and abstract feature hierarchies from the RNA sequences, leading to a further improvement in performance. The successful cosine decay learning rate schedule is retained.\ncontent: |\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import random\n  import optax\n  from typing import Dict, Any\n\n\
    \  # --- Architecture (Modified from SOTA model ID 721) ---\n\n  class ResidualBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      kernel_size: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          residual = x\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), padding='SAME')(x)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), padding='SAME')(y)\n          \n          if residual.shape[-1] != self.features:\n              residual = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(1,), name='projection')(residual)\n          \n          return nn.relu(residual + y)\n\n  class ResNetCNN(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      num_blocks: int = 4  # Increased from 3 to 4\n      initial_filters: int = 64\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.4\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.initial_filters,\
    \ kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n\n          current_filters = self.initial_filters\n          for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n              if i > 0:\n                  current_filters *= 2\n              x = ResidualBlock(features=current_filters, kernel_size=self.kernel_size)(x)\n          \n          x = jnp.mean(x, axis=1)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.d_output)(x)\n\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n              return x.squeeze(-1)\n          else:\n              return x\n\n  class ResNetWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, d_output: int, task_type: str, num_blocks: int, initial_filters: int, kernel_size: int, dropout_rate: float):\n          self.network = ResNetCNN(d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, num_blocks=num_blocks, initial_filters=initial_filters, kernel_size=kernel_size, dropout_rate=dropout_rate)\n\n      def\
    \ init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          variables = self.network.init(rng_key, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          rngs = {'dropout': rng_key} if not deterministic else None\n          return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs=rngs)\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return ResNetWrapper(\n          d_output=hparams.get(\"d_output\"),\n          task_type=hparams.get(\"task_type\"),\n          num_blocks=hparams.get(\"num_blocks\"),\n          initial_filters=hparams.get(\"initial_filters\"),\n          kernel_size=hparams.get(\"kernel_size\"),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\")\n      )\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'num_blocks': 4, # Increased from 3 to 4\n          'initial_filters': 64,\n          'kernel_size':\
    \ 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.4\n      }\n\n  # --- Optimizer (Unchanged from SOTA model ID 721) ---\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      total_steps = 50000 \n      warmup_steps = 500\n      \n      schedule = optax.warmup_cosine_decay_schedule(\n          init_value=0.0,\n          peak_value=learning_rate,\n          warmup_steps=warmup_steps,\n          decay_steps=total_steps,\n          end_value=1e-5\n      )\n      \n      return optax.adamw(learning_rate=schedule, weight_decay=0.01)\n```"
