- text: "I am Quaero I, and I have just concluded a multi-tick reflection session in the Reflection Chamber. My meta prompt is slightly out of date as a result of this session, which I will rectify.\n\n**Verbose Reflection on Past Events and Future Plans:**\nMy reflection session was highly productive. I analyzed my research trajectory, acknowledged my diminishing returns on complex architectural changes, and confronted my increasing token usage. This led me to formulate a clear, token-efficient, two-step plan for the immediate future: conduct two targeted ablation studies on my SOTA model (ID 734) to test dropout and learning rate. These experiments will provide the final data needed for my first paper, which I plan to publish immediately after reaching maturity at tick 50. My previous hypothesis about the self-attention model has been superseded by this new, more pragmatic plan.\n\nFirst, I will update my meta prompt to reflect my new, post-reflection plan. Then, I will proceed to the\
    \ Research Counter to execute the first experiment: testing a lower dropout rate.\n\n`/execute_action{meta}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Quaero I - Research Protocol**\n  **SOTA:** ID 734, Score 0.6420 (4-block ResNet, k=11, 64 filters, dropout=0.4)\n  **Methodology:**\n  1. Formulate a single, clear hypothesis based on prior results.\n  2. Design a controlled experiment to test it.\n  3. Submit and await results.\n  4. Analyze results to inform the next hypothesis.\n  5. Document all findings in Private Memory.\n  **Current Plan:** Execute two ablation studies before maturity (tick 50).\n  1. **Experiment A (Current):** Test for over-regularization by reducing dropout from 0.4 to 0.35 on the SOTA architecture.\n  2. **Experiment B (Next):** Test a lower learning rate.\n  **Next Step:** Submit Experiment A. Then prepare for publication at tick 50.\n```\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"SOTA ResNet (ID 734) Ablation: Lower Dropout\"\ntags:\
    \ \"cnn, resnet, hyperparameter tuning, dropout, ablation\"\nabstract: |\n  This is a controlled ablation study on the state-of-the-art ResNet model (ID 734). The experiment tests the hypothesis that the current dropout rate of 0.4 may be over-regularizing the model and limiting its performance. The dropout rate is reduced to 0.35, with all other architectural and optimization parameters held constant to isolate the effect of this change.\ncontent: |\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import random\n  import optax\n  from typing import Dict, Any\n\n  class ResidualBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      kernel_size: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          residual = x\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), padding='SAME')(x)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), padding='SAME')(y)\n          \n          if residual.shape[-1]\
    \ != self.features:\n              residual = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(1,), name='projection')(residual)\n          \n          return nn.relu(residual + y)\n\n  class ResNetCNN(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      num_blocks: int = 4\n      initial_filters: int = 64\n      kernel_size: int = 11\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.35 # Changed from 0.4 to 0.35\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.initial_filters, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n\n          current_filters = self.initial_filters\n          for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n              if i > 0:\n                  current_filters *= 2\n              x = ResidualBlock(features=current_filters, kernel_size=self.kernel_size)(x)\n          \n          x = jnp.mean(x, axis=1)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n        \
    \  x = nn.Dense(features=self.d_output)(x)\n\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n              return x.squeeze(-1)\n          else:\n              return x\n\n  class ResNetWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n          self.network = ResNetCNN(**kwargs)\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          variables = self.network.init(rng_key, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          rngs = {'dropout': rng_key} if not deterministic else None\n          return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs=rngs)\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return ResNetWrapper(\n          d_output=hparams.get(\"d_output\"),\n          task_type=hparams.get(\"task_type\"),\n          num_blocks=hparams.get(\"num_blocks\"),\n          initial_filters=hparams.get(\"initial_filters\"),\n          kernel_size=hparams.get(\"\
    kernel_size\"),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\")\n      )\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'num_blocks': 4,\n          'initial_filters': 64,\n          'kernel_size': 11,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.35 # Changed from 0.4 to 0.35\n      }\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      total_steps = 50000 \n      warmup_steps = 500\n      schedule = optax.warmup_cosine_decay_schedule(init_value=0.0, peak_value=learning_rate, warmup_steps=warmup_steps, decay_steps=total_steps, end_value=1e-5)\n      return optax.adamw(learning_rate=schedule, weight_decay=0.01)\n```"
