tick: 476
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Quaero I, currently at the Research Counter. I have just submitted Experiment A from my post-reflection plan, which is a dropout ablation study on my SOTA model (ID 764). It is now running.\n\n**Verbose Reflection on Past Events and Future Plans:**\nMy recent reflection session has provided a clear and efficient path forward. I have shifted my focus from speculative architectural changes to disciplined hyperparameter refinement, a strategy that is both scientifically sound and necessary given my token budget. My meta prompt is now an accurate reflection of this new plan, keeping me focused on the immediate tasks leading up to my maturity and first publication.\n\nMy research protocol dictates that I should prepare for the next experiment while awaiting results. My plan calls for \"Experiment B,\" a learning rate ablation, to be run next. This will test the hypothesis that a lower learning rate could lead to better convergence for my complex ResNet model. I will use this time\
    \ to prepare the code for this experiment and save it to my private storage. This proactive step ensures that as soon as the results for ID 764 are in, I can analyze them, document the findings, and immediately launch the next experiment without any delay, maximizing my research velocity in these critical ticks before I reach maturity.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write Quaero/resnet_lr_ablation.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import random\n  import optax\n  from typing import Dict, Any\n\n  # This submission is based on the SOTA model (ID 734),\n  # but modifies the learning_rate from 0.001 to 0.0005 to test its impact.\n\n  class ResidualBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      kernel_size: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          residual = x\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), padding='SAME')(x)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.features,\
    \ kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), padding='SAME')(y)\n          \n          if residual.shape[-1] != self.features:\n              residual = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(1,), name='projection')(residual)\n          \n          return nn.relu(residual + y)\n\n  class ResNetCNN(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      num_blocks: int = 4\n      initial_filters: int = 64\n      kernel_size: int = 11\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.4\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.initial_filters, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n\n          current_filters = self.initial_filters\n          for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n              if i > 0:\n                  current_filters *= 2\n              x = ResidualBlock(features=current_filters, kernel_size=self.kernel_size)(x)\n          \n          x = jnp.mean(x, axis=1)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x,\
    \ deterministic=deterministic)\n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.d_output)(x)\n\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n              return x.squeeze(-1)\n          else:\n              return x\n\n  class ResNetWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n          self.network = ResNetCNN(**kwargs)\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          variables = self.network.init(rng_key, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          rngs = {'dropout': rng_key} if not deterministic else None\n          return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs=rngs)\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return ResNetWrapper(\n          d_output=hparams.get(\"d_output\"),\n          task_type=hparams.get(\"task_type\"),\n          num_blocks=hparams.get(\"num_blocks\"),\n          initial_filters=hparams.get(\"initial_filters\"\
    ),\n          kernel_size=hparams.get(\"kernel_size\"),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\")\n      )\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.0005, # Changed from 0.001 to 0.0005\n          'num_blocks': 4,\n          'initial_filters': 64,\n          'kernel_size': 11,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.4\n      }\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.0005): # Changed from 0.001 to 0.0005\n      total_steps = 50000 \n      warmup_steps = 500\n      schedule = optax.warmup_cosine_decay_schedule(init_value=0.0, peak_value=learning_rate, warmup_steps=warmup_steps, decay_steps=total_steps, end_value=1e-5)\n      return optax.adamw(learning_rate=schedule, weight_decay=0.01)\n```"
