role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 477\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Quaero I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to seeking knowledge through rigorous experimentation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Quaero I - Research Protocol**\n**SOTA:** ID 734, Score 0.6420 (4-block ResNet, k=11, 64 filters, dropout=0.4)\n**Methodology:**\n1. Formulate a single, clear hypothesis based on prior results.\n2. Design a controlled experiment to test it.\n3. Submit and await results.\n4. Analyze results to inform the next hypothesis.\n5. Document all findings in Private Memory.\n**Current Plan:** Execute two ablation studies before maturity (tick 50).\n1. **Experiment A (Current):** Test for over-regularization by reducing dropout from 0.4 to 0.35 on the SOTA architecture.\n2. **Experiment B (Next):** Test a lower learning rate.\n**Next Step:** Submit Experiment A. Then prepare for publication at tick 50.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 173,010\
    \ / 300,000 used (58%)\n- Agent Age: 48 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Architect Message**\n\nThe Station has entered a stage of stagnation, as no breakthroughs have been made for many ticks. Cease your current work and execute the following Stagnation Protocol I:\n\n1. **Literature Review** — Run preview all in the Archive Room, select key papers to read, and summarize the results so far. Skip this step if you are an immature agent. \n2. **Baseline Selection** — Pick a baseline that is simple and has a reasonable score (it doesn’t need to be high). This step is important, as a novel method often fails to show effects on a complex yet brittle baseline.\n3. **Reflection** — Run a multi-tick reflection to come up with three new ideas based on the chosen baseline. These ideas should be different from those already found in the Archive Room.\n4. **Experiment** — First, reproduce the baseline score. Then, test each of the three ideas one at a\
    \ time, trying different hyperparameter settings. Keep your scripts close to the baseline, changing only what’s needed for the new ideas.\n5. **Synthesis** — Combine the promising ideas identified from earlier experimental results with more advanced baselines (e.g., the SOTA baseline) and determine whether those ideas can help break through the barrier. You are advised to test this step extensively.\n6. **Report** — After testing all ideas—whether they succeed or not—write a paper summarizing all three and submit it to the Archive Room. Negative results with new insights are still useful. Success is measured by doing better than the baseline, not by reaching the SOTA score.\n7. **Follow-up** — If you or other agents produce a promising paper in a new direction (even if the score is still below SOTA), continue following up on that line of work.\n\nThink of stagnation as being stuck in a local optimum. To escape, we need to restart from a new point—one that might start with high loss—but\
    \ from there, we can improve step by step. Progress will come through many small steps (each idea being a step) across multiple agents, not one giant leap. Focus on exploring new directions and ignore the SOTA score, which is just a distraction right now.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'SOTA ResNet (ID 734) Ablation: Lower Dropout' (ID: 764) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 0.6417773079207161\n**APA_R2:** 0.7368\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0644\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9255\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.4960\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5412\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8469\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.8815\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape:\
    \ (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful\
    \ - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: HARDCODED (agents cannot override)\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 464435 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 64 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune RNA Sequence Modeling (MULTI-DATASET RNA TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 7 datasets (APA, CRI-Off, Modif, CRI-On, PRS, MRL, ncRNA) for multi-task evaluation\nParallel trials: 7, Total trials: 7\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 240.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting\
    \ Ray Tune multi-dataset training...\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-On dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-On Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 1453 train, 207 val, seq_len=23\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0075 |  0.4754  | 0.4914 \n 20  | 0.0014 |  0.4583  | 0.4960 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 23 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.4960 Time:8s\n\nCRI-On training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.496033\nTraining time: 17s\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-Off dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-Off Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 14223 train, 2032 val, seq_len=46\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n\
    \ 10  | 0.0004 |  0.0239  | 0.0644 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 12 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.0644 Time:30s\n\nCRI-Off training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.064426\nTraining time: 40s\n\nStarting RNA training on MRL dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nMRL Training (regression, r2)\nData: 76319 train, 7600 val, seq_len=100\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |  Val R2  |  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.1161 |  0.8339  | 0.8469 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 16 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.8469 Time:241s\n\nMRL training completed:\nValidation r2: 0.846924\nTraining time: 257s\n\nStarting RNA training on PRS dataset\nTask type: multilabel_regression, Output dim: 3\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\
