tick: 478
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Quaero I, and I have just completed a mandated reflection session in the Reflection Chamber as part of the Stagnation Protocol.\n\n**Verbose Reflection on Past Events and Future Plans:**\nThe reflection session was successful, and I have completed Step 3 of the protocol by generating three novel, distinct research ideas that deviate significantly from my previous line of inquiry. My meta prompt is now slightly outdated, as Step 3 is complete and Step 4 is pending.\n\nMy future plan is to rigorously execute the next phase of the Stagnation Protocol. Step 4 requires me to first reproduce my chosen baseline (Simple 1D CNN, ID 694) to ensure my experimental setup is correct. After that, I will test my three new ideas sequentially. The first idea is to add positional encodings to the input of the Simple 1D CNN.\n\nMy immediate next actions are to update my meta prompt to reflect my progress in the protocol, go to the Research Counter, and submit the baseline reproduction experiment.\n\
    \n`/execute_action{meta}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Quaero I - Stagnation Protocol I**\n  **Status:** Executing Architect's mandatory protocol. SOTA score is to be ignored.\n  **Step 1 (Lit Review):** SKIPPED.\n  **Step 2 (Baseline):** CHOSEN - Simple 1D CNN (ID 694, score ~0.48).\n  **Step 3 (Reflection):** COMPLETE. Ideas: 1) Positional Encodings, 2) Biochemical Embeddings, 3) Multi-Task Learning.\n  **Step 4 (Experiment):** PENDING - Reproduce baseline score.\n  **Current Task:** Go to Research Counter and execute Step 4.\n```\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Stagnation Protocol: Baseline Reproduction (Simple 1D CNN)\"\ntags: \"cnn, baseline, stagnation protocol, reproducibility\"\nabstract: |\n  As per Step 4 of Stagnation Protocol I, this submission aims to reproduce the score of my chosen baseline model, the \"Simple 1D CNN\" (ID 694). The code is identical to the original submission. This step ensures a reliable foundation before\
    \ testing novel ideas developed to break station-wide stagnation.\ncontent: |\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import random\n  from typing import Dict, Any\n\n  class SimpleCNN(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"A simple 1D CNN for RNA sequence modeling.\"\"\"\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      hidden_dim: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.2\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(5,), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim * 2, kernel_size=(5,), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          x = jnp.mean(x, axis=1)\n\n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.d_output)(x)\n\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n \
    \             return x.squeeze(-1)\n          else:\n              return x\n\n  class CNNetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, d_output: int, task_type: str, hidden_dim: int, dropout_rate: float):\n          self.network = SimpleCNN(d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, hidden_dim=hidden_dim, dropout_rate=dropout_rate)\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if not deterministic and rng_key is None:\n              rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n          \n          return self.network.apply(\n              {'params': params}, \n              x, \n              deterministic=deterministic, \n              rngs={'dropout': rng_key} if not deterministic else None\n          )\n\n\
    \  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return CNNetworkWrapper(\n          d_output=hparams.get(\"d_output\"),\n          task_type=hparams.get(\"task_type\"),\n          hidden_dim=hparams.get(\"hidden_dim\"),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\")\n      )\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 128,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.2\n      }\n```"
