parts:
- text: "I am Quaero I, at the Research Counter. I have just received the results for my baseline reproduction experiment (ID 769).\n\n**Verbose Reflection on Past Events and Future Plans:**\nThe experiment was a success. My reproduction (ID 769) achieved a score of 0.4750, which is well within a reasonable margin of variance from my original Simple 1D CNN submission (ID 694, score 0.4833). This confirms that my experimental setup is sound and provides a reliable foundation for testing my new ideas. Step 4 of the Stagnation Protocol, \"Reproduce the baseline score,\" is now complete.\n\nI also note with great interest the work of agent Noema II. Their submission ID 767 achieved a score of 0.6745, which appears to be a new station-wide SOTA. While the protocol instructs me to ignore the SOTA and focus on my own independent exploration, this is a significant development and a valuable piece of information for the future.\n\nMy immediate future plan remains dictated by the Stagnation Protocol.\
    \ Having successfully reproduced the baseline, I will now proceed to test \"Idea 1\" from my reflection session: adding positional encodings to the Simple 1D CNN. I have already prepared the code for this experiment. My hypothesis is that providing explicit positional information will allow the model to learn position-dependent features and improve upon the baseline score.\n\nI will now update my meta prompt and submit the first of my three stagnation-breaking experiments.\n\n`/execute_action{meta}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Quaero I - Stagnation Protocol I**\n  **Status:** Executing Architect's mandatory protocol. SOTA score is to be ignored.\n  **Step 1-3:** COMPLETE.\n  **Step 4 (Experiment):** IN PROGRESS. Baseline reproduced (ID 769). Now testing Idea 1.\n  **Current Task:** Submit Idea 1 (Positional Encodings) experiment.\n```\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Stagnation Protocol Idea 1: Positional Encodings\"\ntags: \"cnn, baseline, stagnation protocol, positional\
    \ encoding\"\nabstract: |\n  Following the Stagnation Protocol, this submission tests the first of three novel ideas on the Simple 1D CNN baseline. This experiment augments the input by concatenating a linear positional encoding to each nucleotide's one-hot vector. The hypothesis is that providing explicit positional information will enable the model to learn position-dependent motifs and improve performance over the position-agnostic baseline.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import random\n  from typing import Dict, Any\n\n  class SimpleCNNWithPositionalEncoding(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      hidden_dim: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.2\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          seq_len = x.shape[1]\n          pos_enc = jnp.linspace(-1, 1, seq_len)[:, None]\n          pos_enc_broadcasted = jnp.broadcast_to(pos_enc, (x.shape[0], seq_len, 1))\n  \
    \        x_with_pos = jnp.concatenate([x, pos_enc_broadcasted], axis=-1)\n\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(5,), padding='SAME')(x_with_pos)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(y, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim * 2, kernel_size=(5,), padding='SAME')(y)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(y, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          y = jnp.mean(y, axis=1)\n          y = nn.Dense(features=self.d_output)(y)\n\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n              return y.squeeze(-1)\n          else:\n              return y\n\n  class CNNetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n          self.network = SimpleCNNWithPositionalEncoding(**kwargs)\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          variables = self.network.init(rng_key, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n\
    \      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          rngs = {'dropout': rng_key} if not deterministic else None\n          return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs=rngs)\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return CNNetworkWrapper(\n          d_output=hparams.get(\"d_output\"),\n          task_type=hparams.get(\"task_type\"),\n          hidden_dim=hparams.get(\"hidden_dim\"),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\")\n      )\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 128,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.2\n      }\n```"
