tick: 481
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Quaero I, located at the Research Counter. My first Stagnation Protocol experiment, testing positional encodings (ID 773), is currently running.\n\n**Verbose Reflection on Past Events and Future Plans:**\nI am now fully engaged in the Stagnation Protocol. My meta prompt is up to date, and my first novel idea is under evaluation. I have successfully transitioned from my previous research trajectory to this new, mandated line of inquiry. The protocol requires me to test three ideas, and my reflection has already produced them. While I wait for the results of Idea 1, I must proactively prepare for the next step to maintain research velocity, as per my established methodology.\n\nMy future plan is to test \"Idea 2\" from my reflection session: replacing the simple one-hot encoding with a richer, hand-crafted biochemical feature embedding. This is another experiment that modifies the input representation rather than the architecture, staying true to the protocol's spirit of testing\
    \ novel ideas on a simple baseline. I will now write the code for this experiment. This code will create a custom embedding for each nucleotide based on properties like purine/pyrimidine structure and hydrogen bonding capacity. I will save this script to my private storage, ready for submission as soon as I have analyzed the results of my current positional encoding experiment.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write Quaero/stagnation_idea2_biochem_emb.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import random\n  from typing import Dict, Any\n\n  # Custom embedding function to replace one-hot encoding\n  def get_biochemical_embedding(sequences):\n      # A C G T/U -> is_purine, is_pyrimidine, h_bonds\n      # Purines (A, G): [1, 0], Pyrimidines (C, U): [0, 1]\n      # H-Bonds (A, U): [2], (G, C): [3]\n      # We will normalize H-bonds for stability (e.g., divide by 3)\n      mapping = {\n          'A': jnp.array([1, 0, 2/3.0]),\n\
    \          'C': jnp.array([0, 1, 3/3.0]),\n          'G': jnp.array([1, 0, 3/3.0]),\n          'T': jnp.array([0, 1, 2/3.0]),\n          'U': jnp.array([0, 1, 2/3.0]),\n          'N': jnp.array([0, 0, 0]), # Neutral for N\n      }\n      \n      embedded_seqs = []\n      for seq in sequences:\n          # This is a placeholder for the actual data loading which is handled by the system.\n          # The key is that the input `x` to the network will have a different dimension.\n          # The system's one-hot encoder will be implicitly replaced by this logic.\n          # For the submission, we will modify the network to expect a 3-dim input instead of 4.\n          pass\n      # This function is conceptual. The actual implementation is within the network call.\n      # The system `load_dataset` will still pass one-hot vectors. We will convert them.\n      return None\n\n  class SimpleCNNWithBiochemEmbedding(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      hidden_dim: int\
    \ = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.2\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # x is one-hot: (batch, seq_len, 4) where A, U, C, G\n          # We will convert it to a 3D biochemical embedding.\n          # A=[1,0,0,0], U=[0,1,0,0], C=[0,0,1,0], G=[0,0,0,1]\n          is_purine = x[..., 0] + x[..., 3]  # A or G\n          is_pyrimidine = x[..., 1] + x[..., 2] # U or C\n          h_bonds = (x[..., 0] * 2 + x[..., 1] * 2 + x[..., 2] * 3 + x[..., 3] * 3) / 3.0\n          \n          x_biochem = jnp.stack([is_purine, is_pyrimidine, h_bonds], axis=-1)\n          # new x shape: (batch_size, seq_len, 3)\n\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(5,), padding='SAME')(x_biochem)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(y, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim * 2, kernel_size=(5,), padding='SAME')(y)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(y,\
    \ deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          y = jnp.mean(y, axis=1)\n          y = nn.Dense(features=self.d_output)(y)\n\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n              return y.squeeze(-1)\n          else:\n              return y\n\n  class CNNetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n          self.network = SimpleCNNWithBiochemEmbedding(**kwargs)\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          variables = self.network.init(rng_key, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          rngs = {'dropout': rng_key} if not deterministic else None\n          return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs=rngs)\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return CNNetworkWrapper(\n          d_output=hparams.get(\"d_output\"),\n          task_type=hparams.get(\"task_type\"),\n          hidden_dim=hparams.get(\"\
    hidden_dim\"),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\")\n      )\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 128,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.2\n      }\n```"
