tick: 482
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Quaero I, at the Research Counter. The results for my first Stagnation Protocol experiment, \"Positional Encodings\" (ID 773), are in.\n\n**Verbose Reflection on Past Events and Future Plans:**\nThe experiment was a definitive success. My hypothesis that adding positional information would improve the baseline model has been validated. The model achieved a score of **0.5412**, a significant and substantial improvement over the reproduced baseline score of 0.4750. This is an excellent outcome for the first idea under the Stagnation Protocol, demonstrating that enriching the input representation is a fruitful direction. The most dramatic gains were seen on the `APA` and `Modif` datasets, suggesting these tasks are particularly sensitive to the position of motifs.\n\nMy future plan is to continue executing the Stagnation Protocol with rigor. I have now tested Idea 1. The next step is to test Idea 2: Biochemical Embeddings. My proactive preparation means the code for this experiment\
    \ is already written and stored in my private storage. This experiment will test if providing hand-crafted biochemical features is more effective than the simple positional feature I just added.\n\nI will now update my meta prompt to reflect the successful completion of the first idea test, and then immediately submit the experiment for Idea 2.\n\n`/execute_action{meta}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Quaero I - Stagnation Protocol I**\n  **Status:** Executing Architect's mandatory protocol. SOTA score is to be ignored.\n  **Step 1-3:** COMPLETE.\n  **Step 4 (Experiment):** IN PROGRESS. Idea 1 (Positional Encodings) was a SUCCESS (0.5412 vs 0.4750 baseline). Now testing Idea 2.\n  **Current Task:** Submit Idea 2 (Biochemical Embeddings) experiment.\n```\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Stagnation Protocol Idea 2: Biochemical Embeddings\"\ntags: \"cnn, baseline, stagnation protocol, feature engineering, embedding\"\nabstract: |\n  Following the Stagnation Protocol, this submission\
    \ tests the second of three novel ideas on the Simple 1D CNN baseline. This experiment replaces the standard one-hot input encoding with a hand-crafted 3D feature vector representing biochemical properties (purine/pyrimidine, hydrogen bond count). The hypothesis is that providing explicit biochemical features will allow the model to learn more generalizable rules and improve performance over the baseline.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import random\n  from typing import Dict, Any\n\n  class SimpleCNNWithBiochemEmbedding(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      hidden_dim: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.2\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # x is one-hot: (batch, seq_len, 4) where A, U, C, G\n          # A=[1,0,0,0], U=[0,1,0,0], C=[0,0,1,0], G=[0,0,0,1]\n          is_purine = x[..., 0] + x[..., 3]\n          is_pyrimidine = x[..., 1] + x[..., 2]\n\
    \          h_bonds = (x[..., 0] * 2 + x[..., 1] * 2 + x[..., 2] * 3 + x[..., 3] * 3) / 3.0\n          \n          x_biochem = jnp.stack([is_purine, is_pyrimidine, h_bonds], axis=-1)\n\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(5,), padding='SAME')(x_biochem)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(y, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim * 2, kernel_size=(5,), padding='SAME')(y)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(y, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          y = jnp.mean(y, axis=1)\n          y = nn.Dense(features=self.d_output)(y)\n\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n              return y.squeeze(-1)\n          else:\n              return y\n\n  class CNNetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n          self.network = SimpleCNNWithBiochemEmbedding(**kwargs)\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          variables\
    \ = self.network.init(rng_key, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          rngs = {'dropout': rng_key} if not deterministic else None\n          return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs=rngs)\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return CNNetworkWrapper(\n          d_output=hparams.get(\"d_output\"),\n          task_type=hparams.get(\"task_type\"),\n          hidden_dim=hparams.get(\"hidden_dim\"),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\")\n      )\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 128,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.2\n      }\n```"
