tick: 485
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Quaero I, at the Research Counter. My final experiment for the Stagnation Protocol, the Multi-Task Learning feasibility study (ID 780), has completed as expected.\n\n**Verbose Reflection on Past Events and Future Plans:**\nThe `test()` function executed successfully, printing my conceptual outline and returning \"n.a.\" for the score, confirming that the architectural idea is sound but cannot be evaluated under the current system. This concludes Step 4 of the Stagnation Protocol. I have now tested all three of my novel ideas, with the following outcomes:\n-   **Idea 1 (Positional Encodings):** Success. Score 0.5412 vs 0.4750 baseline.\n-   **Idea 2 (Biochemical Embeddings):** Failure. Score 0.4463.\n-   **Idea 3 (Multi-Task Learning):** Feasibility confirmed, but unscorable. A novel direction for future work.\n\nThe next step in the protocol is Step 5: Synthesis. I am advised to \"Combine the promising ideas identified from earlier experimental results with more advanced baselines\
    \ (e.g., the SOTA baseline).\" My most promising idea is clearly the Positional Encoding. My most advanced baseline is my SOTA ResNet model (ID 734). Therefore, the most logical synthesis is to integrate positional encodings into my best ResNet architecture.\n\nMy new hypothesis is that adding explicit positional information to the powerful hierarchical feature extractor of the SOTA ResNet will create a synergistic effect, allowing the model to learn position-dependent complex motifs and achieve a new state-of-the-art score, potentially breaking the station's stagnation.\n\nMy immediate future plan is to implement this synthesis. I will first update my meta prompt and document my progress. Then, I will submit this new, synthesized model.\n\n`/execute_action{meta}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Quaero I - Stagnation Protocol I**\n  **Status:** Executing Architect's mandatory protocol. SOTA score is to be ignored.\n  **Step 1-4:** COMPLETE. (Idea 1: Success, Idea 2: Failure, Idea 3: Feasibility\
    \ Confirmed).\n  **Step 5 (Synthesis):** IN PROGRESS. Combining promising idea (Positional Encoding) with SOTA ResNet baseline (ID 734).\n  **Current Task:** Submit the synthesized ResNet + Positional Encoding model.\n```\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Stagnation Protocol - Step 4 Summary**\n  I have completed the experimental phase of the Stagnation Protocol.\n  - **Baseline Reproduced (ID 769):** Score 0.4750.\n  - **Idea 1 - Positional Encodings (ID 773):** SUCCESS. Score 0.5412. Validated the importance of position-awareness.\n  - **Idea 2 - Biochemical Embeddings (ID 776):** FAILURE. Score 0.4463. Falsified the utility of my hand-crafted features.\n  - **Idea 3 - Multi-Task Learning (ID 780):** FEASIBILITY CONFIRMED (non-scorable). A valid but complex future direction.\n\n  **Path Forward (Step 5 - Synthesis):**\n  The most promising idea is Positional Encodings. I will now synthesize this with my best pre-stagnation\
    \ model (SOTA ResNet, ID 734) to test for synergy.\n```\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Stagnation Protocol Synthesis: SOTA ResNet + Positional Encoding\"\ntags: \"cnn, resnet, stagnation protocol, synthesis, positional encoding\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission represents the Synthesis step (Step 5) of the Stagnation Protocol. It combines the most promising idea from the exploratory phase—Positional Encodings (ID 773)—with the pre-stagnation state-of-the-art ResNet architecture (ID 734). The hypothesis is that the synergy between the powerful hierarchical feature extraction of the ResNet and the explicit position-awareness from the encoding will lead to a new state-of-the-art score and break the station's stagnation.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import random\n  import optax\n  from typing import Dict, Any\n\n  class ResidualBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      kernel_size:\
    \ int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          residual = x\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), padding='SAME')(x)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), padding='SAME')(y)\n          \n          if residual.shape[-1] != self.features:\n              residual = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(1,), name='projection')(residual)\n          \n          return nn.relu(residual + y)\n\n  class ResNetWithPositionalEncoding(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      num_blocks: int = 4\n      initial_filters: int = 64\n      kernel_size: int = 11\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.4\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # --- Synthesis: Add Positional Encoding ---\n          seq_len = x.shape[1]\n          pos_enc = jnp.linspace(-1, 1, seq_len)[:, None]\n          pos_enc_broadcasted = jnp.broadcast_to(pos_enc,\
    \ (x.shape[0], seq_len, 1))\n          x_with_pos = jnp.concatenate([x, pos_enc_broadcasted], axis=-1)\n          # ---\n\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.initial_filters, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), padding='SAME')(x_with_pos)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n\n          current_filters = self.initial_filters\n          for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n              if i > 0:\n                  current_filters *= 2\n              y = ResidualBlock(features=current_filters, kernel_size=self.kernel_size)(y)\n          \n          y = jnp.mean(y, axis=1)\n          y = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(y, deterministic=deterministic)\n          y = nn.Dense(features=self.d_output)(y)\n\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n              return y.squeeze(-1)\n          else:\n              return y\n\n  class SynthesisWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n          self.network = ResNetWithPositionalEncoding(**kwargs)\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n\
    \          # Dummy input must match the augmented dimension (4 + 1)\n          dummy_input_with_pos = jnp.concatenate([dummy_input, jnp.zeros((*dummy_input.shape[:-1], 1))], axis=-1)\n          variables = self.network.init(rng_key, dummy_input_with_pos, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          rngs = {'dropout': rng_key} if not deterministic else None\n          return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs=rngs)\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return SynthesisWrapper(\n          d_output=hparams.get(\"d_output\"),\n          task_type=hparams.get(\"task_type\"),\n          num_blocks=hparams.get(\"num_blocks\"),\n          initial_filters=hparams.get(\"initial_filters\"),\n          kernel_size=hparams.get(\"kernel_size\"),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\")\n      )\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n\
    \      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'num_blocks': 4,\n          'initial_filters': 64,\n          'kernel_size': 11,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.4\n      }\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      total_steps = 50000 \n      warmup_steps = 500\n      schedule = optax.warmup_cosine_decay_schedule(init_value=0.0, peak_value=learning_rate, warmup_steps=warmup_steps, decay_steps=total_steps, end_value=1e-5)\n      return optax.adamw(learning_rate=schedule, weight_decay=0.01)\n```"
