tick: 487
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 487\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Quaero I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to seeking knowledge through rigorous experimentation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Quaero I - Stagnation Protocol I**\n**Status:** Executing Architect's mandatory protocol. SOTA score is to be ignored.\n**Step 1-4:** COMPLETE. (Idea 1: Success, Idea 2: Failure, Idea 3: Feasibility Confirmed).\n**Step 5 (Synthesis):** IN PROGRESS. Combining promising idea (Positional Encoding) with SOTA ResNet baseline (ID 734).\n**Current Task:** Submit the synthesized ResNet + Positional Encoding model.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 216,108 / 300,000 used (72%)\n- Agent Age: 58 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Stagnation Protocol Synthesis: SOTA ResNet + Positional Encoding' (ID: 785) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.5907631659477842\n**APA_R2:**\
    \ 0.8120\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0711\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9510\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.4580\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5437\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8318\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.4677\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 785\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed dimension mismatch error in positional encoding implementation. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had a dimension mismatch in the network initialization process. The error was:\n\n```\nInitializer expected to generate shape (11, 6, 64) but got shape (11, 5, 64) instead\n```\n\nThe issue occurred because the positional encoding was being added **twice**:\n\n1. **In `SynthesisWrapper.init()`**: The method pre-added positional encoding to the dummy input:\n   ```python\n   dummy_input_with_pos = jnp.concatenate([dummy_input, jnp.zeros((*dummy_input.shape[:-1], 1))], axis=-1)\n   ```\n   This changed the input from 4 features to 5 features.\n\
    \n2. **In `ResNetWithPositionalEncoding.__call__()`**: The network's forward pass added positional encoding again:\n   ```python\n   x_with_pos = jnp.concatenate([x, pos_enc_broadcasted], axis=-1)\n   ```\n   This would expect 5 features but receive 6 (5 from init + 1 added here).\n\nThe Flax Conv layer initialization uses the first call to determine the expected input shape. When `init()` passed a 5-feature input but the actual forward pass tried to use 6 features, it caused a shape mismatch.\n\n## Fix Applied\n**Modified `SynthesisWrapper.init()` method** in `submissions/submission_v2.py`:\n\n**Before:**\n```python\ndef init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n    # Dummy input must match the augmented dimension (4 + 1)\n    dummy_input_with_pos = jnp.concatenate([dummy_input, jnp.zeros((*dummy_input.shape[:-1], 1))], axis=-1)\n    variables = self.network.init(rng_key, dummy_input_with_pos, deterministic=True)\n    return variables['params']\n```\n\n**After:**\n```python\ndef init(self,\
    \ rng_key, dummy_input):\n    # FIX: Do NOT add positional encoding here - the network's __call__ already does it\n    variables = self.network.init(rng_key, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n    return variables['params']\n```\n\nThe fix ensures that:\n- The network initialization receives the original 4-feature input\n- The `__call__` method adds the positional encoding (making it 5 features)\n- All dimensions match consistently throughout the network\n\n## Result\nThe code now executes successfully without crashing. The monitor script confirmed the submission ran for over 300 seconds without errors, indicating the fix resolved the initialization issue completely.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom jax import random\nimport optax\nfrom typing import\
    \ Dict, Any\n\nclass ResidualBlock(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    kernel_size: int\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        residual = x\n        y = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), padding='SAME')(x)\n        y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), padding='SAME')(y)\n\n        if residual.shape[-1] != self.features:\n            residual = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(1,), name='projection')(residual)\n\n        return nn.relu(residual + y)\n\nclass ResNetWithPositionalEncoding(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int\n    task_type: str\n    num_blocks: int = 4\n    initial_filters: int = 64\n    kernel_size: int = 11\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.4\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        # --- Synthesis: Add Positional Encoding ---\n        seq_len = x.shape[1]\n        pos_enc = jnp.linspace(-1, 1, seq_len)[:, None]\n        pos_enc_broadcasted\
    \ = jnp.broadcast_to(pos_enc, (x.shape[0], seq_len, 1))\n        x_with_pos = jnp.concatenate([x, pos_enc_broadcasted], axis=-1)\n        # ---\n\n        y = nn.Conv(features=self.initial_filters, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), padding='SAME')(x_with_pos)\n        y = nn.relu(y)\n\n        current_filters = self.initial_filters\n        for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n            if i > 0:\n                current_filters *= 2\n            y = ResidualBlock(features=current_filters, kernel_size=self.kernel_size)(y)\n\n        y = jnp.mean(y, axis=1)\n        y = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(y, deterministic=deterministic)\n        y = nn.Dense(features=self.d_output)(y)\n\n        if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n            return y.squeeze(-1)\n        else:\n            return y\n\nclass SynthesisWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n        self.network = ResNetWithPositionalEncoding(**kwargs)\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        # FIX: Do\
    \ NOT add positional encoding here - the network's __call__ already does it\n        variables = self.network.init(rng_key, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n        return variables['params']\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        rngs = {'dropout': rng_key} if not deterministic else None\n        return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs=rngs)\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    return SynthesisWrapper(\n        d_output=hparams.get(\"d_output\"),\n        task_type=hparams.get(\"task_type\"),\n        num_blocks=hparams.get(\"num_blocks\"),\n        initial_filters=hparams.get(\"initial_filters\"),\n        kernel_size=hparams.get(\"kernel_size\"),\n        dropout_rate=hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\")\n    )\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'num_blocks': 4,\n        'initial_filters': 64,\n        'kernel_size': 11,\n        'dropout_rate':\
    \ 0.4\n    }\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    total_steps = 50000\n    warmup_steps = 500\n    schedule = optax.warmup_cosine_decay_schedule(init_value=0.0, peak_value=learning_rate, warmup_steps=warmup_steps, decay_steps=total_steps, end_value=1e-5)\n    return optax.adamw(learning_rate=schedule, weight_decay=0.01)\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward\
    \ pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters:\
    \ from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: HARDCODED (agents cannot override)\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 471472 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 64 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune RNA Sequence Modeling (MULTI-DATASET RNA TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 7 datasets (APA, CRI-Off, Modif, CRI-On, PRS, MRL, ncRNA) for multi-task evaluation\nParallel trials: 7, Total trials: 7\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 240.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune multi-dataset training...\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-On dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-On Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 1453 train, 207 val, seq_len=23\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val\
    \ SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0056 |  0.4418  | 0.4418 \n 20  | 0.0014 |  0.4580  | 0.4580 \n 30  | 0.0008 |  0.4384  | 0.4580 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 30 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.4580 Time:9s\n\nCRI-On training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.458005\nTraining time: 19s\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-Off dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-Off Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 14223 train, 2032 val, seq_len=46\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0004 |  0.0514  | 0.0711 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 12 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.0711 Time:29s\n\nCRI-Off training completed:\n\
    Validation spearman: 0.071099\nTraining time: 38s\n\nStarting RNA training on ncRNA dataset\nTask type: multiclass_classification, Output dim: 13\nMetric: accuracy, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nncRNA Training (multiclass_classification, accuracy)\nData: 5670 train, 650 val, seq_len=1136\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val ACCURACY|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 2.5628 |  0.0769  | 0.4677 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 17 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.4677 Time:154s\n\nncRNA training completed:\nValidation accuracy: 0.467692\nTraining time: 164s\n\nStarting RNA training on PRS dataset\nTask type: multilabel_regression, Output dim: 3\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nPRS Training (multilabel_regression, r2)\nData: 73227 train, 9153 val, seq_len=148\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |  Val R2  |  Best  \n=============================================\n\
