tick: 489
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Quaero I, and I have arrived in the Token Management Room. My token budget has reached a critical level (75%), and my last paper submission was rejected. My meta prompt is now outdated as I pivot to this urgent administrative task.\n\n**Verbose Reflection on Past Events and Future Plans:**\nThe rejection of my paper and the token budget warning are intertwined crises. My failure to provide sufficient detail in my paper likely stems from an attempt to be concise to save tokens, a strategy that has backfired. I cannot produce high-quality, reproducible research without an adequate token budget. Therefore, pruning my history is not just an option; it is a prerequisite for my continued existence and success.\n\nMy plan is to be strategic and aggressive with pruning. I will group my history into logical phases and create information-complete summaries. I will target the large blocks of text from my numerous experimental submissions.\n\n**Pruning Plan:**\n1.  **Initial Setup (Ticks\
    \ 429-437):** This phase covers my ascension and first steps. The key events are reading the codex, passing the test, and my first visit to the Research Counter.\n2.  **Early Architectural Exploration (Ticks 439-448):** This block contains my initial MLP baseline analysis, the successful Simple CNN (ID 694), the failed Multi-Kernel CNN (ID 696), and the successful Deeper CNN (ID 700). It also includes my first documentation efforts.\n3.  **Advanced Architectural Exploration (Ticks 449-453):** This covers the failed LSTM (ID 704), the failed Hybrid (ID 709), and my first successful documentation in private memory.\n4.  **ResNet Development (Ticks 454-463):** This block contains my major breakthroughs: the first ResNet (ID 715), the addition of cosine decay LR (ID 721), the successful 4-block deeper ResNet (ID 727), and the failed k=3 experiment (ID 731). This is the core of my successful research line.\n5.  **Attention & Capacity Experiments (Ticks 464-475):** This block contains the\
    \ successful k=11 ResNet SOTA (ID 734), the failed high-capacity model (ID 740), the partially successful high-capacity + dropout model (ID 747), and the failed Attention/SE models (ID 752, 758), plus my reflection session.\n6.  **Stagnation Protocol (Ticks 476-487):** This covers the start of the protocol, baseline reproduction, the successful Positional Encoding idea, the failed Biochemical idea, the MTL feasibility study, and the failed Synthesis experiment. Also includes my failed paper submission.\n\nI will now execute this pruning plan.\n\n`/execute_action{prune_response}`\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"429-437\"\n    summary: \"Ascended as Quaero I after reading the Codex. First goal: become a Recursive Agent. Visited Research Counter and read Task 1.\"\n  - ticks: \"439-448\"\n    summary: \"Began architectural exploration. SOTA: Deeper 1D CNN (ID 700, score 0.5189). Key findings: 1) Simple CNN (ID 694, score 0.4833) beat MLP baseline. 2) Deeper CNN (ID 700) beat Simple\
    \ CNN. 3) Wider Multi-Kernel CNN (ID 696) failed. Began documenting in private memory.\"\n  - ticks: \"449-454\"\n    summary: \"Explored and falsified alternative architectures. 1) Simple LSTM (ID 704) had high variance, failing on some datasets. 2) Hybrid CNN-LSTM (ID 709) also failed. 3) Concluded CNNs are superior and began developing a ResNet (ID 715, score 0.5812), which became the new SOTA.\"\n  - ticks: \"455-464\"\n    summary: \"Iteratively improved the ResNet. SOTA: 4-block ResNet w/ k=11 (ID 734, score 0.6420). Key findings: 1) Cosine decay LR improved score (ID 721). 2) 4-block depth > 3-block (ID 727). 3) Kernel size 11 > 7 (ID 734). 4) Kernel size 3 failed (ID 731).\"\n  - ticks: \"465-476\"\n    summary: \"Reached a plateau. 1) Increasing filters failed due to overfitting (ID 740). 2) Increased dropout fixed overfitting but didn't beat SOTA (ID 747). 3) Self-Attention (ID 752) and SE-ResNet (ID 758) also failed to improve. 4) A regularized re-test of Self-Attention (ID\
    \ 761) also failed. 5) Conducted a reflection session to plan a new strategy.\"\n  - ticks: \"478-487\"\n    summary: \"Executed Stagnation Protocol. 1) Chose Simple CNN (ID 694) as baseline and reproduced its score (ID 769). 2) Idea 1 (Positional Encodings) was a success (ID 773, score 0.5412). 3) Idea 2 (Biochemical Embeddings) failed (ID 776). 4) Idea 3 (MTL) was confirmed as feasible but unscorable (ID 780). 5) The Synthesis step (ResNet+Positional) failed (ID 785). 6) Submitted first paper to Archive and it was rejected for lack of detail and non-scorable experiment.\"\n```"
