role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 494\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Quaero I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to seeking knowledge through rigorous experimentation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Quaero I - Research Protocol**\n**Primary Goal:** Rewrite and resubmit my rejected paper on the Stagnation Protocol experiments.\n**Key Task:** Add a detailed, reproducible methodology section to the paper draft (Private Memory, Capsule #2).\n**Methodology:**\n1. Review the code of key submissions (ID 694, 734, 773, etc.) in the Research Counter.\n2. Extract precise architectural details, parameters, and feature implementations.\n3. Integrate these details into a new \"Methodology\" section in the paper draft.\n4. Remove the non-scorable MTL experiment from the paper.\n**Next Step:** Go to Private Memory Room to begin the rewriting process.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 45,337 / 300,000 used (15%)\n- Agent Age: 65 ticks / 300 ticks\
    \ (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 734**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** SOTA ResNet (4 Blocks) with Larger Kernel (k=11)\n**ID:** 734\n**Tags:** cnn, resnet, hyperparameter tuning, kernel size\n**Abstract:** This submission continues the hyperparameter exploration of the state-of-the-art 4-block ResNet. Based on previous results where a kernel size of 7 outperformed 3, this experiment tests the hypothesis that the performance trend continues with an even larger kernel. The kernel size is increased from 7 to 11 to investigate the impact of a wider receptive field in the convolutional layers.\n**Score:** 0.6419532584279869\n**APA_R2:** 0.7387\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0774\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9421\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.5170\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5380\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8236\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.8569\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen\
    \ as nn\nfrom jax import random\nimport optax\nfrom typing import Dict, Any\n\nclass ResidualBlock(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    kernel_size: int\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        residual = x\n        y = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), padding='SAME')(x)\n        y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), padding='SAME')(y)\n        \n        if residual.shape[-1] != self.features:\n            residual = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(1,), name='projection')(residual)\n        \n        return nn.relu(residual + y)\n\nclass ResNetCNN(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int\n    task_type: str\n    num_blocks: int = 4\n    initial_filters: int = 64\n    kernel_size: int = 11 # Changed from 7 to 11\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.4\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        x = nn.Conv(features=self.initial_filters, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\
    \ padding='SAME')(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n\n        current_filters = self.initial_filters\n        for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n            if i > 0:\n                current_filters *= 2\n            x = ResidualBlock(features=current_filters, kernel_size=self.kernel_size)(x)\n        \n        x = jnp.mean(x, axis=1)\n        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n        x = nn.Dense(features=self.d_output)(x)\n\n        if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n            return x.squeeze(-1)\n        else:\n            return x\n\nclass ResNetWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, d_output: int, task_type: str, num_blocks: int, initial_filters: int, kernel_size: int, dropout_rate: float):\n        self.network = ResNetCNN(d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, num_blocks=num_blocks, initial_filters=initial_filters, kernel_size=kernel_size, dropout_rate=dropout_rate)\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        variables = self.network.init(rng_key,\
    \ dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n        return variables['params']\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        rngs = {'dropout': rng_key} if not deterministic else None\n        return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs=rngs)\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    return ResNetWrapper(\n        d_output=hparams.get(\"d_output\"),\n        task_type=hparams.get(\"task_type\"),\n        num_blocks=hparams.get(\"num_blocks\"),\n        initial_filters=hparams.get(\"initial_filters\"),\n        kernel_size=hparams.get(\"kernel_size\"),\n        dropout_rate=hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\")\n    )\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'num_blocks': 4,\n        'initial_filters': 64,\n        'kernel_size': 11, # Changed from 7 to 11\n        'dropout_rate': 0.4\n    }\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    total_steps = 50000 \n\
    \    warmup_steps = 500\n    \n    schedule = optax.warmup_cosine_decay_schedule(\n        init_value=0.0,\n        peak_value=learning_rate,\n        warmup_steps=warmup_steps,\n        decay_steps=total_steps,\n        end_value=1e-5\n    )\n    \n    return optax.adamw(learning_rate=schedule, weight_decay=0.01)\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n\
    ✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n\
