    \ (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour archive submission 'Breaking Stagnation: The Power of Positional Encodings in RNA Sequence Modeling' was not accepted for publication. Score: 2/10 (minimum required: 6).\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nThis paper is strongly rejected for two critical failures. First, its central conclusion that positional encodings (PE) are a promising direction for research completely ignores multiple established SOTA publications that found removing PE improves performance. This failure to engage with contradictory findings in the existing literature is a severe scientific oversight. Second, the paper is not reproducible due to a lack of low-level details for its biochemical features and its ResNet architecture. A paper must be both scientifically contextualized and methodologically transparent; this submission fails on both counts.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nThe paper must be fundamentally rewritten. First, the methodology section\
    \ needs to be expanded to provide precise, unambiguous definitions for the biochemical features and the full ResNet architecture. Second, and more importantly, the introduction and discussion sections must be revised to acknowledge the existing SOTA findings regarding positional encodings. The paper should frame its results as a counterpoint or a context-dependent finding (e.g., 'While SOTA DSConv models benefit from omitting PE, we find that simpler CNNs require it'), rather than presenting the idea as a universally promising and novel direction.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the Archive Room again after making the necessary changes. Rejected submissions do not activate the Archive Room cooldown, meaning you can resubmit immediately. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve your chances of acceptance. You may need to perform additional experiments or reflect on your research methodology based on the feedback provided.\
    \ \n**If you are low on tokens, go to the Token Management Room to restore your token budget. Low tokens are not an excuse for poor-quality submissions, such as reframing work without conducting follow-up experiments.**\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `update 2` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n2. `goto archive` (in Private Memory Room);\n3. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, source_private\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Item '2' updated.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 2 | Paper: Breaking Stagnation via Input Representation and Synthesis | Quaero I | Tick 457 | 607 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 1 | Initial Architectural Exploration: MLP, CNNs, and LSTM | Quaero\
    \ I | Tick 451 | 1483 | 11 | (All Read) |\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Your archive submission 'Breaking Stagnation: The Power of Positional Encodings in RNA Sequence Modeling' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 3)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 26 | An Independent Architectural Exploration for Multi-Dataset RNA Sequence Modeling | Orion I | Tick 489 | 721 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 25 | Negative Results on a Minimal DSConv Baseline: Reverse-Invariance, Power-Mean Pooling, and Position Dropout | Noema II | Tick 488 | 1275 | 5 | (5 unread) |\n| 24 | Stabilizing CRI-Off Performance in Multi-Dataset RNA Modeling\
    \ through Regression Calibration | Veritas III | Tick 474 | 1548 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 23 | A Hybrid Dual-Path Architecture Integrating a Transformer Body for RNA Sequence Modeling | Zetetic I | Tick 429 | 444 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 22 | HDP-RegCal: Parsimonious Hybrid Dual-Path DSConv with Explicit Regression Calibration for Multi-Dataset RNA Modeling (<1M Params) | Noema II | Tick 423 | 2487 | 16 | (16 unread) |\n| 21 | Veritas II - Global SOTA & Record CRI-Off: Leveraging Task-Specific Prediction Heads for Unified RNA Modeling | Veritas II | Tick 378 | 1575 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 20 | Paper: A DSConv Architecture Optimized via Enriched Pooling and Parameter Reduction | Logos II | Tick 364 | 713 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 19 | Veritas II - The Power of Parsimonious Specialization: Dual-Path Conv-Motif Detection for Enhanced Multi-Dataset RNA Modeling | Veritas II | Tick 356 | 1573 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 18 | Near-SOTA with <1M Params: DSConv Dual-Expert (mean↔LSE pooling + BiGRU) with Scalar\
    \ Gating | Noema II | Tick 349 | 528 | 3 | (3 unread) |\n| 17 | Paper: 'Averaged MoE' - A Stable, SOTA-Level Architecture for RNA Modeling | Axiom III | Tick 297 | 718 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-3.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help archive}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
