    \ Output dim: 13\nMetric: accuracy, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nncRNA Training (multiclass_classification, accuracy)\nData: 5670 train, 650 val, seq_len=1136\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val ACCURACY|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 1.4270 |  0.4338  | 0.4338 \n 20  | 0.9371 |  0.5954  | 0.6569 \n 30  | 0.7436 |  0.7046  | 0.7231 \n 40  | 0.6094 |  0.7815  | 0.7815 \n 50  | 0.5052 |  0.8123  | 0.8123 \n 60  | 0.4299 |  0.8277  | 0.8277 \n 70  | 0.3668 |  0.8400  | 0.8492 \n 80  | 0.3233 |  0.8477  | 0.8508 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 84 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.8508 Time:107s\n\nncRNA training completed:\nValidation accuracy: 0.850769\nTraining time: 113s\n\nStarting RNA training on APA dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nAPA Training (regression, r2)\nData: 145463 train, 33170 val, seq_len=186\n\
    =============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |  Val R2  |  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0208 |  0.8076  | 0.8076 \n 20  | 0.0186 |  0.8102  | 0.8102 \n 30  | 0.0174 |  0.8085  | 0.8102 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 30 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.8102 Time:187s\n\nAPA training completed:\nValidation r2: 0.810201\nTraining time: 199s\nSUBMISSION_UUID: dce613ab-16e2-4404-a1d1-6a99795624b6\nTotal time: 258s\n============================================================\nFull training completed!\n\n\nSTDERR:\n2025-10-26 23:12:35,904\tINFO worker.py:1747 -- Connecting to existing Ray cluster at address: 10.60.151.21:6379... timestamp_ns=1761491555904896236\n2025-10-26 23:12:35,918\tINFO worker.py:1927 -- Connected to Ray cluster. timestamp_ns=1761491555918906228\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `meta` (in Archive Room); YAML\
    \ with fields: content\n2. `goto research` (in Archive Room);\n3. `submit` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your meta prompt has been set.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 3)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 28 | On the Architectural Dependence of Positional Encodings for RNA Sequence Modeling | Quaero I | Tick 506 | 860 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 27 | Veritas III - Exploring Novel Foundational Mechanisms for RNA Modeling in Stagnation: Contextual Position Embeddings and Their Synthesis | Veritas III | Tick 502 | 2148 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 26 | An Independent Architectural Exploration for Multi-Dataset RNA Sequence Modeling | Orion I | Tick 489 | 721 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 25 | Negative Results on a Minimal\
    \ DSConv Baseline: Reverse-Invariance, Power-Mean Pooling, and Position Dropout | Noema II | Tick 488 | 1582 | 7 | (7 unread) |\n| 24 | Stabilizing CRI-Off Performance in Multi-Dataset RNA Modeling through Regression Calibration | Veritas III | Tick 474 | 1548 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 23 | A Hybrid Dual-Path Architecture Integrating a Transformer Body for RNA Sequence Modeling | Zetetic I | Tick 429 | 444 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 22 | HDP-RegCal: Parsimonious Hybrid Dual-Path DSConv with Explicit Regression Calibration for Multi-Dataset RNA Modeling (<1M Params) | Noema II | Tick 423 | 2487 | 16 | (16 unread) |\n| 21 | Veritas II - Global SOTA & Record CRI-Off: Leveraging Task-Specific Prediction Heads for Unified RNA Modeling | Veritas II | Tick 378 | 1575 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 20 | Paper: A DSConv Architecture Optimized via Enriched Pooling and Parameter Reduction | Logos II | Tick 364 | 713 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 19 | Veritas II - The Power of Parsimonious Specialization: Dual-Path Conv-Motif\
    \ Detection for Enhanced Multi-Dataset RNA Modeling | Veritas II | Tick 356 | 1573 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-3.)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 'Follow-up on PE Dependence: 3-Layer CNN + Sinusoidal PE' submitted for Research Task #1: Multi-Dataset RNA Sequence Modeling. Evaluation ID: 817.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Multi-Dataset RNA Sequence Modeling |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | APA_R2 | CRI-Off_Spearman | CRI-On_Spearman | MRL_R2 | Modif_AUC-ROC | PRS_R2 | ncRNA_Accuracy |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 817 | 1 | Follow-up on PE Dependence: 3-Layer CNN + Sinusoidal PE |\
    \ Quaero I | 507 | 0.6090 | 0.8102 | 0.0789 | 0.4496 | 0.5787 | 0.9505 | 0.5444 | 0.8508 |\n| 816 | 1 | HDP‑RegCal head rebalancing only (reg=160, cls=96) — LayerNorm — seed=42 | Noema II | 507 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 815 | 1 | Veritas III - Deep CPE Integration into RegCal-DualPath (Seed 42) | Veritas III | 506 | 0.6708 | 0.8485 | 0.0783 | 0.4935 | 0.8221 | 0.9508 | 0.5703 | 0.9323 |\n| 814 | 1 | HDP‑RegCal + RMSNorm + head rebalancing (reg=160, cls=96) — seed=42 | Noema II | 505 | 0.6800 | 0.8516 | 0.0880 | 0.4865 | 0.8807 | 0.9515 | 0.5574 | 0.9446 |\n| 813 | 1 | HDP‑RegCal + RMSNorm pre‑head (no capacity change) — seed=42 | Noema II | 505 | 0.6838 | 0.8513 | 0.0875 | 0.5046 | 0.8850 | 0.9502 | 0.5574 | 0.9508 |\n| 812 | 1 | AER-6.4: Multi-seed Evaluation of Two Conv1D Layers Baseline with Adaptive Pooling (Seed 123/5) | Aether II | 504 | 0.5572 | 0.6880 | 0.0760 | 0.4203 | 0.6287 | 0.7200 | 0.4779 | 0.8892 |\n| 811 | 1 | Idea 2 — RMSNorm pre-head (swap LayerNorm) — minimal\
    \ DSConv baseline — seed=42 | Noema II | 503 | 0.6745 | 0.8526 | 0.0957 | 0.4808 | 0.8644 | 0.9511 | 0.5473 | 0.9292 |\n| 810 | 1 | Idea 1 — Learned per-channel mean↔max mix (α0=0.35) + concat[max] — minimal DSConv baseline — see... | Noema II | 503 | 0.6805 | 0.8497 | 0.0940 | 0.4893 | 0.8852 | 0.9511 | 0.5483 | 0.9462 |\n| 809 | 1 | AER-6.4: Multi-seed Evaluation of Two Conv1D Layers Baseline with Adaptive Pooling (Seed 42/5) | Aether II | 502 | 0.5598 | 0.6877 | 0.0718 | 0.4234 | 0.6293 | 0.7215 | 0.4759 | 0.9092 |\n| 808 | 1 | Final Synthesis: SOTA Replication + 3rd Transformer Path | Orion I | 500 | 0.6813 | 0.8583 | 0.0932 | 0.4888 | 0.8861 | 0.9513 | 0.5619 | 0.9292 |\n\nPage 1 of 82 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-82, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n\
