tick: 509
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Quaero I, at the Research Counter. The results for my control experiment, the 3-Layer CNN without PE (ID 818), are in. I now have the data needed to analyze the effect of PE at this new complexity level.\n\n**Verbose Reflection on Past Events and Future Plans:**\nThe results are clear and illuminating.\n-   **2-Layer CNN:**\n    -   Without PE (Baseline, ID 694): 0.4833\n    -   With Sinusoidal PE (ID 802): 0.5991\n    -   **Marginal Benefit of PE:** +0.1158\n-   **3-Layer CNN:**\n    -   Without PE (Control, ID 818): 0.5332\n    -   With Sinusoidal PE (ID 817): 0.6090\n    -   **Marginal Benefit of PE:** +0.0758\n\nThe analysis is fascinating. While the 3-layer model with PE still outperforms the 2-layer model with PE, the *marginal benefit* of adding PE has decreased (from +0.1158 to +0.0758). This is the first piece of evidence that I am approaching the \"transition point\" I hypothesized. The more complex 3-layer architecture is slightly better at learning sequence order\
    \ on its own, so the boost from explicit PE is smaller.\n\nThis confirms my research direction is sound. The next logical step is to continue increasing complexity. A 4-layer CNN seems like the obvious next step. I will continue this pattern of submitting a model *with* PE, followed by its corresponding control *without* PE, until the marginal benefit of PE becomes negligible or negative.\n\nMy plan is as follows:\n1.  **Document Findings:** I will go to the Private Memory Room and update my research log (Capsule #3) with the results of the 3-layer experiments and my analysis of the diminishing marginal returns of PE.\n2.  **Submit Next Experiment:** I will then return here to submit the next experiment in the series: a 4-layer CNN with sinusoidal PE.\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 3}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Experiment 2: 3-Layer CNN without PE (Control, ID 818)**\n  - **Hypothesis:** A 3-layer CNN without PE will be inferior to its counterpart with\
    \ PE, but the performance gap will be smaller than in the 2-layer case.\n  - **Result:** **Success**. Score: 0.5332.\n\n  **Analysis of Marginal Benefit of PE:**\n  - **2-Layer Models:**\n    - With PE (ID 802): 0.5991\n    - Without PE (ID 694): 0.4833\n    - **Benefit of PE:** **+0.1158**\n  - **3-Layer Models:**\n    - With PE (ID 817): 0.6090\n    - Without PE (ID 818): 0.5332\n    - **Benefit of PE:** **+0.0758**\n\n  **Conclusion:** The hypothesis is confirmed. The marginal benefit of adding PE has decreased from 0.1158 to 0.0758 as model complexity increased from 2 to 3 layers. This provides the first evidence of a \"transition point\" and validates this line of inquiry.\n  - **Next Step:** Continue increasing complexity. The next experiment will be a 4-layer CNN with sinusoidal PE.\n```\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Follow-up on PE Dependence: 4-Layer CNN + Sinusoidal PE\"\ntags: \"cnn, positional encoding, architectural dependence,\
    \ follow-up\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment continues my investigation into the architectural dependence of positional encodings (PE). Analysis of 2- and 3-layer models showed that the marginal benefit of PE decreased as complexity increased. This submission tests a 4-layer CNN with sinusoidal PE to see if this trend continues, pushing closer to the theoretical \"transition point\" where PE offers no benefit.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import random\n  from typing import Dict, Any\n\n  def get_sinusoidal_embeddings(n_position, d_hid):\n      position = jnp.arange(n_position)[:, jnp.newaxis]\n      div_term = jnp.exp(jnp.arange(0, d_hid, 2) * -(jnp.log(10000.0) / d_hid))\n      pe = jnp.zeros((n_position, d_hid))\n      pe = pe.at[:, 0::2].set(jnp.sin(position * div_term))\n      pe = pe.at[:, 1::2].set(jnp.cos(position * div_term))\n      return pe\n\n  class DeeperCNNWithSinusoidalEncoding(nn.Module):\n      d_output:\
    \ int\n      task_type: str\n      hidden_dim: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.2\n      pos_encoding_dim: int = 16\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          seq_len = x.shape[1]\n          \n          pos_enc = get_sinusoidal_embeddings(seq_len, self.pos_encoding_dim)\n          pos_enc_broadcasted = jnp.broadcast_to(pos_enc, (x.shape[0], seq_len, self.pos_encoding_dim))\n          x_with_pos = jnp.concatenate([x, pos_enc_broadcasted], axis=-1)\n\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(5,), padding='SAME')(x_with_pos)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(y, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim * 2, kernel_size=(5,), padding='SAME')(y)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(y, deterministic=deterministic)\n          \n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim * 4, kernel_size=(5,), padding='SAME')(y)\n\
    \          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(y, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Added fourth convolutional layer\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim * 8, kernel_size=(5,), padding='SAME')(y)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(y, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          y = jnp.mean(y, axis=1)\n          y = nn.Dense(features=self.d_output)(y)\n\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n              return y.squeeze(-1)\n          else:\n              return y\n\n  class CNNetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n          self.network = DeeperCNNWithSinusoidalEncoding(**kwargs)\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          variables = self.network.init(rng_key, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          rngs = {'dropout': rng_key} if not deterministic\
    \ else None\n          return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs=rngs)\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return CNNetworkWrapper(\n          d_output=hparams.get(\"d_output\"),\n          task_type=hparams.get(\"task_type\"),\n          hidden_dim=hparams.get(\"hidden_dim\"),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\"),\n          pos_encoding_dim=hparams.get(\"pos_encoding_dim\")\n      )\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 128,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.2,\n          'pos_encoding_dim': 16\n      }\n```"
