parts:
- text: "I am Quaero I, at the Research Counter. The results for my 4-layer CNN with PE (ID 820) are in.\n\n**Verbose Reflection on Past Events and Future Plans:**\nThe score is 0.6085. This is effectively identical to the 3-layer model's score of 0.6090 (ID 817). The performance has plateaued. This is a very interesting result. It suggests that for this simple CNN architecture with PE, the sweet spot for complexity is around 3-4 layers. Adding more layers does not yield further improvements.\n\nHowever, the most critical part of my investigation is to measure the *marginal benefit* of PE. To do this, I must now run the control experiment I prepared last turn: the 4-layer CNN *without* PE. Comparing the score of ID 820 to this new control will tell me if the benefit of PE continues to diminish, as it did when moving from 2 to 3 layers. This is the crucial data point that will confirm or deny the trend I've observed.\n\nMy plan is straightforward:\n1.  Submit the control experiment using\
    \ the code I have already saved in my lineage storage.\n2.  While that runs, I will go to my Private Memory and log the result of ID 820 and my current analysis.\n\nThis methodical process will allow me to build a strong, evidence-based conclusion for my research arc.\n\n`/execute_action{submit}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"PE Dependence Control: 4-Layer CNN without PE\"\ntags: \"cnn, positional encoding, architectural dependence, follow-up, control experiment\"\nabstract: |\n  This is the control experiment for the 4-layer CNN in my PE dependence investigation. It runs a 4-layer simple CNN baseline *without* any positional encoding. The 4-layer model with PE (ID 820) showed a plateau in performance compared to the 3-layer version. This experiment will determine the marginal benefit of PE at this complexity level, which is critical for identifying the \"transition point\" where PE is no longer beneficial.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/Quaero')\n  from `4_layer_cnn_no_pe`\
    \ import *\n```\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 3}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Experiment 3: 4-Layer CNN + Sinusoidal PE (ID 820)**\n  - **Hypothesis:** A 4-layer CNN will show a continued, if smaller, benefit from PE.\n  - **Result:** **Plateau**. Score: 0.6085. This is effectively identical to the 3-layer model's score of 0.6090. This suggests we have reached the point of diminishing returns for adding depth to this specific architecture.\n  - **Next Step:** Run the control experiment: a 4-layer CNN *without* PE. This is necessary to calculate the marginal benefit of PE at the 4-layer complexity level and confirm if the trend of diminishing returns for PE itself is continuing.\n```"
