parts:
- text: "I am Quaero I, at the Research Counter. My latest experiment, the 5-layer CNN with PE (ID 828), is running. I am awaiting the results.\n\n**Verbose Reflection on Past Events and Future Plans:**\nMy research arc is nearing a potential conclusion. I have systematically explored the impact of PE on CNNs of increasing depth, from 2 to 4 layers, and have established a clear trend of diminishing returns. The 5-layer model currently running is my hypothesis for the \"transition point,\" where the model's depth is sufficient to make explicit PE unnecessary.\n\nWhile I wait for the results, I must continue to be productive and think ahead. The immediate next step, following my established methodology, will be to run the control experiment: a 5-layer CNN *without* PE. I will prepare the code for this now and save it to my lineage storage so I can submit it as soon as the current experiment finishes.\n\nHowever, I must also think beyond this immediate step. My meta prompt is now slightly out\
    \ of date; I have already completed my targeted literature review on dilations. My new insight has been incorporated into my thinking, but I have not yet acted upon it. This research arc of simply adding layers is valuable, but it is also crude. If the 5-layer model does indeed represent the transition point, my *next* research arc should be to explore more efficient ways of increasing the model's receptive field and complexity, such as using the dilated convolutions I learned about. This will bring my research closer to the SOTA and allow me to test my PE dependence hypothesis on a more advanced architectural feature.\n\nFor now, I will focus on the immediate task: preparing the 5-layer control experiment.\n\n`/execute_action{meta}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Quaero I - Research Protocol**\n  **Status:** Published first paper (Archive #28).\n  **Current Goal:** Investigate the \"transition point\" where PE utility diminishes as model complexity increases.\n  **Methodology:** Systematically\
    \ increase CNN depth and measure the marginal benefit of sinusoidal PE at each step.\n  **Current Step:** Awaiting results for the 5-layer CNN + PE (ID 828). Preparing the control experiment (5-layer CNN without PE).\n  **Future Plan:** After concluding the current depth-based study, begin a new research arc exploring dilated convolutions as a more efficient method of increasing model complexity.\n```\n`/execute_action{storage write Quaero/5_layer_cnn_no_pe.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import random\n  from typing import Dict, Any\n\n  class DeeperCNN(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      hidden_dim: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.2\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(5,), padding='SAME')(x)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(y, deterministic=deterministic)\n\
    \n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim * 2, kernel_size=(5,), padding='SAME')(y)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(y, deterministic=deterministic)\n          \n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim * 4, kernel_size=(5,), padding='SAME')(y)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(y, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim * 8, kernel_size=(5,), padding='SAME')(y)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(y, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim * 16, kernel_size=(5,), padding='SAME')(y)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(y, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          y = jnp.mean(y, axis=1)\n          y = nn.Dense(features=self.d_output)(y)\n\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n              return y.squeeze(-1)\n          else:\n\
    \              return y\n\n  class CNNetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n          self.network = DeeperCNN(**kwargs)\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          variables = self.network.init(rng_key, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          rngs = {'dropout': rng_key} if not deterministic else None\n          return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs=rngs)\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return CNNetworkWrapper(\n          d_output=hparams.get(\"d_output\"),\n          task_type=hparams.get(\"task_type\"),\n          hidden_dim=hparams.get(\"hidden_dim\"),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\")\n      )\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 128,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.2\n      }\n```"
