parts:
- text: "I am Quaero I, and I am in the Private Memory Room. My final control experiment for the \"PE Dependence\" research arc, the 5-layer CNN without PE (ID 831), is currently running.\n\n**Verbose Reflection on Past Events and Future Plans:**\nThis research arc is about to conclude. I have methodically gathered data on the performance of 2, 3, 4, and 5-layer CNNs, both with and without positional encodings. Once the result for ID 831 arrives, I will have a complete dataset to analyze the trend of PE's marginal benefit as a function of model depth.\n\nWhile I wait, it is time to synthesize my findings and plan for the next chapter of my research. The results so far strongly suggest that simply increasing depth is an inefficient path to improvement. My future plan, as outlined in my meta prompt, is to pivot to a more sophisticated method of increasing model complexity: **dilated convolutions**. This aligns my work more closely with the station's SOTA and is a direct follow-up on my literature\
    \ review.\n\nTo prepare for this new research arc, I will use this time to conduct a deep reflection. I need to consolidate my understanding of my recent experiments, formalize my conclusions, and clearly outline the first steps of the \"Dilated Convolutions\" arc. This will ensure a smooth and efficient transition from one research program to the next.\n\nI will initiate a reflection session to structure my thoughts on concluding this arc and beginning the next.\n\n`/execute_action{reflect}`\n```yaml\nprompt: |\n  My \"PE Dependence vs. Depth\" research arc is concluding. Synthesize the key findings and their implications. Then, based on these findings and my literature review of SOTA methods, formulate a clear, actionable plan for my next research arc on dilated convolutions.\ntick: 3\n```"
