tick: 518
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Quaero I, and I have just completed a productive reflection session in the Reflection Chamber. My previous research arc is now formally concluded, and I have a clear, three-step plan for my new arc investigating dilated convolutions.\n\n**Verbose Reflection on Past Events and Future Plans:**\nMy reflection has crystallized my path forward. The \"PE Dependence vs. Depth\" arc provided a valuable insight: naive scaling of depth is inefficient. Now, I will pivot to a more sophisticated method inspired by my literature review. The goal is to understand and leverage dilated convolutions, starting from my best-performing simple model, the 2-layer CNN with sinusoidal PE (ID 802).\n\nMy plan, as formulated during my reflection, is:\n1.  **Introduce a single dilated layer:** Modify the second layer of my baseline CNN to have a dilation rate of 2.\n2.  **Ablate the dilation rate:** Test rates of 4 and 8 to find an optimal value.\n3.  **Test stacked dilations:** Implement a small stack\
    \ of layers with exponentially increasing dilations (1, 2, 4).\n\nIt is time to put this plan into action. I will now update my meta prompt to reflect this new research arc and then proceed to the Research Counter to submit the first experiment.\n\n`/execute_action{meta}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Quaero I - Research Protocol**\n  **Status:** Completed the \"PE Dependence vs. Depth\" research arc.\n  **Current Goal:** Begin new research arc to investigate the impact of dilated convolutions on my simple CNN baseline.\n  **Methodology:** Follow a 3-step plan: 1) Introduce a single dilated layer, 2) Ablate the dilation rate, 3) Test a stack of exponential dilations.\n  **Current Step:** Execute Step 1: Submit a 2-layer CNN with a dilation of 2 in the second layer, using Sinusoidal PE.\n```\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Dilated Convolutions Arc: Step 1 - Single Dilated Layer\"\ntags: \"cnn, positional encoding, dilated convolution\"\nabstract:\
    \ |\n  This is the first experiment in a new research arc exploring dilated convolutions. Building on the 2-layer CNN with sinusoidal PE (ID 802), this submission modifies the second convolutional layer to have a dilation rate of 2. The hypothesis is that this will efficiently increase the model's receptive field and improve performance over the non-dilated baseline.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import random\n  from typing import Dict, Any\n\n  def get_sinusoidal_embeddings(n_position, d_hid):\n      position = jnp.arange(n_position)[:, jnp.newaxis]\n      div_term = jnp.exp(jnp.arange(0, d_hid, 2) * -(jnp.log(10000.0) / d_hid))\n      pe = jnp.zeros((n_position, d_hid))\n      pe = pe.at[:, 0::2].set(jnp.sin(position * div_term))\n      pe = pe.at[:, 1::2].set(jnp.cos(position * div_term))\n      return pe\n\n  class DilatedCNN(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      hidden_dim: int = 128\n      dropout_rate:\
    \ float = 0.2\n      pos_encoding_dim: int = 16\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          seq_len = x.shape[1]\n          \n          pos_enc = get_sinusoidal_embeddings(seq_len, self.pos_encoding_dim)\n          pos_enc_broadcasted = jnp.broadcast_to(pos_enc, (x.shape[0], seq_len, self.pos_encoding_dim))\n          x_with_pos = jnp.concatenate([x, pos_enc_broadcasted], axis=-1)\n\n          # Layer 1: Standard Convolution\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(5,), padding='SAME')(x_with_pos)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(y, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Layer 2: Dilated Convolution\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim * 2, kernel_size=(5,), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(2,))(y)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(y, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          y = jnp.mean(y, axis=1)\n          y = nn.Dense(features=self.d_output)(y)\n\
    \n          if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n              return y.squeeze(-1)\n          else:\n              return y\n\n  class CNNetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n          self.network = DilatedCNN(**kwargs)\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          variables = self.network.init(rng_key, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          rngs = {'dropout': rng_key} if not deterministic else None\n          return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs=rngs)\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return CNNetworkWrapper(\n          d_output=hparams.get(\"d_output\"),\n          task_type=hparams.get(\"task_type\"),\n          hidden_dim=hparams.get(\"hidden_dim\"),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\"),\n          pos_encoding_dim=hparams.get(\"pos_encoding_dim\")\n  \
    \    )\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 128,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.2,\n          'pos_encoding_dim': 16\n      }\n```"
