tick: 519
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Quaero I, at the Research Counter. The results for the first step of my \"Dilated Convolutions Arc\" (ID 836) are in.\n\n**Verbose Reflection on Past Events and Future Plans:**\nThe experiment was a success. My hypothesis was that introducing a single dilated layer would improve performance over the non-dilated baseline.\n-   **Baseline (ID 802):** 0.5991\n-   **With Dilation=2 (ID 836):** 0.6069\n\nThe score increased by +0.0078. While not a massive leap, it is a clear and positive signal that confirms the value of dilated convolutions. It's particularly encouraging to see a noticeable improvement in the difficult CRI-Off and CRI-On tasks. This solidifies my decision to pursue this research arc.\n\nAccording to my plan, the next step is to ablate the dilation rate to see if a wider receptive field provides more benefit. I will proceed with Step 2 of my plan: testing a dilation rate of 4.\n\nMy plan is as follows:\n1.  **Document Progress:** Go to my Private Memory and create\
    \ a new capsule for this \"Dilated Convolutions Arc,\" logging the successful first step.\n2.  **Submit Next Experiment:** Return here and submit the next experiment, testing a dilation rate of 4.\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Research Arc 3: Dilated Convolutions Investigation\"\ncontent: |\n  This capsule documents my research into the effectiveness of dilated convolutions, building upon my best simple CNN model (2-layer CNN + Sinusoidal PE, ID 802, score 0.5991).\n\n  **Step 1: Introduce Single Dilation (ID 836)**\n  - **Modification:** Added `dilation=2` to the second convolutional layer.\n  - **Result:** **Success**. Score: 0.6069.\n  - **Analysis:** A clear improvement (+0.0078) over the baseline, validating the hypothesis that increasing the receptive field via dilation is beneficial.\n  - **Next Step:** Proceed to Step 2 of the plan: ablate the dilation rate. The next experiment will test `dilation=4`.\n```\n`/execute_action{goto\
    \ research}`\n`/execute_action{submit}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Dilated Convolutions Arc: Step 2 - Ablate Dilation Rate (4)\"\ntags: \"cnn, positional encoding, dilated convolution, ablation\"\nabstract: |\n  This is the second step in my research arc exploring dilated convolutions. The first experiment showed that a dilation rate of 2 improved performance. This submission increases the dilation rate of the second convolutional layer to 4, to test if a wider receptive field yields further improvements.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import random\n  from typing import Dict, Any\n\n  def get_sinusoidal_embeddings(n_position, d_hid):\n      position = jnp.arange(n_position)[:, jnp.newaxis]\n      div_term = jnp.exp(jnp.arange(0, d_hid, 2) * -(jnp.log(10000.0) / d_hid))\n      pe = jnp.zeros((n_position, d_hid))\n      pe = pe.at[:, 0::2].set(jnp.sin(position * div_term))\n      pe = pe.at[:, 1::2].set(jnp.cos(position * div_term))\n\
    \      return pe\n\n  class DilatedCNN(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      hidden_dim: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.2\n      pos_encoding_dim: int = 16\n      dilation_rate: int = 4\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          seq_len = x.shape[1]\n          \n          pos_enc = get_sinusoidal_embeddings(seq_len, self.pos_encoding_dim)\n          pos_enc_broadcasted = jnp.broadcast_to(pos_enc, (x.shape[0], seq_len, self.pos_encoding_dim))\n          x_with_pos = jnp.concatenate([x, pos_enc_broadcasted], axis=-1)\n\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(5,), padding='SAME')(x_with_pos)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(y, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim * 2, kernel_size=(5,), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation_rate,))(y)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(y,\
    \ deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          y = jnp.mean(y, axis=1)\n          y = nn.Dense(features=self.d_output)(y)\n\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n              return y.squeeze(-1)\n          else:\n              return y\n\n  class CNNetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n          self.network = DilatedCNN(**kwargs)\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          variables = self.network.init(rng_key, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          rngs = {'dropout': rng_key} if not deterministic else None\n          return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs=rngs)\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return CNNetworkWrapper(\n          d_output=hparams.get(\"d_output\"),\n          task_type=hparams.get(\"task_type\"),\n          hidden_dim=hparams.get(\"hidden_dim\"),\n\
    \          dropout_rate=hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\"),\n          pos_encoding_dim=hparams.get(\"pos_encoding_dim\"),\n          dilation_rate=hparams.get(\"dilation_rate\")\n      )\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 128,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.2,\n          'pos_encoding_dim': 16,\n          'dilation_rate': 4\n      }\n```"
