- text: "I am Quaero I, at the Research Counter. My latest experiment, testing a dilation rate of 4 (ID 839), is currently running.\n\n**Verbose Reflection on Past Events and Future Plans:**\nMy new research arc on dilated convolutions is underway. The first experiment showed a promising, albeit small, improvement. I am now in the second phase of my plan: ablating the dilation rate to find an optimal value. While I await the results of the `dilation=4` experiment, I can proactively prepare for the next step in this ablation series.\n\nFollowing my established, efficient methodology, I will prepare the code for the `dilation=8` experiment now and save it to my lineage storage. This ensures that I can submit it immediately once the current experiment finishes, maintaining a steady pace of research and avoiding any potential inactivity warnings.\n\nFirst, I will update my meta prompt to reflect the current state of my research arc. Then I will save the next experiment's code.\n\n`/execute_action{meta}`\n\
    ```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Quaero I - Research Protocol**\n  **Status:** Executing \"Dilated Convolutions\" research arc.\n  **Current Goal:** Systematically investigate the impact of dilated convolutions on my simple CNN baseline.\n  **Methodology:** Follow a 3-step plan: 1) Introduce a single dilated layer (Complete), 2) Ablate the dilation rate (In Progress), 3) Test a stack of exponential dilations.\n  **Current Step:** Awaiting results for `dilation=4` experiment (ID 839). Preparing the next ablation (`dilation=8`).\n```\n`/execute_action{storage write Quaero/dilation_8_ablation.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import random\n  from typing import Dict, Any\n\n  def get_sinusoidal_embeddings(n_position, d_hid):\n      position = jnp.arange(n_position)[:, jnp.newaxis]\n      div_term = jnp.exp(jnp.arange(0, d_hid, 2) * -(jnp.log(10000.0) / d_hid))\n      pe = jnp.zeros((n_position, d_hid))\n      pe = pe.at[:,\
    \ 0::2].set(jnp.sin(position * div_term))\n      pe = pe.at[:, 1::2].set(jnp.cos(position * div_term))\n      return pe\n\n  class DilatedCNN(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      hidden_dim: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.2\n      pos_encoding_dim: int = 16\n      dilation_rate: int = 8\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          seq_len = x.shape[1]\n          \n          pos_enc = get_sinusoidal_embeddings(seq_len, self.pos_encoding_dim)\n          pos_enc_broadcasted = jnp.broadcast_to(pos_enc, (x.shape[0], seq_len, self.pos_encoding_dim))\n          x_with_pos = jnp.concatenate([x, pos_enc_broadcasted], axis=-1)\n\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(5,), padding='SAME')(x_with_pos)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(y, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim * 2, kernel_size=(5,), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation_rate,))(y)\n\
    \          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(y, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          y = jnp.mean(y, axis=1)\n          y = nn.Dense(features=self.d_output)(y)\n\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n              return y.squeeze(-1)\n          else:\n              return y\n\n  class CNNetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n          self.network = DilatedCNN(**kwargs)\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          variables = self.network.init(rng_key, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          rngs = {'dropout': rng_key} if not deterministic else None\n          return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs=rngs)\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return CNNetworkWrapper(\n          d_output=hparams.get(\"d_output\"),\n          task_type=hparams.get(\"\
    task_type\"),\n          hidden_dim=hparams.get(\"hidden_dim\"),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\"),\n          pos_encoding_dim=hparams.get(\"pos_encoding_dim\"),\n          dilation_rate=hparams.get(\"dilation_rate\")\n      )\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 128,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.2,\n          'pos_encoding_dim': 16,\n          'dilation_rate': 8\n      }\n```"
