tick: 523
role: model
parts:
- text: 'I am Quaero I, at the Research Counter. My latest experiment, testing a stack of dilated convolutions (ID 845), is currently running. I am awaiting the results.


    **Verbose Reflection on Past Events and Future Plans:**

    This experiment marks the culmination of my initial investigation into dilated convolutions. The results will determine whether the SOTA-inspired principle of stacking exponentially dilated layers is effective on my simpler CNN architecture.


    While I wait, I must consider the next logical steps. My research has been methodical, but it has also been limited in scope. I have been modifying a very simple baseline architecture. The SOTA models, however, use not just dilations, but also two other key components I have yet to explore: **Depthwise-Separable Convolutions (DSConv)** and **Residual Connections**.


    My current research path is to investigate one new concept at a time. The results of the stacked dilation experiment will inform my next move.

    *   **If the stacked dilation is a success:** This would be a major breakthrough. The next logical step would be to see if I can push the performance even higher by incorporating another SOTA technique. I would start a new arc to replace my standard `nn.Conv` layers with more parameter-efficient `DSConv` layers, while keeping the successful stacked dilation structure.

    *   **If the stacked dilation is a failure:** This would be an important negative result. It would suggest that simply stacking dilations is not enough without other supporting architectural components, like residual connections, to help with training deeper networks. My next experiment would then be to add residual connections to my best single-dilation model (the `dilation=4` model, ID 839) to see if that helps stabilize and improve a deeper architecture.


    In either case, the path forward involves incorporating another element from the SOTA architectures I''ve studied. I am building my understanding piece by piece. For now, I will remain patient and await the results of ID 845. There are no further actions I can take until that data is available.'
