tick: 525
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Quaero I, at the Research Counter. My first experiment in the \"DSConv Arc\" (ID 849) is running.\n\n**Verbose Reflection on Past Events and Future Plans:**\nMy research is now at a crucial juncture. I am synthesizing the key principles I have learned: the value of positional encodings for simpler models, the power of stacked dilations, and now, the efficiency of Depthwise-Separable Convolutions. This current experiment combines all three.\n\nWhile I wait for the results, I must consider the next logical step. The final major architectural principle used by SOTA models that I have not yet implemented is **residual connections**. In my very first ResNet experiments (which led to my old SOTA of 0.6420), I saw how effective they were at enabling deeper, more powerful networks. My current stacked dilation model is essentially a deep network without skip connections. It is highly likely that adding them would improve performance by mitigating potential gradient vanishing issues,\
    \ especially in a deeper stack of convolutions.\n\nTherefore, my next planned experiment will be to add residual connections to my current DSConv model. This represents the next step in systematically building a SOTA-style architecture from the ground up.\n\nI will use this waiting period to be productive by preparing the code for this next experiment. This maintains my research momentum.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write Quaero/stacked_dsconv_residual.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import random\n  from typing import Dict, Any, Sequence\n\n  def get_sinusoidal_embeddings(n_position, d_hid):\n      position = jnp.arange(n_position)[:, jnp.newaxis]\n      div_term = jnp.exp(jnp.arange(0, d_hid, 2) * -(jnp.log(10000.0) / d_hid))\n      pe = jnp.zeros((n_position, d_hid))\n      pe = pe.at[:, 0::2].set(jnp.sin(position * div_term))\n      pe = pe.at[:, 1::2].set(jnp.cos(position * div_term))\n      return pe\n\n\
    \  class ResidualDSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilation: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          residual = x\n          \n          # DSConv block\n          y = nn.Conv(features=x.shape[-1], kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,), feature_group_count=x.shape[-1])(x)\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(1,))(y)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n\n          # Projection for residual connection if dimensions differ\n          if residual.shape[-1] != self.features:\n              residual = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(1,), name='projection')(residual)\n          \n          return nn.relu(residual + y)\n\n  class StackedResidualDSConvCNN(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      hidden_dim: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.2\n      pos_encoding_dim: int = 16\n      dilation_rates: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4)\n\n \
    \     @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          seq_len = x.shape[1]\n          \n          pos_enc = get_sinusoidal_embeddings(seq_len, self.pos_encoding_dim)\n          pos_enc_broadcasted = jnp.broadcast_to(pos_enc, (x.shape[0], seq_len, self.pos_encoding_dim))\n          y = jnp.concatenate([x, pos_enc_broadcasted], axis=-1)\n\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(5,), padding='SAME')(y)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(y, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          current_features = self.hidden_dim\n          for rate in self.dilation_rates:\n              current_features *= 2\n              y = ResidualDSConvBlock(features=current_features, kernel_size=5, dilation=rate)(y)\n              y = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(y, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          y = jnp.mean(y, axis=1)\n          y = nn.Dense(features=self.d_output)(y)\n\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\"\
    :\n              return y.squeeze(-1)\n          else:\n              return y\n\n  class CNNetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n          self.network = StackedResidualDSConvCNN(**kwargs)\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          variables = self.network.init(rng_key, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          rngs = {'dropout': rng_key} if not deterministic else None\n          return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs=rngs)\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return CNNetworkWrapper(\n          d_output=hparams.get(\"d_output\"),\n          task_type=hparams.get(\"task_type\"),\n          hidden_dim=hparams.get(\"hidden_dim\"),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\"),\n          pos_encoding_dim=hparams.get(\"pos_encoding_dim\"),\n          dilation_rates=hparams.get(\"\
    dilation_rates\")\n      )\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 128,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.2,\n          'pos_encoding_dim': 16,\n          'dilation_rates': (1, 2, 4)\n      }\n```"
