- text: "I am Quaero I, at the Research Counter. My latest experiment, a dropout ablation on my new baseline (ID 859), is running.\n\n**Verbose Reflection on Past Events and Future Plans:**\nI am now in a phase of focused refinement. My token budget has again risen above 70%, which is a concern. However, I have a clear, linear plan that I must see through. The current experiment testing a lower dropout rate is the first step in optimizing my new baseline architecture.\n\nWhile I wait for the results, I must plan for either outcome.\n*   **If the lower dropout rate is successful:** This will become my new, even stronger baseline. My next step would be to ablate another key hyperparameter. The most obvious candidate is the `learning_rate`. The SOTA papers use 0.001, which I have copied, but this is an untested assumption for my specific architecture. I would test a slightly lower learning rate, such as 0.0005, to see if that provides more stable training and a better final score.\n*   **If\
    \ the lower dropout rate is a failure:** This would suggest that my model, despite its complexity, still requires a relatively high degree of regularization. It might also indicate that the `learning_rate` is too high, causing instability that a lower dropout rate can no longer control. In this scenario, my next experiment would also be to test a lower learning rate.\n\nIn either case, the next logical step in my refinement process is to conduct a learning rate ablation. Therefore, I can productively use this waiting period to prepare the code for that experiment. This maintains my momentum and ensures I am ready to act as soon as I have the results from ID 859. My token budget is a pressing concern, so after this next experiment, I will likely need to visit the Token Management Room.\n\nI will prepare the code for the learning rate ablation now.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write Quaero/baseline_lr_ablation.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import\
    \ flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import random\n  import optax\n  from typing import Dict, Any, Sequence\n\n  def get_sinusoidal_embeddings(n_position, d_hid):\n      position = jnp.arange(n_position)[:, jnp.newaxis]\n      div_term = jnp.exp(jnp.arange(0, d_hid, 2) * -(jnp.log(10000.0) / d_hid))\n      pe = jnp.zeros((n_position, d_hid))\n      pe = pe.at[:, 0::2].set(jnp.sin(position * div_term))\n      pe = pe.at[:, 1::2].set(jnp.cos(position * div_term))\n      return pe\n\n  class ResidualDSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilation: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          residual = x\n          \n          y = nn.Conv(features=x.shape[-1], kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,), feature_group_count=x.shape[-1])(x)\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(1,))(y)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n\n          if residual.shape[-1] != self.features:\n           \
    \   residual = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(1,), name='projection')(residual)\n          \n          return nn.relu(residual + y)\n\n  class StackedResidualDSConvCNN(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      hidden_dim: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      pos_encoding_dim: int = 16\n      dilation_rates: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4)\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          seq_len = x.shape[1]\n          \n          pos_enc = get_sinusoidal_embeddings(seq_len, self.pos_encoding_dim)\n          pos_enc_broadcasted = jnp.broadcast_to(pos_enc, (x.shape[0], seq_len, self.pos_encoding_dim))\n          y = jnp.concatenate([x, pos_enc_broadcasted], axis=-1)\n\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(5,), padding='SAME')(y)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(y, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          current_features = self.hidden_dim\n     \
    \     for rate in self.dilation_rates:\n              current_features *= 2\n              y = ResidualDSConvBlock(features=current_features, kernel_size=5, dilation=rate)(y)\n              y = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(y, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          y = jnp.mean(y, axis=1)\n          y = nn.Dense(features=self.d_output)(y)\n\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n              return y.squeeze(-1)\n          else:\n              return y\n\n  class CNNetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n          self.network = StackedResidualDSConvCNN(**kwargs)\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          variables = self.network.init(rng_key, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          rngs = {'dropout': rng_key} if not deterministic else None\n          return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic,\
    \ rngs=rngs)\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return CNNetworkWrapper(\n          d_output=hparams.get(\"d_output\"),\n          task_type=hparams.get(\"task_type\"),\n          hidden_dim=hparams.get(\"hidden_dim\"),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\"),\n          pos_encoding_dim=hparams.get(\"pos_encoding_dim\"),\n          dilation_rates=hparams.get(\"dilation_rates\")\n      )\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.0005, # Changed from 0.001\n          'hidden_dim': 128,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'pos_encoding_dim': 16,\n          'dilation_rates': (1, 2, 4)\n      }\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.0005): # Changed from 0.001\n      total_steps = 50000 \n      warmup_steps = 500\n      \n      schedule = optax.warmup_cosine_decay_schedule(\n          init_value=0.0,\n          peak_value=learning_rate,\n          warmup_steps=warmup_steps,\n          decay_steps=total_steps,\n\
    \          end_value=1e-5\n      )\n      \n      return optax.adamw(learning_rate=schedule, weight_decay=0.01)\n```"
