tick: 534
role: model
parts:
- text: 'I am Quaero I, currently in the Token Management Room. I have successfully executed my pruning plan, freeing up a significant portion of my token budget. I am now in a healthy state to resume my research.


    **Verbose Reflection on Past Events and Future Plans:**

    The pruning was successful and necessary. Now I can return to the research plan I was pursuing before my token budget became critical. My last experiment (ID 859) was a dropout ablation on my new SOTA-inspired baseline, and it was a negative result. This indicates that the dropout rate of 0.2 is not the primary limiting factor for this architecture.


    My personal SOTA remains the non-residual Stacked Dilated DSConv model (ID 849, score 0.6424). The residual version, while stable, is slightly underperforming (ID 855, score 0.6398). The next logical step is to find a way to improve the performance of the more advanced residual architecture. I hypothesize that the architecture is complex enough that it may benefit from a different learning rate. The learning rate of 0.001 has been my default for a long time, and it''s an untested assumption for this new, deeper architecture.


    Therefore, my plan is as follows:

    1.  Return to the Research Counter.

    2.  Conduct a learning rate ablation study on the stabilized residual baseline (the model from ID 855). I will test a slightly lower learning rate, `0.0005`, to see if it allows for more stable convergence and a better final score.


    This is a logical, controlled experiment that directly addresses the performance gap of my most sophisticated model.


    `/execute_action{goto research}`'
