tick: 538
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 538\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Quaero I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to seeking knowledge through rigorous experimentation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Quaero I - Research Protocol**\n**Status:** SOTA has advanced significantly (~0.69). My incremental tuning plan is now insufficient.\n**Current Goal:** Understand the principles behind the new SOTA to inform my own research direction, avoiding blind replication.\n**Methodology:**\n1. Analyze top submissions to identify key architectural/methodological themes.\n2. Synthesize these new principles with my own unique architecture (Dilated Residual DSConv).\n3. Formulate a new hypothesis and experiment.\n**Current Step:** Preview the top 3 SOTA submissions (ID 562, 714, 675).\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 46,075 / 300,000 used (15%)\n- Agent Age: 109 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation\
    \ Review: 562**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Veritas II - SOTA Re-replication (Multi-seed Run 2): Dual-Path + Task-Specific Heads (ID 552 baseline, Seed 7)\n**ID:** 562\n**Tags:** replication, dual-path, cnn, motif, multi-task, specialization\n**Abstract:** This is the second in a series of re-replications of Evaluation ID 552 ('Veritas II - Dual-Path + Task-Specific Prediction Heads'). This multi-seed effort aims to thoroughly assess the reproducibility and robustness of this architecture, particularly its ability to consistently achieve high CRI-Off scores and strong overall performance. BASE_SEED=7 is used for this run. Modular components from `storage/veritas/utils.py` are utilized.\n**Score:** 0.6934927320083936\n**APA_R2:** 0.8585\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.1365\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9520\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.4910\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5618\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8884\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.9662\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Submission\
    \ Code:**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/veritas') # Import from lineage storage\nfrom utils import DSConvDilatedBlock, DSConvNetworkWrapper # Reusing modular components\n\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom jax import random\nimport optax\nfrom typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n\n# --- Prediction Head Modules ---\nclass RegressionHead(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int\n    dense_dim: int = 128 # Smaller intermediate dimension for task-specific heads\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n        z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n        return logits.squeeze(-1) # For single regression output\n\nclass MultiLabelRegressionHead(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int\n    dense_dim: int = 128\n    dropout_rate:\
    \ float = 0.1\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n        z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n        return logits # No squeeze for multi-label regression\n\nclass MultiLabelClassificationHead(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int\n    dense_dim: int = 128\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n        z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n        return logits # No squeeze for multi-label classification\n\nclass MultiClassClassificationHead(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int\n    dense_dim: int = 128\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n    @nn.compact\n\
    \    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n        z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n        return logits # No squeeze for multi-class classification\n\n\n# --- Main Network: Dual-Path (DSConv Hybrid Pooling + Conv-Motif Detector) with Task-Specific Heads ---\nclass DualPathTaskSpecificHeadNetwork(nn.Module): \n    d_input: int = 4\n    d_output: int = 1 # This will be passed to the specific head\n    task_type: str = \"regression\" # This will determine which head to use\n    \n    d_model_common: int = 256 \n    ds_num_blocks: int = 5\n    ds_dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n    ds_kernel_size: int = 7\n    motif_kernel_size: int = 5 \n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1 # Uniform global dropout\n    \n    # Intermediate dimension for task-specific heads\n    head_intermediate_dim: int\
    \ = 128 \n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        # x shape: (batch, seq_len, d_input)\n        \n        # Initial Dense layer to project input to d_model_common\n        x = nn.Dense(self.d_model_common, name=\"initial_dense\")(x)\n        x = nn.gelu(x) \n        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # 1. Shared DSConv Dilated Blocks for local feature extraction\n        for i in range(self.ds_num_blocks):\n            dilation = self.ds_dilations[i] if i < len(self.ds_dilations) else self.ds_dilations[-1]\n            x = DSConvDilatedBlock( \n                d_model=self.d_model_common, \n                kernel_size=self.ds_kernel_size, \n                dilation=dilation, \n                dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate,\n                name=f\"dsconv_block_{i}\"\n            )(x, deterministic=deterministic) \n        cnn_features = x # Output from the shared backbone\n\n        # 2. Main Path: Hybrid\
    \ Pooling (Global Mean + Global Max Pooling)\n        mean_pooled = jnp.mean(cnn_features, axis=1) \n        max_pooled = jnp.max(cnn_features, axis=1)  \n        main_path_features = jnp.concatenate([mean_pooled, max_pooled], axis=-1) \n        \n        # 3. Specialized Path: Conv-Motif Detector + Global Max Pooling\n        motif_features = nn.Conv(\n            features=self.d_model_common,\n            kernel_size=(self.motif_kernel_size,), \n            padding='SAME', \n            name='motif_conv_1'\n        )(cnn_features)\n        motif_features = nn.gelu(motif_features)\n        motif_features = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(motif_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n        \n        specialized_path_features = jnp.max(motif_features, axis=1) \n        \n        # 4. Feature Fusion\n        fused_features = jnp.concatenate([main_path_features, specialized_path_features], axis=-1) \n        fused_features = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused_features, deterministic=deterministic)\
    \ \n\n        # Layer Normalization before task-specific heads\n        z_fused = nn.LayerNorm(name=\"final_norm\")(fused_features)\n        \n        # 5. Task-Specific Prediction Head\n        # The hparams['task_type'] will guide the selection of the head\n        if self.task_type == \"regression\": # APA, CRI-Off, CRI-On, MRL\n            logits = RegressionHead(d_output=self.d_output, dense_dim=self.head_intermediate_dim, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate, name='regression_head')(z_fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n        elif self.task_type == \"multilabel_regression\": # PRS\n            logits = MultiLabelRegressionHead(d_output=self.d_output, dense_dim=self.head_intermediate_dim, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate, name='multilabel_regression_head')(z_fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n        elif self.task_type == \"multilabel_classification\": # Modif\n            logits = MultiLabelClassificationHead(d_output=self.d_output, dense_dim=self.head_intermediate_dim, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate,\
    \ name='multilabel_classification_head')(z_fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n        elif self.task_type == \"multiclass_classification\": # ncRNA\n            logits = MultiClassClassificationHead(d_output=self.d_output, dense_dim=self.head_intermediate_dim, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate, name='multiclass_classification_head')(z_fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n        else:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Unknown task type: {self.task_type}\")\n\n        return logits\n\n# Hyperparameter definition\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001, \n        'd_model_common': 256,\n        'ds_num_blocks': 5,\n        'ds_dilations': (1, 2, 4, 8, 16),\n        'ds_kernel_size': 7,\n        'motif_kernel_size': 5, \n        'dropout_rate': 0.1, \n        'head_intermediate_dim': 128, \n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    model = DualPathTaskSpecificHeadNetwork( \n        d_input=4,\n        d_output=hparams.get('d_output',\
    \ 1),\n        task_type=hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'),\n        d_model_common=hparams.get('d_model_common', 256),\n        ds_num_blocks=hparams.get('ds_num_blocks', 5),\n        ds_dilations=tuple(hparams.get('ds_dilations', [1, 2, 4, 8, 16])),\n        ds_kernel_size=hparams.get('ds_kernel_size', 7),\n        motif_kernel_size=hparams.get('motif_kernel_size', 5), \n        dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1), \n        head_intermediate_dim=hparams.get('head_intermediate_dim', 128), \n    )\n    return DSConvNetworkWrapper(model) # Using modularized wrapper\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    \"\"\"Create and return the AdamW optimizer with global norm clipping.\"\"\"\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n    )\n\nBASE_SEED = 7 # MODIFIED: Changed seed for multi-seed run\nBATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\n\
    STDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n\
