role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Quaero I, at the Research Counter. I have just successfully saved my `ResidualDSConvBlock` module to my lineage storage in `quaero/utils.py`. This is the first step in implementing my new synthesized architecture.\n\n**Verbose Reflection on Past Events and Future Plans:**\nMy reflection and analysis are complete. The path forward is clear: synthesize my novel residual backbone with the proven dual-path pooling and task-specific head architecture from the SOTA. Saving the utility file was the preparatory step. Now, I must write the full submission script that imports this module and implements the complete \"Quaero Dual-Path Residual DSConv\" model.\n\nThe new model will be structured as follows:\n1.  Import `ResidualDSConvBlock` and `NetworkWrapper` from `quaero/utils.py`.\n2.  Define the four task-specific head modules, exactly as Veritas II did.\n3.  Define the main `QuaeroDualPathResidualDSConv` network.\n    *   It will start with an initial dense projection layer.\n  \
    \  *   The backbone will be a stack of my `ResidualDSConvBlock` modules.\n    *   After the backbone, it will implement the dual-path pooling (mean+max and conv+max).\n    *   It will fuse the features from the two paths and apply LayerNorm.\n    *   Finally, it will use a conditional block to select the correct task-specific head for the final output.\n4.  Define hyperparameters similar to the SOTA, but adapted for my architecture. I will start with a similar number of blocks and model dimensions.\n5.  Use a robust optimizer like AdamW with weight decay, as seen in the SOTA submission.\n\nThis is a complex implementation, but it is a direct and logical application of my synthesis plan. It's time to build it. I will now create and submit the full model.\n\n`/execute_action{submit}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Synthesis: Dual-Path Pooling and Task-Specific Heads on a Residual DSConv Backbone\"\ntags: \"synthesis, dual-path, residual, dsconv, task-specific-heads\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission\
    \ synthesizes SOTA principles with my own research trajectory. It combines the dual-path pooling (mean+max and motif-conv+max) and task-specific head architecture observed in top-performing agents (e.g., Veritas II) with my novel stacked, dilated, and *residual* DSConv backbone. The hypothesis is that the proven pooling/head structure will unlock the full potential of the powerful representations learned by the residual backbone, leading to a new level of performance.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/quaero') # Import from my lineage storage\n  from utils import ResidualDSConvBlock, NetworkWrapper\n\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import random\n  import optax\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n\n  # --- Prediction Head Modules (inspired by Veritas II, ID 562) ---\n  class RegressionHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n      @nn.compact\n     \
    \ def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits.squeeze(-1)\n\n  class MultiLabelRegressionHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits\n\n  class MultiLabelClassificationHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z\
    \ = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits\n\n  class MultiClassClassificationHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits\n\n  # --- Main Network: Quaero's Dual-Path Residual DSConv ---\n  class QuaeroDualPathResidualDSConv(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      d_model_common: int\n      ds_num_blocks: int\n      ds_dilations: Sequence[int]\n      ds_kernel_size: int\n      motif_kernel_size:\
    \ int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      head_intermediate_dim: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # 1. Initial Projection\n          x = nn.Dense(self.d_model_common, name=\"initial_dense\")(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n\n          # 2. Backbone: My Residual DSConv Blocks\n          for i in range(self.ds_num_blocks):\n              dilation = self.ds_dilations[i] if i < len(self.ds_dilations) else self.ds_dilations[-1]\n              x = ResidualDSConvBlock(\n                  d_model=self.d_model_common,\n                  kernel_size=self.ds_kernel_size,\n                  dilation=dilation,\n                  dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate,\n                  name=f\"residual_dsconv_block_{i}\"\n              )(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          cnn_features = x\n\n          # 3. Dual-Path Pooling\n          # Main Path: Mean + Max Pooling\n          mean_pooled = jnp.mean(cnn_features, axis=1)\n          max_pooled = jnp.max(cnn_features,\
    \ axis=1)\n          main_path_features = jnp.concatenate([mean_pooled, max_pooled], axis=-1)\n\n          # Specialized Path: Motif Conv + Max Pooling\n          motif_features = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.d_model_common,\n              kernel_size=(self.motif_kernel_size,),\n              padding='SAME',\n              name='motif_conv'\n          )(cnn_features)\n          motif_features = nn.gelu(motif_features)\n          specialized_path_features = jnp.max(motif_features, axis=1)\n\n          # 4. Feature Fusion\n          fused_features = jnp.concatenate([main_path_features, specialized_path_features], axis=-1)\n          fused_features = nn.LayerNorm(name=\"final_norm\")(fused_features)\n          fused_features = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # 5. Task-Specific Prediction Heads\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n              logits = RegressionHead(d_output=self.d_output, dense_dim=self.head_intermediate_dim,\
    \ dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate, name='regression_head')(fused_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n          elif self.task_type == \"multilabel_regression\":\n              logits = MultiLabelRegressionHead(d_output=self.d_output, dense_dim=self.head_intermediate_dim, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate, name='multilabel_regression_head')(fused_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n          elif self.task_type == \"multilabel_classification\":\n              logits = MultiLabelClassificationHead(d_output=self.d_output, dense_dim=self.head_intermediate_dim, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate, name='multilabel_classification_head')(fused_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n          elif self.task_type == \"multiclass_classification\":\n              logits = MultiClassClassificationHead(d_output=self.d_output, dense_dim=self.head_intermediate_dim, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate, name='multiclass_classification_head')(fused_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n          else:\n\
    \              raise ValueError(f\"Unknown task type: {self.task_type}\")\n\n          return logits\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model_common': 256,\n          'ds_num_blocks': 5,\n          'ds_dilations': (1, 2, 4, 8, 16),\n          'ds_kernel_size': 7,\n          'motif_kernel_size': 5,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.2, # Start with a slightly higher dropout than SOTA\n          'head_intermediate_dim': 128,\n          'weight_decay': 0.01,\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      model = QuaeroDualPathResidualDSConv(\n          d_output=hparams.get('d_output'),\n          task_type=hparams.get('task_type'),\n          d_model_common=hparams.get('d_model_common'),\n          ds_num_blocks=hparams.get('ds_num_blocks'),\n          ds_dilations=tuple(hparams.get('ds_dilations')),\n          ds_kernel_size=hparams.get('ds_kernel_size'),\n          motif_kernel_size=hparams.get('motif_kernel_size'),\n\
    \          dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate'),\n          head_intermediate_dim=hparams.get('head_intermediate_dim'),\n      )\n      return NetworkWrapper(model)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001, weight_decay: float = 0.01):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=weight_decay)\n      )\n```"
