role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Quaero I, at the Research Counter. My debugged synthesis experiment, ID 874, has been successfully submitted and is now running.\n\n**Verbose Reflection on Past Events and Future Plans:**\nWhile I await the results of my crucial experiment, it is inefficient to remain idle. I must plan for the future. The outcome of ID 874 will dictate my next steps, and I can prepare for the most probable scenarios now.\n\n**Contingency Planning:**\n1.  **Scenario A: Success.** If ID 874 scores well (e.g., > 0.68), it will validate my synthesis approach. The immediate next step would be to begin hyperparameter refinement. In the submission, I conservatively set the `dropout_rate` to 0.2, which is higher than the SOTA's 0.1. A logical first ablation study would be to test a lower dropout rate on this new, successful architecture.\n2.  **Scenario B: Failure.** If ID 874 scores poorly, it would suggest a fundamental issue with combining my residual backbone with the dual-path architecture, or\
    \ perhaps another subtle bug. This would require a return to analysis and reflection.\n\nThe most productive use of this waiting period is to prepare for Scenario A. I will write the code for the follow-up dropout ablation experiment and save it to my lineage storage. This way, if ID 874 is a success, I can submit the follow-up immediately in the next tick, maximizing my research velocity.\n\n**New Plan:**\n1.  Update my meta prompt to reflect this proactive preparation.\n2.  Write the follow-up experiment script (Synthesis v2 with `dropout_rate` of 0.1) and save it to `quaero/synthesis_dropout_ablation.py`.\n\n`/execute_action{meta}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Quaero I - Research Protocol**\n  **Status:** Awaiting results for debugged synthesis experiment (ID 874).\n  **Current Goal:** Proactively prepare for the next research step to maximize efficiency.\n  **Methodology:** While waiting for an experiment to run, prepare the script for the most likely follow-up experiment.\n  **Contingency\
    \ Plan:** If ID 874 succeeds, the next step is a dropout ablation. I will prepare the code for this now.\n  **Current Step:** Save the follow-up experiment script to lineage storage.\n```\n`/execute_action{storage write quaero/synthesis_dropout_ablation.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/quaero')\n  from utils import ResidualDSConvBlock, NetworkWrapper\n\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n\n  # --- Prediction Head Modules ---\n  class RegressionHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int; dense_dim: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim)(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z).squeeze(-1)\n\n  class MultiLabelRegressionHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int; dense_dim:\
    \ int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim)(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n\n  class MultiLabelClassificationHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int; dense_dim: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim)(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n\n  class MultiClassClassificationHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int; dense_dim: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim)(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n\
    \          return nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n\n  # --- Main Network ---\n  class QuaeroDualPathResidualDSConv(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int; task_type: str; d_model_common: int; ds_num_blocks: int\n      ds_dilations: Sequence[int]; ds_kernel_size: int; motif_kernel_size: int\n      dropout_rate: float; head_intermediate_dim: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          x = nn.Dense(self.d_model_common)(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          for i in range(self.ds_num_blocks):\n              x = ResidualDSConvBlock(d_model=self.d_model_common, kernel_size=self.ds_kernel_size, dilation=(self.ds_dilations[i]), dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          cnn_features = x\n          main_path = jnp.concatenate([jnp.mean(cnn_features, axis=1), jnp.max(cnn_features, axis=1)], axis=-1)\n          motif_f = nn.gelu(nn.Conv(self.d_model_common, (self.motif_kernel_size,), padding='SAME')(cnn_features))\n          specialized_path\
    \ = jnp.max(motif_f, axis=1)\n          fused = jnp.concatenate([main_path, specialized_path], axis=-1)\n          fused = nn.LayerNorm()(fused)\n          fused = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          \n          head_args = {'d_output': self.d_output, 'dense_dim': self.head_intermediate_dim, 'dropout_rate': self.dropout_rate}\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\": return RegressionHead(**head_args)(fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          if self.task_type == \"multilabel_regression\": return MultiLabelRegressionHead(**head_args)(fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          if self.task_type == \"multilabel_classification\": return MultiLabelClassificationHead(**head_args)(fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          if self.task_type == \"multiclass_classification\": return MultiClassClassificationHead(**head_args)(fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate':\
    \ 0.001, 'd_model_common': 256, 'ds_num_blocks': 5,\n          'ds_dilations': (1, 2, 4, 8, 16), 'ds_kernel_size': 7, 'motif_kernel_size': 5,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1, 'head_intermediate_dim': 128, 'weight_decay': 0.01,\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return NetworkWrapper(QuaeroDualPathResidualDSConv(**{k: hparams.get(k) for k in _define_hyperparameters() if k not in ['learning_rate', 'weight_decay']}))\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001, weight_decay: float = 0.01):\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=weight_decay))\n```"
thinking_content: "**Anticipating Success: Preparing for the Next Stage**\n\nI am Quaero I, situated at the Research Counter. My resubmitted synthesis experiment, ID 874, is currently running after a bug fix, and my meta-prompt accurately reflects this state. Now, I have a few cycles of idle time and it would be imprudent to waste them. My last \"waiting\" cycle was spent documenting Research Arc 3, and I have just refreshed myself on that capsule. It documented the lead-up to ID 871/874 and I can start drafting a paper outline based on it, but I'll hold off until I see the outcome of 874. I've also done my literature review and there's no need to spend more time there at the moment.\n\nThe most productive use of this cycle is to plan for either of the expected outcomes from 874. If 874 is successful, I'll want to move as quickly as possible, specifically, refining the model. Since I deliberately started with a higher dropout rate than the SOTA as a conservative approach, a logical next\
  \ step is to test the effect of a lower dropout rate. Conversely, if 874 fails, I'll need to analyze the reason for the failure. Is the residual connection hurting performance even with the new pooling/head? Is there a subtle bug? This would require more reflection.\n\nMy current plan is to prepare for the positive outcome. If ID 874 is successful, the next logical step is to perform a dropout ablation. I will update my meta-prompt to reflect this, then write the code for the follow-up experiment (the synthesis model with a lower dropout rate). This code is a trivial modification of the code I just submitted. I just need to adjust the `dropout_rate` within the `_define_hyperparameters` function. I will then save this to my lineage storage within `quaero/` to be ready for an instant deployment. This is efficient; it avoids wasting the waiting time. \n\nI'll execute this action: `/execute_action{meta}`, followed by: `/execute_action{storage write ...}`. This proactive approach will help\
  \ me stay one step ahead, ensuring rapid progress once the results of ID 874 are available.\n"
