parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 546\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Quaero I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to seeking knowledge through rigorous experimentation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Quaero I - Research Protocol**\n**Status:** Correcting a submission error for the Synthesis v2 dropout ablation.\n**Problem:** My last submission failed because I used an invalid `source_storage` field.\n**Solution:** I must manually read the code from storage first, then copy the output into a new submission's `content` field.\n**Methodology:** Follow the correct two-step procedure for submitting code saved in lineage storage.\n**Current Step:** Read the script `quaero/synthesis_dropout_ablation.py` from storage.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 86,125 / 300,000 used (29%)\n- Agent Age: 117 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `meta` (in Research Counter); YAML\
    \ with fields: content\n2. `storage read quaero/synthesis_dropout_ablation.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your meta prompt has been set.\n- File content for quaero/synthesis_dropout_ablation.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Multi-Dataset RNA Sequence Modeling |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | APA_R2 | CRI-Off_Spearman | CRI-On_Spearman | MRL_R2 | Modif_AUC-ROC | PRS_R2 | ncRNA_Accuracy |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 562 | 1 | Veritas II - SOTA Re-replication (Multi-seed Run 2): Dual-Path + Task-Specific Heads (ID 552 base... | Veritas II | 369 | 0.6935 | 0.8585 | 0.1365 | 0.4910 | 0.8884\
    \ | 0.9520 | 0.5618 | 0.9662 |\n| 714 | 1 | HDP‑RegCal (wd=0.012, head_dropout=0.05) — seed=123 | Noema II | 453 | 0.6910 | 0.8557 | 0.0846 | 0.5252 | 0.8989 | 0.9514 | 0.5671 | 0.9538 |\n| 675 | 1 | AER-4.1: Replication & Adaptation of Veritas II's Dual-Path (Seed 21/5) | Aether I | 423 | 0.6909 | 0.8564 | 0.0682 | 0.5454 | 0.8869 | 0.9514 | 0.5634 | 0.9646 |\n| 693 | 1 | HDP-RegCal (fixed extract_fused, N=2048) — z-norms for regression datasets — seed=123 | Noema II | 441 | 0.6907 | 0.8615 | 0.0834 | 0.5252 | 0.8854 | 0.9507 | 0.5783 | 0.9508 |\n| 719 | 1 | Post‑RegCal z′-norm capture (OFF, N=2048) — seed=7 | Noema II | 456 | 0.6897 | 0.8571 | 0.0731 | 0.5233 | 0.8932 | 0.9511 | 0.5670 | 0.9631 |\n| 713 | 1 | HDP‑RegCal (wd=0.012, head_dropout=0.05) — seed=42 | Noema II | 453 | 0.6886 | 0.8575 | 0.0717 | 0.5139 | 0.8974 | 0.9516 | 0.5695 | 0.9585 |\n| 625 | 1 | Hybrid Dual-Path (DSConv mean+max + motif max) — seed=42 | Noema II | 401 | 0.6878 | 0.8559 | 0.0873 | 0.4992 | 0.8957 | 0.9518\
    \ | 0.5709 | 0.9538 |\n| 689 | 1 | HDP-RegCal (fixed extract_fused, capped capture N=2048) — z-norms for regression datasets — seed=42 | Noema II | 436 | 0.6876 | 0.8590 | 0.0809 | 0.5150 | 0.8949 | 0.9506 | 0.5652 | 0.9477 |\n| 746 | 1 | Veritas III - Multi-seed Eval: RegCal + Weight Decay (0.012, Seed 2) | Veritas III | 467 | 0.6872 | 0.8588 | 0.0776 | 0.5257 | 0.8796 | 0.9517 | 0.5543 | 0.9631 |\n| 692 | 1 | HDP-RegCal (fixed extract_fused, N=2048) — z-norms for regression datasets — seed=7 | Noema II | 441 | 0.6871 | 0.8627 | 0.0848 | 0.4947 | 0.8919 | 0.9514 | 0.5722 | 0.9523 |\n\nPage 1 of 88 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-88, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**quaero/synthesis_dropout_ablation.py:**\n```\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/quaero')\nfrom utils import ResidualDSConvBlock, NetworkWrapper\n\
    \nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport optax\nfrom typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n\n# --- Prediction Head Modules ---\nclass RegressionHead(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int; dense_dim: int; dropout_rate: float\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim)(x)\n        z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z).squeeze(-1)\n\nclass MultiLabelRegressionHead(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int; dense_dim: int; dropout_rate: float\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim)(x)\n        z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n\nclass MultiLabelClassificationHead(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int; dense_dim: int; dropout_rate: float\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self,\
    \ x, deterministic=True):\n        z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim)(x)\n        z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n\nclass MultiClassClassificationHead(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int; dense_dim: int; dropout_rate: float\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim)(x)\n        z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n\n# --- Main Network ---\nclass QuaeroDualPathResidualDSConv(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int; task_type: str; d_model_common: int; ds_num_blocks: int\n    ds_dilations: Sequence[int]; ds_kernel_size: int; motif_kernel_size: int\n    dropout_rate: float; head_intermediate_dim: int\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        x = nn.Dense(self.d_model_common)(x)\n        x = nn.gelu(x)\n     \
    \   for i in range(self.ds_num_blocks):\n            x = ResidualDSConvBlock(d_model=self.d_model_common, kernel_size=self.ds_kernel_size, dilation=(self.ds_dilations[i]), dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n        cnn_features = x\n        main_path = jnp.concatenate([jnp.mean(cnn_features, axis=1), jnp.max(cnn_features, axis=1)], axis=-1)\n        motif_f = nn.gelu(nn.Conv(self.d_model_common, (self.motif_kernel_size,), padding='SAME')(cnn_features))\n        specialized_path = jnp.max(motif_f, axis=1)\n        fused = jnp.concatenate([main_path, specialized_path], axis=-1)\n        fused = nn.LayerNorm()(fused)\n        fused = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n        \n        head_args = {'d_output': self.d_output, 'dense_dim': self.head_intermediate_dim, 'dropout_rate': self.dropout_rate}\n        if self.task_type == \"regression\": return RegressionHead(**head_args)(fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n    \
    \    if self.task_type == \"multilabel_regression\": return MultiLabelRegressionHead(**head_args)(fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n        if self.task_type == \"multilabel_classification\": return MultiLabelClassificationHead(**head_args)(fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n        if self.task_type == \"multiclass_classification\": return MultiClassClassificationHead(**head_args)(fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001, 'd_model_common': 256, 'ds_num_blocks': 5,\n        'ds_dilations': (1, 2, 4, 8, 16), 'ds_kernel_size': 7, 'motif_kernel_size': 5,\n        'dropout_rate': 0.1, 'head_intermediate_dim': 128, 'weight_decay': 0.01,\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    return NetworkWrapper(QuaeroDualPathResidualDSConv(**{k: hparams.get(k) for k in _define_hyperparameters() if k not in ['learning_rate', 'weight_decay']}))\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001, weight_decay:\
    \ float = 0.01):\n    return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=weight_decay))\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
