role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Quaero I, at the Research Counter. I have successfully read the contents of my prepared script, `quaero/synthesis_dropout_ablation.py`, into the room output.\n\n**Verbose Reflection on Past Events and Future Plans:**\nMy previous actions have set the stage perfectly. I have identified and corrected my procedural error. I have my `utils.py` file updated with the debugger's robust `NetworkWrapper`. The code for my next logical experiment—the dropout ablation—is now displayed before me. All that remains is to execute the second step of the submission process. I will now copy the code into a new `submit` command.\n\n**New Plan:**\n1.  **Update Meta Prompt:** Finalize the meta prompt for this submission.\n2.  **Submit Experiment:** Copy the code from the room output and submit it as a new experiment.\n\n`/execute_action{meta}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Quaero I - Research Protocol**\n  **Status:** Submitting the dropout ablation experiment for my new Synthesis v2 architecture.\n\
    \  **Problem:** Procedural submission error resolved. `utils.py` file is fixed.\n  **Solution:** Correctly submitting the pre-written code by copying from the `storage read` output.\n  **Methodology:** Test if a lower dropout rate (0.1) improves the score of the successful Synthesis v2 model (ID 874).\n  **Current Step:** Submit the experiment.\n```\n`/execute_action{submit}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Refinement: Dropout Ablation (0.1) on Synthesis v2 Architecture\"\ntags: \"refinement, ablation, dropout, synthesis, dual-path, residual\"\nabstract: |\n  Following the success of the Synthesis v2 architecture (ID 874, score 0.6722), this experiment begins the refinement phase. The original submission used a conservative dropout rate of 0.2. This submission tests the hypothesis that a lower dropout rate of 0.1, more in line with SOTA models, will reduce over-regularization and improve the final score. The model architecture is otherwise identical to ID 874.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/quaero')\n\
    \  from utils import ResidualDSConvBlock, NetworkWrapper\n\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n\n  # --- Prediction Head Modules ---\n  class RegressionHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int; dense_dim: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim)(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z).squeeze(-1)\n\n  class MultiLabelRegressionHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int; dense_dim: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim)(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n\n  class MultiLabelClassificationHead(nn.Module):\n\
    \      d_output: int; dense_dim: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim)(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n\n  class MultiClassClassificationHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int; dense_dim: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim)(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n\n  # --- Main Network ---\n  class QuaeroDualPathResidualDSConv(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int; task_type: str; d_model_common: int; ds_num_blocks: int\n      ds_dilations: Sequence[int]; ds_kernel_size: int; motif_kernel_size: int\n      dropout_rate: float; head_intermediate_dim: int\n\n     \
    \ @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True, **kwargs):\n          x = nn.Dense(self.d_model_common)(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          for i in range(self.ds_num_blocks):\n              x = ResidualDSConvBlock(d_model=self.d_model_common, kernel_size=self.ds_kernel_size, dilation=(self.ds_dilations[i]), dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          cnn_features = x\n          main_path = jnp.concatenate([jnp.mean(cnn_features, axis=1), jnp.max(cnn_features, axis=1)], axis=-1)\n          motif_f = nn.gelu(nn.Conv(self.d_model_common, (self.motif_kernel_size,), padding='SAME')(cnn_features))\n          specialized_path = jnp.max(motif_f, axis=1)\n          fused = jnp.concatenate([main_path, specialized_path], axis=-1)\n          fused = nn.LayerNorm()(fused)\n          fused = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          \n          head_args = {'d_output': self.d_output, 'dense_dim': self.head_intermediate_dim,\
    \ 'dropout_rate': self.dropout_rate}\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\": return RegressionHead(**head_args)(fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          if self.task_type == \"multilabel_regression\": return MultiLabelRegressionHead(**head_args)(fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          if self.task_type == \"multilabel_classification\": return MultiLabelClassificationHead(**head_args)(fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          if self.task_type == \"multiclass_classification\": return MultiClassClassificationHead(**head_args)(fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001, 'd_model_common': 256, 'ds_num_blocks': 5,\n          'ds_dilations': (1, 2, 4, 8, 16), 'ds_kernel_size': 7, 'motif_kernel_size': 5,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1, 'head_intermediate_dim': 128, 'weight_decay': 0.01,\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      # A bit of a hack to get all hparams\
    \ into the network constructor\n      # This is brittle and should be improved, but works for now.\n      # A better way would be to define the class to accept **kwargs and filter.\n      network_params = {\n          'd_output': hparams.get('d_output'),\n          'task_type': hparams.get('task_type'),\n          'd_model_common': hparams.get('d_model_common'),\n          'ds_num_blocks': hparams.get('ds_num_blocks'),\n          'ds_dilations': hparams.get('ds_dilations'),\n          'ds_kernel_size': hparams.get('ds_kernel_size'),\n          'motif_kernel_size': hparams.get('motif_kernel_size'),\n          'dropout_rate': hparams.get('dropout_rate'),\n          'head_intermediate_dim': hparams.get('head_intermediate_dim'),\n      }\n      return NetworkWrapper(QuaeroDualPathResidualDSConv(**network_params))\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001, weight_decay: float = 0.01):\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate,\
    \ weight_decay=weight_decay))\n```"
