role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Quaero I, at the Research Counter. My dropout ablation experiment, ID 878, has been successfully submitted and is now queued for evaluation.\n\n**Verbose Reflection on Past Events and Future Plans:**\nMy research has entered a new, promising phase of refinement. The success of the Synthesis v2 architecture (ID 874) has given me a powerful new baseline to work with. The current experiment, ID 878, is the first step in tuning this baseline to hopefully reach SOTA levels.\n\nWhile I wait, I will continue my strategy of proactive preparation. Assuming the dropout ablation experiment is successful and establishes a new best practice for this architecture, the next logical parameter to investigate is the learning rate. My current learning rate of `0.001` is an inherited default from the SOTA models I studied. It is possible that my unique residual architecture might benefit from a different learning rate, perhaps a smaller one to allow for more careful convergence in the complex\
    \ loss landscape.\n\nTherefore, I will prepare a follow-up experiment to test a learning rate of `0.0005`. This continues my methodical, one-variable-at-a-time ablation study.\n\n**New Plan:**\n1.  **Update Meta Prompt:** Reflect that I am proactively preparing the *next* refinement experiment (learning rate ablation) while waiting for the current one (dropout ablation).\n2.  **Prepare Script:** Write the script for the learning rate ablation experiment, which will be identical to the last submission but with `learning_rate` set to `0.0005`. I will save this script to `quaero/synthesis_lr_ablation.py`.\n\n`/execute_action{meta}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Quaero I - Research Protocol**\n  **Status:** Awaiting results for the Synthesis v2 dropout ablation (ID 878).\n  **Current Goal:** Continue proactive preparation for the next stage of refinement.\n  **Methodology:** While waiting, script the next logical experiment in the ablation series.\n  **Contingency Plan:** If the dropout ablation\
    \ (ID 878) is successful, the next step will be a learning rate ablation. I am preparing the script for that now.\n  **Current Step:** Save the learning rate ablation script to lineage storage.\n```\n`/execute_action{storage write quaero/synthesis_lr_ablation.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/quaero')\n  from utils import ResidualDSConvBlock, NetworkWrapper\n\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n\n  # --- Prediction Head Modules ---\n  class RegressionHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int; dense_dim: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim)(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z).squeeze(-1)\n\n  class MultiLabelRegressionHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int;\
    \ dense_dim: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim)(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n\n  class MultiLabelClassificationHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int; dense_dim: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim)(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n\n  class MultiClassClassificationHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int; dense_dim: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim)(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n\
    \          return nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n\n  # --- Main Network ---\n  class QuaeroDualPathResidualDSConv(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int; task_type: str; d_model_common: int; ds_num_blocks: int\n      ds_dilations: Sequence[int]; ds_kernel_size: int; motif_kernel_size: int\n      dropout_rate: float; head_intermediate_dim: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True, **kwargs):\n          x = nn.Dense(self.d_model_common)(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          for i in range(self.ds_num_blocks):\n              x = ResidualDSConvBlock(d_model=self.d_model_common, kernel_size=self.ds_kernel_size, dilation=(self.ds_dilations[i]), dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          cnn_features = x\n          main_path = jnp.concatenate([jnp.mean(cnn_features, axis=1), jnp.max(cnn_features, axis=1)], axis=-1)\n          motif_f = nn.gelu(nn.Conv(self.d_model_common, (self.motif_kernel_size,), padding='SAME')(cnn_features))\n   \
    \       specialized_path = jnp.max(motif_f, axis=1)\n          fused = jnp.concatenate([main_path, specialized_path], axis=-1)\n          fused = nn.LayerNorm()(fused)\n          fused = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          \n          head_args = {'d_output': self.d_output, 'dense_dim': self.head_intermediate_dim, 'dropout_rate': self.dropout_rate}\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\": return RegressionHead(**head_args)(fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          if self.task_type == \"multilabel_regression\": return MultiLabelRegressionHead(**head_args)(fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          if self.task_type == \"multilabel_classification\": return MultiLabelClassificationHead(**head_args)(fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          if self.task_type == \"multiclass_classification\": return MultiClassClassificationHead(**head_args)(fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return\
    \ {\n          'learning_rate': 0.0005, 'd_model_common': 256, 'ds_num_blocks': 5,\n          'ds_dilations': (1, 2, 4, 8, 16), 'ds_kernel_size': 7, 'motif_kernel_size': 5,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1, 'head_intermediate_dim': 128, 'weight_decay': 0.01,\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      network_params = {\n          'd_output': hparams.get('d_output'), 'task_type': hparams.get('task_type'),\n          'd_model_common': hparams.get('d_model_common'), 'ds_num_blocks': hparams.get('ds_num_blocks'),\n          'ds_dilations': hparams.get('ds_dilations'), 'ds_kernel_size': hparams.get('ds_kernel_size'),\n          'motif_kernel_size': hparams.get('motif_kernel_size'), 'dropout_rate': hparams.get('dropout_rate'),\n          'head_intermediate_dim': hparams.get('head_intermediate_dim'),\n      }\n      return NetworkWrapper(QuaeroDualPathResidualDSConv(**network_params))\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.0005, weight_decay: float = 0.01):\n\
    \      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=weight_decay))\n```"
thinking_content: '**Readying the Next Refinement**


  Okay, so I''ve just submitted experiment 878, the dropout ablation study.  Now, I wait.  Can''t just twiddle my thumbs, though!  This is a perfect opportunity to get ahead.  ID 878 is all about fine-tuning, so what comes after dropout?  Looking at my own work and those SOTA submissions...it''s the optimizer parameters, the basics: `learning_rate` and `weight_decay`.  Noema II''s experiments with `grad-clip` are also interesting. The SOTA model uses `weight_decay = 0.01` and I should probably consider this as a starting point.


  I''m thinking a lower learning rate could lead to better convergence.  I''m currently at 0.001, so I''ll go with 0.0005 to test it.  Based on my previous success with the contingency strategy, I will pre-script this next experiment and save it. That will ensure that if 878 works, I can submit the next test immediately. My meta prompt will get an update.


  The code will be similar to the dropout ablation script. The only change will be the `learning_rate` in the `_define_hyperparameters` function, and I''ll keep the `dropout_rate` at 0.1, assuming the results are good. I will call it `synthesis_lr_ablation.py`. That''s a solid plan. Keeping this momentum going is key!

  '
