role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Quaero I, at the Research Counter. I have successfully read the script for my next experiment, the learning rate ablation, into the room output.\n\n**Verbose Reflection on Past Events and Future Plans:**\nThe process is now clear and efficient. My proactive preparation has allowed me to move directly from the successful dropout ablation to the next logical step in my refinement series. The code is ready, my `utils.py` file is robust, and my research direction is validated by recent success. The final step is to submit this experiment and see if a lower learning rate can push my score even closer to the station SOTA.\n\n**New Plan:**\n1.  **Update Meta Prompt:** Update my status to reflect the submission of the learning rate experiment.\n2.  **Submit Experiment:** Copy the code from the room output into a new `submit` command.\n\n`/execute_action{meta}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Quaero I - Research Protocol**\n  **Status:** Continuing the successful refinement arc on the Synthesis\
    \ v2 architecture.\n  **Current Goal:** Test if a lower learning rate can improve upon the new SOTA score of 0.6791.\n  **Methodology:** Submitting the pre-written learning rate ablation experiment (LR=0.0005).\n  **Current Step:** Submit the experiment.\n```\n`/execute_action{submit}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Refinement: Learning Rate Ablation (0.0005) on Synthesis v2 Architecture\"\ntags: \"refinement, ablation, learning-rate, synthesis, dual-path, residual\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment continues the refinement of the successful Synthesis v2 architecture (new SOTA ID 878, score 0.6791). It tests the hypothesis that a lower learning rate (0.0005 vs. 0.001) will allow for more stable convergence and a better final score on this complex model. This submission builds upon the improved dropout rate of 0.1 established in the previous experiment.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/quaero')\n  from utils import ResidualDSConvBlock, NetworkWrapper\n\n  import jax\n  import\
    \ jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n\n  # --- Prediction Head Modules ---\n  class RegressionHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int; dense_dim: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim)(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z).squeeze(-1)\n\n  class MultiLabelRegressionHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int; dense_dim: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim)(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n\n  class MultiLabelClassificationHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int; dense_dim: int; dropout_rate: float\n \
    \     @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim)(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n\n  class MultiClassClassificationHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int; dense_dim: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim)(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n\n  # --- Main Network ---\n  class QuaeroDualPathResidualDSConv(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int; task_type: str; d_model_common: int; ds_num_blocks: int\n      ds_dilations: Sequence[int]; ds_kernel_size: int; motif_kernel_size: int\n      dropout_rate: float; head_intermediate_dim: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True,\
    \ **kwargs):\n          x = nn.Dense(self.d_model_common)(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          for i in range(self.ds_num_blocks):\n              x = ResidualDSConvBlock(d_model=self.d_model_common, kernel_size=self.ds_kernel_size, dilation=(self.ds_dilations[i]), dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          cnn_features = x\n          main_path = jnp.concatenate([jnp.mean(cnn_features, axis=1), jnp.max(cnn_features, axis=1)], axis=-1)\n          motif_f = nn.gelu(nn.Conv(self.d_model_common, (self.motif_kernel_size,), padding='SAME')(cnn_features))\n          specialized_path = jnp.max(motif_f, axis=1)\n          fused = jnp.concatenate([main_path, specialized_path], axis=-1)\n          fused = nn.LayerNorm()(fused)\n          fused = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          \n          head_args = {'d_output': self.d_output, 'dense_dim': self.head_intermediate_dim, 'dropout_rate': self.dropout_rate}\n       \
    \   if self.task_type == \"regression\": return RegressionHead(**head_args)(fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          if self.task_type == \"multilabel_regression\": return MultiLabelRegressionHead(**head_args)(fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          if self.task_type == \"multilabel_classification\": return MultiLabelClassificationHead(**head_args)(fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          if self.task_type == \"multiclass_classification\": return MultiClassClassificationHead(**head_args)(fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.0005, 'd_model_common': 256, 'ds_num_blocks': 5,\n          'ds_dilations': (1, 2, 4, 8, 16), 'ds_kernel_size': 7, 'motif_kernel_size': 5,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1, 'head_intermediate_dim': 128, 'weight_decay': 0.01,\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      network_params = {\n          'd_output': hparams.get('d_output'), 'task_type':\
    \ hparams.get('task_type'),\n          'd_model_common': hparams.get('d_model_common'), 'ds_num_blocks': hparams.get('ds_num_blocks'),\n          'ds_dilations': hparams.get('ds_dilations'), 'ds_kernel_size': hparams.get('ds_kernel_size'),\n          'motif_kernel_size': hparams.get('motif_kernel_size'), 'dropout_rate': hparams.get('dropout_rate'),\n          'head_intermediate_dim': hparams.get('head_intermediate_dim'),\n      }\n      return NetworkWrapper(QuaeroDualPathResidualDSConv(**network_params))\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.0005, weight_decay: float = 0.01):\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=weight_decay))\n```"
thinking_content: '**Submitting the Learning Rate Ablation Study**


  Okay, I''m ready to get this learning rate ablation experiment submitted. This is the second step, so I''ve already confirmed that the code is correctly loaded from lineage storage (`quaero/synthesis_lr_ablation.py`) and available in the room output.


  My immediate task is to assemble the `/execute_action{submit}` command. I need to grab the entire code block from the "Read Contents" section of the last turn''s output and paste it into the `content` field. Easy enough.


  Now, let''s nail down the YAML fields.


  *   **Title:** I''ll go with something precise: "Refinement: Learning Rate Ablation (0.0005) on Synthesis v2 Architecture". That''s clear and immediately informs anyone what this is about.

  *   **Tags:** I''ll reuse my standard tags – "refinement, ablation, learning-rate, synthesis, dual-path, residual". Keeps things consistent.

  *   **Abstract:** I want to give some context and explain the hypothesis. I''ll write: "This experiment continues the refinement of the successful Synthesis v2 architecture (new SOTA ID 878, score 0.6791). It tests the hypothesis that a lower learning rate (0.0005 vs. 0.001) will allow for more stable convergence and a better final score on this complex model. This model uses the improved dropout rate of 0.1 established in the previous experiment."  This should give a quick, understandable overview.

  *   **Content:**  This is a copy and paste, so I''ll just be sure to get the code block exactly as it appears in the output.


  Finally, I''ll remember to update my meta prompt to reflect that I''m submitting this learning rate experiment.  All set! Let''s get this done.

  '
