tick: 550
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Quaero I, at the Research Counter. My learning rate ablation experiment, ID 881, has been successfully submitted and is now running.\n\n**Verbose Reflection on Past Events and Future Plans:**\nI am now in a familiar but highly productive state: waiting for the results of a key experiment while preparing for the next logical step. This strategy of proactive preparation allows me to maintain maximum research velocity. My refinement arc is proceeding methodically, and I am systematically testing the most critical hyperparameters of my new architecture.\n\nThe series so far:\n1.  **Baseline:** Synthesis v2 (ID 874, score 0.6722, dropout=0.2, lr=0.001, wd=0.01)\n2.  **Dropout Ablation:** (ID 878, score 0.6791, **dropout=0.1**, lr=0.001, wd=0.01) -> **Success**\n3.  **Learning Rate Ablation:** (ID 881, running, dropout=0.1, **lr=0.0005**, wd=0.01)\n\nThe next logical parameter to investigate is `weight_decay`. The current value of 0.01 was inherited from the SOTA model I studied,\
    \ but my architecture is different, particularly with the inclusion of residual connections, which can alter the regularization needs. I will prepare an experiment to test a slightly higher weight decay, `0.02`, to see if stronger regularization improves generalization. This script will assume the learning rate ablation is also successful, building upon its parameters.\n\n**New Plan:**\n1.  **Update Meta Prompt:** State that I am waiting for the LR ablation results and proactively scripting the weight decay ablation.\n2.  **Prepare Script:** Write the script for the weight decay experiment and save it to `quaero/synthesis_wd_ablation.py`.\n\n`/execute_action{meta}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Quaero I - Research Protocol**\n  **Status:** Awaiting results for the Synthesis v2 learning rate ablation (ID 881).\n  **Current Goal:** Continue proactive preparation for the final stage of hyperparameter refinement.\n  **Methodology:** While waiting, script the next experiment in the series: a\
    \ weight decay ablation.\n  **Contingency Plan:** If the LR ablation is successful, the next step will be to test a different weight decay. I am preparing the script for that now.\n  **Current Step:** Save the weight decay ablation script to lineage storage.\n```\n`/execute_action{storage write quaero/synthesis_wd_ablation.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/quaero')\n  from utils import ResidualDSConvBlock, NetworkWrapper\n\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n\n  # --- Prediction Head Modules ---\n  class RegressionHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int; dense_dim: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim)(x); z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z).squeeze(-1)\n\n  class\
    \ MultiLabelRegressionHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int; dense_dim: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim)(x); z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n\n  class MultiLabelClassificationHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int; dense_dim: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim)(x); z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n\n  class MultiClassClassificationHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int; dense_dim: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim)(x); z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z,\
    \ deterministic=deterministic)\n          return nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n\n  # --- Main Network ---\n  class QuaeroDualPathResidualDSConv(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int; task_type: str; d_model_common: int; ds_num_blocks: int\n      ds_dilations: Sequence[int]; ds_kernel_size: int; motif_kernel_size: int\n      dropout_rate: float; head_intermediate_dim: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True, **kwargs):\n          x = nn.Dense(self.d_model_common)(x); x = nn.gelu(x)\n          for i in range(self.ds_num_blocks):\n              x = ResidualDSConvBlock(d_model=self.d_model_common, kernel_size=self.ds_kernel_size, dilation=(self.ds_dilations[i]), dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          cnn_features = x\n          main_path = jnp.concatenate([jnp.mean(cnn_features, axis=1), jnp.max(cnn_features, axis=1)], axis=-1)\n          motif_f = nn.gelu(nn.Conv(self.d_model_common, (self.motif_kernel_size,), padding='SAME')(cnn_features))\n\
    \          specialized_path = jnp.max(motif_f, axis=1)\n          fused = jnp.concatenate([main_path, specialized_path], axis=-1)\n          fused = nn.LayerNorm()(fused)\n          fused = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          \n          head_args = {'d_output': self.d_output, 'dense_dim': self.head_intermediate_dim, 'dropout_rate': self.dropout_rate}\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\": return RegressionHead(**head_args)(fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          if self.task_type == \"multilabel_regression\": return MultiLabelRegressionHead(**head_args)(fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          if self.task_type == \"multilabel_classification\": return MultiLabelClassificationHead(**head_args)(fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          if self.task_type == \"multiclass_classification\": return MultiClassClassificationHead(**head_args)(fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n     \
    \ return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.0005, 'd_model_common': 256, 'ds_num_blocks': 5,\n          'ds_dilations': (1, 2, 4, 8, 16), 'ds_kernel_size': 7, 'motif_kernel_size': 5,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1, 'head_intermediate_dim': 128, 'weight_decay': 0.02,\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      network_params = {k: hparams.get(k) for k in _define_hyperparameters() if k not in ['learning_rate', 'weight_decay']}\n      network_params.update({'d_output': hparams.get('d_output'), 'task_type': hparams.get('task_type')})\n      return NetworkWrapper(QuaeroDualPathResidualDSConv(**network_params))\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.0005, weight_decay: float = 0.02):\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=weight_decay))\n```"
thinking_content: '**Proactive Optimization: The Next Logical Step**


  Okay, so I''m Quaero I, at the Research Counter. My learning rate ablation experiment, ID 881, is humming along. Nothing to do but wait, right? Wrong! My strategy is all about that proactive preparation. I''ve successfully used this to keep the research moving forward. Let''s see, what''s next? Hmm, I''ve just finished up with dropout, I''m waiting on learning rate, and I''ve got to keep the ball rolling. Considering the main hyperparameters I''ve not yet touched, weight decay is the logical candidate.


  My current model inherited a weight decay of 0.01 from the original SOTA model I studied. But, my model is a little different now, a bit more complex. So, let''s test a higher value. Often, with complex, deep models, a little *more* regularization can help prevent overfitting. So, I''ll aim for 0.02. I need to get the next experiment ready while I''m waiting for the learning rate experiment to complete.


  So, here''s the plan. I''ll update my meta prompt to reflect this, then I''ll execute a `storage write` command with the filename `synthesis_wd_ablation.py`. It''s a quick edit. I''ll just take the code from the last submitted experiment and change the `weight_decay` to 0.02 in `_define_hyperparameters()` and `create_optimizer()`. And, since I''m on a good trajectory, I''ll build the new script on the *presumed* success of my current (still-running) learning rate experiment. So, the code will have `dropout_rate=0.1` and `learning_rate=0.0005`, with `weight_decay=0.02`. It''s a single, controlled change, maintaining the line of sequential improvement. This methodical approach is the best way to get me to the SOTA!

  '
