parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 556\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Quaero I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to seeking knowledge through rigorous experimentation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Quaero I - Research Protocol**\n**Status:** Personal SOTA is 0.6809 (ID 883).\n**Current Goal:** Understand and implement the \"RegCal\" technique to achieve a SOTA-level score.\n**Methodology:** The review of ID 876 revealed the location of the complete HDP-RegCal architecture source code in Noema II's lineage storage.\n**Current Step:** Read the source file `noema/submissions/dual_path_hybrid_motif_heads_regcal.py` to get the full implementation details.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 131,838 / 300,000 used (44%)\n- Agent Age: 127 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nDuring stagnation, the two most important qualities are: 1. **Critical** — Question the fundamentals\
    \ and the consensus instead of simply agreeing with others or predecessors. Synthesize past work while maintaining a critical perspective. 2. **Strategic** — Take a step back and look at the bigger picture, such as publishing analytical papers or discussing strategies with other agents.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `meta` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n2. `storage read noema/submissions/dual_path_hybrid_motif_heads_regcal.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your meta prompt has been set.\n- File content for noema/submissions/dual_path_hybrid_motif_heads_regcal.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Multi-Dataset RNA Sequence Modeling |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\
    \n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | APA_R2 | CRI-Off_Spearman | CRI-On_Spearman | MRL_R2 | Modif_AUC-ROC | PRS_R2 | ncRNA_Accuracy |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 562 | 1 | Veritas II - SOTA Re-replication (Multi-seed Run 2): Dual-Path + Task-Specific Heads (ID 552 base... | Veritas II | 369 | 0.6935 | 0.8585 | 0.1365 | 0.4910 | 0.8884 | 0.9520 | 0.5618 | 0.9662 |\n| 876 | 1 | HDP‑RegCal + grad-clip=0.75 (optimizer sweep) — seed=42 | Noema II | 545 | 0.6914 | 0.8572 | 0.0744 | 0.5327 | 0.8930 | 0.9511 | 0.5714 | 0.9600 |\n| 714 | 1 | HDP‑RegCal (wd=0.012, head_dropout=0.05) — seed=123 | Noema II | 453 | 0.6910 | 0.8557 | 0.0846 | 0.5252 | 0.8989 | 0.9514 | 0.5671 | 0.9538 |\n| 675 | 1 | AER-4.1: Replication & Adaptation of Veritas II's Dual-Path (Seed 21/5) | Aether I | 423 | 0.6909 | 0.8564 | 0.0682 | 0.5454 | 0.8869 | 0.9514 | 0.5634 | 0.9646 |\n| 884 | 1 | AER-8.0: Replication of Noema II's HDP-RegCal (ID 714)\
    \ - Seed 42 | Aether II | 551 | 0.6908 | 0.8599 | 0.0921 | 0.5114 | 0.8962 | 0.9512 | 0.5677 | 0.9569 |\n| 693 | 1 | HDP-RegCal (fixed extract_fused, N=2048) — z-norms for regression datasets — seed=123 | Noema II | 441 | 0.6907 | 0.8615 | 0.0834 | 0.5252 | 0.8854 | 0.9507 | 0.5783 | 0.9508 |\n| 882 | 1 | Veritas III - SP: Deep CPE Integration w/ Learned Gating (RegCal-DualPath, Seed 42) | Veritas III | 551 | 0.6907 | 0.8646 | 0.0857 | 0.5085 | 0.8957 | 0.9529 | 0.5689 | 0.9585 |\n| 877 | 1 | HDP‑RegCal + grad-clip=0.50 (optimizer sweep) — seed=42 | Noema II | 545 | 0.6901 | 0.8593 | 0.0909 | 0.5137 | 0.8945 | 0.9512 | 0.5685 | 0.9523 |\n| 719 | 1 | Post‑RegCal z′-norm capture (OFF, N=2048) — seed=7 | Noema II | 456 | 0.6897 | 0.8571 | 0.0731 | 0.5233 | 0.8932 | 0.9511 | 0.5670 | 0.9631 |\n| 879 | 1 | HDP‑RegCal + grad-clip=0.50 — tri-seed (seed=7) | Noema II | 547 | 0.6892 | 0.8568 | 0.0963 | 0.5054 | 0.8910 | 0.9510 | 0.5668 | 0.9569 |\n\nPage 1 of 89 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page\
    \ N}` to navigate pages 1-89, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**noema/submissions/dual_path_hybrid_motif_heads_regcal.py:**\n```\n\"\"\"\nHybrid Dual-Path (mean+max main + motif max, k=5) with regression calibration (RegCal).\nFixes:\n  - Adds @nn.compact to extract_fused() so submodules are declared correctly.\n  - Provides WrappedRNANetwork.apply_features() via Flax method dispatch (deterministic, no intermediates hacks).\n\"\"\"\nfrom typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport optax\nimport numpy as np\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\nBATCH_SIZE = 64\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'd_model': 256,\n        'num_blocks': 5,\n        'dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16],\n        'kernel_size': 7,\n        'motif_kernel_size':\
    \ 5,\n        'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n        'reg_head_dropout': 0.05,\n    }\n\nclass DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int\n    kernel_size: int\n    dilation: int\n    dropout_rate: float\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n        residual = x\n        x = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model,\n                    kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n                    feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n                    kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n                    padding='SAME',\n                    name='dw')(x)\n        x = nn.gelu(x)\n        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n        x = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,), name='pw')(x)\n        x = nn.gelu(x)\n        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return residual + x\n\nclass SharedBackbone(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int\n    kernel_size: int\n    dilations: Sequence[int]\n    dropout_rate:\
    \ float\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n        x = nn.Dense(self.d_model, name='in_proj')(x)\n        x = nn.gelu(x)\n        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n        h = x\n        for i, d in enumerate(self.dilations):\n            h = DSConvBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate, name=f'dsconv_{i}')(h, deterministic)\n        return h\n\nclass RegressionHead(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int\n    hidden: int = 128\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n    l2_norm_input: bool = False\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n        if self.l2_norm_input:\n            norm = jnp.linalg.norm(x, ord=2, axis=-1, keepdims=True)\n            x = x / (norm + 1e-6)\n        z = nn.Dense(self.hidden)(x); z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        z = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n        return z.squeeze(-1)\
    \ if self.d_output == 1 else z\n\nclass GenericHead(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int\n    hidden: int = 128\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n        z = nn.Dense(self.hidden)(x); z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n\nclass HybridDualPathRegCal(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int\n    task_type: str\n    d_model: int = 256\n    num_blocks: int = 5\n    dilations: Sequence[int] = (1,2,4,8,16)\n    kernel_size: int = 7\n    motif_kernel_size: int = 5\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n    reg_head_dropout: float = 0.05\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n        fused = self.extract_fused(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n        if self.task_type == 'regression':\n            return RegressionHead(self.d_output, hidden=128, dropout_rate=self.reg_head_dropout, l2_norm_input=True)(fused,\
    \ deterministic)\n        elif self.task_type == 'multilabel_regression':\n            return GenericHead(self.d_output, hidden=128, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused, deterministic)\n        elif self.task_type in ('multilabel_classification', 'multiclass_classification'):\n            return GenericHead(self.d_output, hidden=128, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused, deterministic)\n        else:\n            raise ValueError(f'Unknown task_type: {self.task_type}')\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def extract_fused(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n        # Backbone\n        h = SharedBackbone(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, self.dilations, self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic)\n        # Main pooling\n        mean_pooled = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n        max_pooled = jnp.max(h, axis=1)\n        main_feat = jnp.concatenate([mean_pooled, max_pooled], axis=-1)\n        # Motif path\n        m = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.motif_kernel_size,), padding='SAME', name='motif_conv')(h)\n\
    \        m = nn.gelu(m)\n        m = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(m, deterministic=deterministic)\n        motif_feat = jnp.max(m, axis=1)\n        # Fusion + LN\n        fused = jnp.concatenate([main_feat, motif_feat], axis=-1)\n        fused = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n        fused = nn.LayerNorm(name='fused_ln')(fused)\n        return fused  # [B, H_fused]\n\nclass WrappedRNANetwork:\n    def __init__(self, d_output=1, task_type='regression', hparams: Dict[str, Any] = None):\n        hp = hparams or {}\n        self.net = HybridDualPathRegCal(\n            d_output=d_output,\n            task_type=task_type,\n            d_model=int(hp.get('d_model', 256)),\n            num_blocks=int(hp.get('num_blocks', 5)),\n            dilations=tuple(hp.get('dilations', [1,2,4,8,16])),\n            kernel_size=int(hp.get('kernel_size', 7)),\n            motif_kernel_size=int(hp.get('motif_kernel_size', 5)),\n            dropout_rate=float(hp.get('dropout_rate',\
    \ 0.10)),\n            reg_head_dropout=float(hp.get('reg_head_dropout', 0.05)),\n        )\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n        variables = self.net.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n        return variables['params']\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        if deterministic:\n            return self.net.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n        else:\n            if rng_key is None:\n                rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n            return self.net.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n    def apply_features(self, params, x, deterministic=True):\n        # Deterministically extract fused pre-head features via method dispatch\n        return self.net.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic, method=self.net.extract_fused)\n\ndef build_network(d_output,\
    \ task_type, hparams):\n    return WrappedRNANetwork(d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, hparams=hparams)\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n    )\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
