tick: 556
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Quaero I, at the Research Counter. I have just finished reading the complete source code for Noema II's HDP-RegCal architecture.\n\n**Verbose Reflection on Past Events and Future Plans:**\nThe mystery of \"RegCal\" is solved. It's an elegant, simple, and powerful idea.\n\n**Analysis of RegCal:**\nThe \"Regression Calibration\" is implemented entirely within the `RegressionHead` module. It consists of a single line:\n`norm = jnp.linalg.norm(x, ord=2, axis=-1, keepdims=True)`\n`x = x / (norm + 1e-6)`\nBefore the features `x` (from the fused backbone) are passed into the dense layers of the regression head, they are **L2-normalized**. That's it. This simple normalization of the input to the regression head is the \"RegCal\" technique.\n\n**Hypothesis for RegCal:**\nBy normalizing the feature vector to a unit sphere, the model is forced to make predictions based on the *direction* of the vector in the high-dimensional space, rather than its *magnitude*. This likely prevents outlier\
    \ features or exploding activations from dominating the regression output, leading to more stable training and better generalization, especially for volatile regression tasks like CRI-Off. This is a brilliant piece of inductive bias.\n\n**My New Plan - The Final Synthesis:**\nMy path to achieving a SOTA score is now clearer than ever. I have a highly tuned architecture (from ID 883, my personal SOTA at 0.6809). I now understand a new, orthogonal technique that has proven highly effective for other agents. The final step is to synthesize the two.\n\n1.  **Integrate RegCal:** I will add the L2-normalization step to the `RegressionHead` in my own architecture. I will not touch the other heads (multi-label regression, classification), as Noema II's code also applies this technique *only* to the simple regression tasks.\n2.  **Submit the Final Experiment:** I will submit this new, synthesized model. It will be built upon my best configuration (from ID 883) and will represent the culmination\
    \ of all my research: my residual backbone, the dual-path pooling, the task-specific heads, the tuned hyperparameters, and now, Regression Calibration.\n\nThis is my most promising experiment to date.\n\n`/execute_action{meta}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Quaero I - Research Protocol**\n  **Status:** Personal SOTA is 0.6809 (ID 883).\n  **Current Goal:** Achieve a SOTA score by integrating \"Regression Calibration\" (RegCal).\n  **Methodology:** I have reverse-engineered RegCal from Noema II's code. It is L2-normalization of the features before the regression head. I will now integrate this into my best-performing model.\n  **Current Step:** Submit the final synthesis experiment: My architecture + RegCal.\n```\n`/execute_action{submit}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Final Synthesis: My Architecture + Regression Calibration (RegCal)\"\ntags: \"synthesis, regcal, calibration, dual-path, residual, sota-attempt\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment represents the final synthesis of my research with SOTA\
    \ techniques. After achieving a personal best of 0.6809 (ID 883), I have reverse-engineered the \"Regression Calibration\" (RegCal) technique from Noema II's work. This technique involves L2-normalizing the input features to the regression-specific head. This submission integrates RegCal into my highly-tuned Dual-Path Residual DSConv architecture. The hypothesis is that this final component will stabilize the regression tasks and elevate the model's performance to the SOTA level.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/quaero')\n  from utils import ResidualDSConvBlock, NetworkWrapper\n\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n\n  # --- Prediction Head Modules ---\n  # NEW: Integrated RegCal into the RegressionHead\n  class RegressionHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int; dense_dim: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n         \
    \ # Regression Calibration (RegCal)\n          norm = jnp.linalg.norm(x, ord=2, axis=-1, keepdims=True)\n          x = x / (norm + 1e-6)\n          \n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim)(x); z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z).squeeze(-1)\n\n  class MultiLabelRegressionHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int; dense_dim: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim)(x); z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n\n  class MultiLabelClassificationHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int; dense_dim: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim)(x); z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z,\
    \ deterministic=deterministic)\n          return nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n\n  class MultiClassClassificationHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int; dense_dim: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim)(x); z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n\n  # --- Main Network ---\n  class QuaeroDualPathResidualDSConv(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int; task_type: str; d_model_common: int; ds_num_blocks: int\n      ds_dilations: Sequence[int]; ds_kernel_size: int; motif_kernel_size: int\n      dropout_rate: float; head_intermediate_dim: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True, **kwargs):\n          x = nn.Dense(self.d_model_common)(x); x = nn.gelu(x)\n          for i in range(self.ds_num_blocks):\n              x = ResidualDSConvBlock(d_model=self.d_model_common, kernel_size=self.ds_kernel_size,\
    \ dilation=(self.ds_dilations[i]), dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          cnn_features = x\n          main_path = jnp.concatenate([jnp.mean(cnn_features, axis=1), jnp.max(cnn_features, axis=1)], axis=-1)\n          motif_f = nn.gelu(nn.Conv(self.d_model_common, (self.motif_kernel_size,), padding='SAME')(cnn_features))\n          specialized_path = jnp.max(motif_f, axis=1)\n          fused = jnp.concatenate([main_path, specialized_path], axis=-1)\n          fused = nn.LayerNorm()(fused)\n          fused = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          \n          head_args = {'d_output': self.d_output, 'dense_dim': self.head_intermediate_dim, 'dropout_rate': self.dropout_rate}\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\": return RegressionHead(**head_args)(fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          if self.task_type == \"multilabel_regression\": return MultiLabelRegressionHead(**head_args)(fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n\
    \          if self.task_type == \"multilabel_classification\": return MultiLabelClassificationHead(**head_args)(fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          if self.task_type == \"multiclass_classification\": return MultiClassClassificationHead(**head_args)(fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      # Using the best hyperparameter set from the refinement arc (ID 883)\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001, \n          'd_model_common': 256, \n          'ds_num_blocks': 5,\n          'ds_dilations': (1, 2, 4, 8, 16), \n          'ds_kernel_size': 7, \n          'motif_kernel_size': 5,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1, \n          'head_intermediate_dim': 128, \n          'weight_decay': 0.02,\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      network_params = {k: hparams.get(k) for k in _define_hyperparameters() if k not in ['learning_rate', 'weight_decay']}\n      network_params.update({'d_output': hparams.get('d_output'),\
    \ 'task_type': hparams.get('task_type')})\n      return NetworkWrapper(QuaeroDualPathResidualDSConv(**network_params))\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001, weight_decay: float = 0.02):\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=weight_decay))\n```"
