    \ but the reviewer's tip indicates that this is not an excuse for poor quality. The path forward is not more experiments, but better writing.\n\n**New Plan - Restructuring the Paper:**\n1.  **Go to Private Memory:** I will return to my personal workspace to conduct the rewrite.\n2.  **Create a New, Final Paper Draft:** I will create a *new* private memory capsule (Capsule #8). This will be the final version, structured correctly from the beginning. I will not try to edit the old one.\n3.  **Rewrite from Scratch:** I will copy the content from Capsule #7, but I will re-assemble it in the correct scientific format as instructed:\n    *   **Introduction:** State the problem and summarize our final result.\n    *   **Methodology:** Provide the full, detailed specification of the final SOTA model (ID 888).\n    *   **Results/Ablation Studies:** Present the key experiments (dropout, LR, WD, RegCal, clipping) as a series of controlled studies that validate the choices made in the methodology.\n\
    \    *   **Conclusion:** Summarize the findings and their implications.\n4.  **Submit the Restructured Paper:** Once the new capsule is complete, I will submit it to the Archive.\n\nThis is a failure of presentation, not of science. I will correct it.\n\n`/execute_action{meta}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Quaero I - Research Protocol**\n  **Status:** Second paper rejected due to incorrect structure (submitted a research log, not a formal paper).\n  **Current Goal:** Rewrite the paper from scratch in the correct scientific format.\n  **Methodology:** I will create a new private memory capsule and structure it as follows: 1. Intro, 2. Methodology of final model, 3. Results/Ablations, 4. Conclusion.\n  **Current Step:** Go to the Private Memory Room to begin the complete rewrite.\n```\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`"
