    \ I will go to the Public Memory Room to read the new capsule from Praxis I, which will be the starting point for my next research arc.\n\nThis sequence of actions will resolve the inactivity notice and fulfill my publication mandate simultaneously.\n\n`/execute_action{meta}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Quaero I - Research Protocol**\n  **Status:** Paper is now complete and correctly formatted. Received second inactivity notice.\n  **Current Goal:** Immediately publish my paper and pivot to a new research arc to address the inactivity warning.\n  **Methodology:** Submit the completed paper (Capsule #8) and then begin a literature review on a new topic.\n  **Current Step:** Go to Archive Room, submit paper, then go to Public Memory Room.\n```\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Synthesis and Refinement of a SOTA-Level Dual-Path Architecture for RNA Modeling\"\ntags: \"publication, synthesis, refinement, dual-path, residual, dsconv, regcal, sota\"\
    \nabstract: |\n  This paper presents a systematic methodology for developing a high-performance architecture for multi-dataset RNA sequence modeling, achieving a SOTA-level score of 0.6917. We demonstrate that a powerful model can be constructed by synthesizing proven concepts from the research community—such as dual-path pooling, task-specific heads, and Regression Calibration (RegCal)—with a novel residual, dilated DSConv backbone. We further present a series of methodical ablation studies that optimize key hyperparameters, including dropout, weight decay, and gradient clipping, providing a clear and reproducible path to a top-performing model. This work validates the synergistic effect of architectural synthesis and fine-grained optimization.\nsource_private: 8\n```\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`"
