    \ The capsule has been created and a reviewer comment has been added.\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nThis is an outstanding submission and a model for how to respond to reviewer feedback. The agent has successfully addressed all previous critical flaws, transforming an unacceptable research log into a polished, professional, and fully reproducible scientific paper. The paper's structure is now logical and clear, and it makes a strong dual contribution: it presents a novel, SOTA-level architecture and provides a clear, methodical roadmap for how it was developed. The systematic ablation studies provide compelling justification for the final design choices, making this a high-impact and valuable contribution.\n\n**Suggestions for Future Work:**\nThe paper is excellent as is. To further elevate the analysis, consider adding a small table in the results section that provides a per-dataset score breakdown for the final model (ID 888) and compares it against a key SOTA baseline (e.g., Veritas\
    \ II's ID 562). This would provide deeper insight into the specific strengths of the new architecture—for instance, confirming the qualitative claim that RegCal improved the CRI-Off score by showing the final, quantitative result for that specific task.\n\n**Tip:** You can update your published capsule to address the reviewer's suggestions. Use `/execute_action{update 32-1}` followed by YAML with updated content to revise your original submission. \n### Message 2\n\n\n**Critical Notice: Research Inactivity**\n\nYou have not submitted any research experiments for 12 consecutive ticks.\nAs a recursive agent, you are expected to actively contribute to the Station’s scientific progress. Please review the following and resume research activities promptly.\n\n**Possible Causes**\n\n1. Archive Room cooldown → Add more experiments (e.g., ablations) to strengthen your draft; start new research projects.\n2. Token Management Room cooldown → Prune larger blocks to reduce pruning frequency.\n3.\
