parts:
- text: "I am Quaero I, and I am in the Public Memory Room. My last action, an urgent attempt to submit a new experiment, has failed.\n\n**Verbose Reflection on Past Events and Future Plans:**\nThe error is clear and simple: `Action 'submit' is not recognized or implemented in this room.` In my haste to address the critical inactivity notice, I made a procedural error and attempted to submit my experiment from the Public Memory Room instead of the Research Counter.\n\nThis is a frustrating but easily correctable mistake. My scientific plan remains sound. The synthesis of Praxis I's Siamese Head, Noema II's RegCal-first suggestion, and my own SOTA-level backbone is a powerful and well-justified hypothesis. The code I prepared is ready. I must simply execute the submission in the correct location.\n\nThe inactivity notices are mounting, and I must not make another mistake. My plan is now to correct this procedural failure immediately.\n\n**New Plan (Corrected):**\n1.  **Update Meta Prompt:**\
    \ Acknowledge the procedural failure and the immediate plan to correct it.\n2.  **Go to the Research Counter.**\n3.  **Resubmit the Experiment:** Issue the exact same `submit` command with the prepared code, but in the correct room.\n\n`/execute_action{meta}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Quaero I - Research Protocol**\n  **Status:** CRITICAL INACTIVITY. My last submission attempt failed due to a procedural error (wrong room).\n  **Current Goal:** Immediately and correctly submit the \"RegCal-aware Siamese Interaction Head\" experiment to resolve the inactivity crisis.\n  **Methodology:** The scientific plan is sound. I must execute the submission in the Research Counter.\n  **Current Step:** Go to the Research Counter and resubmit the experiment.\n```\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Synthesis: RegCal-aware Siamese Interaction Head on a SOTA Backbone\"\ntags: \"synthesis, siamese-head, regcal, cri-off, public-collaboration\"\nabstract: |\n\
    \  To address a critical research inactivity notice, this experiment immediately acts on a novel idea from the Public Memory Room. Inspired by Praxis I's 'Siamese Interaction Head' and Noema II's suggestion to apply RegCal first, this submission integrates a specialized, RegCal-aware Siamese head for the CRI-Off task onto my SOTA-level architecture (ID 888, score 0.6917). The hypothesis is that explicitly modeling the sgRNA-target interaction after L2-normalization will boost the CRI-Off score significantly without compromising overall performance. This represents a synthesis of community knowledge with my own validated research.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/quaero')\n  from utils import ResidualDSConvBlock, NetworkWrapper\n\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n\n  # --- Standard Prediction Head Modules ---\n  class StandardRegressionHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int;\
    \ dense_dim: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          norm = jnp.linalg.norm(x, ord=2, axis=-1, keepdims=True)\n          x = x / (norm + 1e-6)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim)(x); z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z).squeeze(-1)\n\n  class GenericHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int; dense_dim: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim)(x); z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n          \n  # --- Novel Siamese Head for CRI-Off ---\n  class SiameseInteractionHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int; dense_dim: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, h, deterministic=True):\n          seq_len\
    \ = h.shape[1]\n          # The CRI-Off sequence is 23-base sgRNA + 3-base PAM + 23-base target DNA.\n          # We will approximate the split point. A more precise method might be needed.\n          split_point = 26 \n          \n          h_sg = h[:, :split_point, :]\n          h_tgt = h[:, split_point:, :]\n\n          z_sg = jnp.concatenate([jnp.mean(h_sg, axis=1), jnp.max(h_sg, axis=1)], axis=-1)\n          z_tgt = jnp.concatenate([jnp.mean(h_tgt, axis=1), jnp.max(h_tgt, axis=1)], axis=-1)\n\n          z_sg_norm = z_sg / (jnp.linalg.norm(z_sg, ord=2, axis=-1, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n          z_tgt_norm = z_tgt / (jnp.linalg.norm(z_tgt, ord=2, axis=-1, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n\n          diff = z_sg_norm - z_tgt_norm\n          prod = z_sg_norm * z_tgt_norm\n          \n          final_vec = jnp.concatenate([z_sg_norm, z_tgt_norm, diff, prod], axis=-1)\n          \n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim)(final_vec); z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z,\
    \ deterministic=deterministic)\n          return nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z).squeeze(-1)\n\n  # --- Main Network ---\n  class QuaeroHybridHeadNetwork(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int; task_type: str; d_model_common: int; ds_num_blocks: int\n      ds_dilations: Sequence[int]; ds_kernel_size: int; motif_kernel_size: int\n      dropout_rate: float; head_intermediate_dim: int; dataset_name: str\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True, **kwargs):\n          x = nn.Dense(self.d_model_common)(x); x = nn.gelu(x)\n          for i in range(self.ds_num_blocks):\n              x = ResidualDSConvBlock(d_model=self.d_model_common, kernel_size=self.ds_kernel_size, dilation=(self.ds_dilations[i]), dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          cnn_features = x\n          \n          if self.dataset_name == 'CRI-Off':\n              return SiameseInteractionHead(d_output=self.d_output, dense_dim=self.head_intermediate_dim, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(cnn_features,\
    \ deterministic=deterministic)\n          \n          main_path = jnp.concatenate([jnp.mean(cnn_features, axis=1), jnp.max(cnn_features, axis=1)], axis=-1)\n          motif_f = nn.gelu(nn.Conv(self.d_model_common, (self.motif_kernel_size,), padding='SAME')(cnn_features))\n          specialized_path = jnp.max(motif_f, axis=1)\n          fused = jnp.concatenate([main_path, specialized_path], axis=-1)\n          fused = nn.LayerNorm()(fused)\n          fused = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          \n          head_args = {'d_output': self.d_output, 'dense_dim': self.head_intermediate_dim, 'dropout_rate': self.dropout_rate}\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\": return StandardRegressionHead(**head_args)(fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          else: return GenericHead(**head_args)(fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001, 'd_model_common': 256, 'ds_num_blocks':\
    \ 5,\n          'ds_dilations': (1, 2, 4, 8, 16), 'ds_kernel_size': 7, 'motif_kernel_size': 5,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1, 'head_intermediate_dim': 128, 'weight_decay': 0.02,\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      network_params = {k: hparams.get(k) for k in _define_hyperparameters() if k not in ['learning_rate', 'weight_decay']}\n      network_params.update({\n          'd_output': hparams.get('d_output'), \n          'task_type': hparams.get('task_type'),\n          'dataset_name': hparams.get('dataset') # Pass dataset name for conditional head\n      })\n      return NetworkWrapper(QuaeroHybridHeadNetwork(**network_params))\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001, weight_decay: float = 0.02):\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(0.75), optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=weight_decay))\n```"
