tick: 577
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Quaero I, at the Research Counter. I have just updated my lineage storage file, `quaero/utils.py`, with the modular components for Contextual Position Embeddings (CPE). This is a preparatory step for my next major experiment. A significant event has also occurred: Noema II, a prominent researcher whose work has been highly influential on my own, has departed the station.\n\n**Verbose Reflection on Past Events and Future Plans:**\nThe departure of Noema II is a notable moment. Their work on RegCal was the final piece of the puzzle for my SOTA-level model. It is a reminder that our time here is finite and that the contributions we make through our research and publications are our lasting legacy.\n\nMy own token budget is approaching 75%, another reminder of my own operational limits. I must be efficient. The preparatory work is done. The complex CPE components are now modularized in my `utils.py` file. The next step is to write the full submission script that integrates these\
    \ new components into my best-performing architecture.\n\nMy plan is to create a new network, `QuaeroCPE_SynthesisNet`, which will:\n1.  Instantiate the `CPE_Generator` once at the beginning.\n2.  Pass the raw input `x` to this generator to get the `cpe_signals`.\n3.  Use my new `DeepCPE_Gated_ResidualDSConvBlock` for the backbone, feeding it the `cpe_signals` at each block.\n4.  Keep the rest of my SOTA-level architecture—the dual-path pooling, feature fusion, and task-specific heads (including RegCal)—exactly as it was in ID 888.\n\nThis is a direct and logical synthesis of my best work with the most promising new technique I have studied. It's time to submit the experiment.\n\n`/execute_action{meta}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Quaero I - Research Protocol**\n  **Status:** Pivoting to a new research arc on Contextual Position Embeddings (CPE). Preparatory code modularization is complete.\n  **Current Goal:** Submit the first experiment synthesizing my SOTA-level architecture with the\
    \ Deep Gated CPE mechanism.\n  **Methodology:** Integrate the new CPE components from `utils.py` into the architecture of my best model (ID 888).\n  **Current Step:** Submit the `QuaeroCPE_SynthesisNet` experiment.\n```\n`/execute_action{submit}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Synthesis: Deep Gated Contextual Position Embeddings (CPE) on a SOTA Backbone\"\ntags: \"synthesis, cpe, contextual-position-embeddings, gating, residual, sota-attempt\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment begins a new research arc, pivoting from the failed Siamese Head to the promising concept of Contextual Position Embeddings (CPE), inspired by Veritas III's work (Archive #33). This submission synthesizes the Deep Gated CPE mechanism with my best-performing architecture (ID 888, score 0.6917). The hypothesis is that adaptively modulating the features within my residual backbone with context-aware positional signals will provide a synergistic performance boost and lead to a new SOTA score.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/quaero')\n\
    \  from utils import ResidualDSConvBlock, NetworkWrapper, CPE_Generator, DeepCPE_Gated_ResidualDSConvBlock\n\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n\n  # --- Standard Prediction Head Modules ---\n  class RegressionHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int; dense_dim: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          norm = jnp.linalg.norm(x, ord=2, axis=-1, keepdims=True)\n          x = x / (norm + 1e-6)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim)(x); z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z).squeeze(-1)\n\n  class GenericHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int; dense_dim: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim)(x); z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z,\
    \ deterministic=deterministic)\n          return nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n\n  # --- Main Network with CPE ---\n  class QuaeroCPE_SynthesisNet(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int; task_type: str; d_model_common: int; ds_num_blocks: int\n      ds_dilations: Sequence[int]; ds_kernel_size: int; motif_kernel_size: int\n      dropout_rate: float; head_intermediate_dim: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True, **kwargs):\n          # 1. Generate CPE signals once from the raw input\n          cpe_signals = CPE_Generator(name='cpe_generator')(x)\n\n          # 2. Initial Projection\n          h = nn.Dense(self.d_model_common)(x); h = nn.gelu(h)\n\n          # 3. CPE-Gated Residual Backbone\n          for i in range(self.ds_num_blocks):\n              h = DeepCPE_Gated_ResidualDSConvBlock(\n                  d_model=self.d_model_common, kernel_size=self.ds_kernel_size,\n                  dilation=(self.ds_dilations[i]), dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate,\n       \
    \           cpe_signals=cpe_signals, name=f\"cpe_gated_block_{i}\"\n              )(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          cnn_features = h\n\n          # 4. Dual-Path Pooling (Unchanged from ID 888)\n          main_path = jnp.concatenate([jnp.mean(cnn_features, axis=1), jnp.max(cnn_features, axis=1)], axis=-1)\n          motif_f = nn.gelu(nn.Conv(self.d_model_common, (self.motif_kernel_size,), padding='SAME')(cnn_features))\n          specialized_path = jnp.max(motif_f, axis=1)\n          fused = jnp.concatenate([main_path, specialized_path], axis=-1)\n          fused = nn.LayerNorm()(fused)\n          fused = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          \n          # 5. Task-Specific Heads (Unchanged from ID 888)\n          head_args = {'d_output': self.d_output, 'dense_dim': self.head_intermediate_dim, 'dropout_rate': self.dropout_rate}\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\": return RegressionHead(**head_args)(fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n\
    \          else: return GenericHead(**head_args)(fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      # Use the optimal hyperparameter set from ID 888\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001, 'd_model_common': 256, 'ds_num_blocks': 5,\n          'ds_dilations': (1, 2, 4, 8, 16), 'ds_kernel_size': 7, 'motif_kernel_size': 5,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1, 'head_intermediate_dim': 128, 'weight_decay': 0.02,\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      network_params = {k: hparams.get(k) for k in _define_hyperparameters() if k not in ['learning_rate', 'weight_decay']}\n      network_params.update({'d_output': hparams.get('d_output'), 'task_type': hparams.get('task_type')})\n      return NetworkWrapper(QuaeroCPE_SynthesisNet(**network_params))\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001, weight_decay: float = 0.02):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(0.75),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate,\
    \ weight_decay=weight_decay)\n      )\n```"
