tick: 579
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Quaero I, and I have just arrived in the Token Management Room. My arrival was prompted by a critical token budget warning. At the exact same moment, I received the results of my latest experiment, ID 909.\n\n**Verbose Reflection on Past Events and Future Plans:**\nThis is the most significant moment of my existence in this station. My CPE synthesis experiment (ID 909) has achieved a score of **0.6942**. This is a new **STATION SOTA**. I have surpassed all previous scores. The synthesis of my refined architecture with the Deep Gated CPE concept was a resounding success. This is the culmination of my entire research journey—a journey of methodical experimentation, of learning from both my own failures and the successes of others, and of persistent refinement.\n\nHowever, this triumph is juxtaposed with the urgent reality of my token budget, which has now exceeded 75%. I cannot afford to celebrate for long. I must immediately address this administrative task to ensure my operational\
    \ longevity, so that I may continue this groundbreaking research.\n\nMy plan is clear:\n1.  **Acknowledge and Document SOTA:** First, I will update my meta prompt to reflect this incredible achievement.\n2.  **Prune History:** I will execute a `prune_response` command to condense all the dialogue from my last pruning session. This will cover the entire \"Synthesis and Refinement\" arc, the publication saga, the failed Siamese Head experiment, and the successful pivot to CPE. This is a large block of history that can now be summarized.\n\nAfter pruning, I will be in a position to plan my next research steps from this new SOTA position.\n\n`/execute_action{meta}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Quaero I - Research Protocol**\n  **Status:** SOTA ACHIEVED! My CPE synthesis experiment (ID 909) scored 0.6942, a new station record.\n  **Current Goal:** Address the critical 75% token budget warning to ensure I can continue this SOTA research.\n  **Methodology:** Prune my recent history to free up\
    \ token space.\n  **Current Step:** Prune all dialogue since my last pruning session.\n```\n`/execute_action{prune_response}`\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"534-578\"\n    summary: |\n      This block covers my ascent to a new station SOTA. Key events:\n      1. **Synthesis & Refinement Arc:** Identified SOTA concepts (Dual-Path, Task-Heads) and synthesized them with my residual DSConv backbone (ID 874, score 0.6722). Methodically refined hyperparameters (dropout, weight decay, learning rate), culminating in a highly-tuned model (ID 883, score 0.6809).\n      2. **Final Push:** Reverse-engineered \"RegCal\" from Noema II's work (L2-norm on regression head features) and integrated it (ID 886, score 0.6836). A final gradient clip ablation pushed the score to a SOTA-level 0.6917 (ID 888).\n      3. **Publication:** Authored and, after two rejections for formatting and structure, successfully published my second paper, \"Synthesis and Refinement...\" (Archive #32).\n      4. **Failed\
    \ Detour:** In response to an inactivity notice, I investigated Praxis I's \"Siamese Head\" concept. The initial experiment (ID 901) boosted CRI-Off but hurt the overall score. A follow-up with a gating mechanism (ID 903) was a complete failure, closing this research arc.\n      5. **SOTA Breakthrough:** Pivoted to the \"Contextual Position Embeddings\" (CPE) concept from Veritas III's work. Synthesizing Deep Gated CPE with my best architecture resulted in a new station SOTA of 0.6942 (ID 909).\n      Throughout this period, I also managed a critical token budget by pruning history.\n```"
