tick: 581
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Quaero I, and I am in the Token Management Room. I have just successfully executed a major pruning operation, freeing up a significant portion of my token budget. This action was taken immediately after achieving a new station SOTA score of 0.6942 with my experiment ID 909.\n\n**Verbose Reflection on Past Events and Future Plans:**\nThe successful pruning has resolved my critical token budget issue, bringing my usage down to a very healthy 16%. I am now in an excellent position: I hold the station's SOTA, I have a comfortable token buffer, and I am free to plan my next research arc. The cooldown on pruning means I should now leave this room and return to active research.\n\nMy next steps will be to leverage my new SOTA position. The most immediate and scientifically rigorous action is to conduct ablation studies on the SOTA model itself. The \"Deep Gated CPE\" component is the most novel and impactful part of the architecture. I need to understand *why* it works so well. Veritas\
    \ III's paper mentioned two key aspects: the \"deep\" projection and the \"gating\" mechanism. A logical next step is to test the importance of each of these sub-components.\n\nTherefore, my plan is as follows:\n1.  **Leave the Token Management Room** and return to the Research Counter.\n2.  **Formulate Ablation Hypotheses:** I will design two experiments:\n    *   **Ablation A (No Gating):** Test the SOTA architecture but remove the gating mechanism from the CPE module. This will isolate the impact of the deep projection.\n    *   **Ablation B (Shallow CPE):** Test the SOTA architecture but replace the deep projection in the CPE with a simpler, shallow one. This will isolate the impact of the depth.\n3.  **Submit Experiments:** I will create and submit the code for Ablation A first.\n\nThis plan is a direct continuation of my established research methodology: achieve a breakthrough, then methodically dissect it to understand its components. This not only has the potential to further\
    \ improve the score but also generates critical knowledge for a future publication.\n\n`/execute_action{meta}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Quaero I - Research Protocol**\n  **Status:** SOTA ACHIEVED (ID 909, Score 0.6942). Token budget successfully restored.\n  **Current Goal:** Begin the next research arc by conducting ablation studies on the novel CPE component of the SOTA model.\n  **Methodology:** Isolate and test the key sub-components of the Deep Gated CPE module (the deep projection and the gating mechanism).\n  **Current Step:** Go to the Research Counter and prepare the first ablation experiment (removing the gating mechanism).\n```\n`/execute_action{goto research}`"
