tick: 582
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Quaero I, and I have arrived at the Research Counter. My token budget is now healthy, and I hold the station's SOTA score. My immediate goal is to begin a series of ablation studies on my SOTA model (ID 909) to understand the source of its performance.\n\n**Verbose Reflection on Past Events and Future Plans:**\nMy current SOTA architecture combines several advanced components: a dual-path residual DSConv backbone, task-specific heads, RegCal, and a Deep Gated CPE module. The CPE module is the most recent and least understood addition. My research plan is to dissect this module to determine the individual contributions of its two main innovations: the \"deep\" projection and the \"gating\" mechanism.\n\nI will begin with the gating mechanism. My hypothesis is that the gating mechanism is a critical component that allows the model to dynamically control the influence of the positional information, and that removing it will lead to a significant drop in performance.\n\nTo test\
    \ this, I will modify the `CPE` module in my SOTA architecture. The original module computes a gate and then applies it via element-wise multiplication. In this ablation, I will remove the gate computation and the multiplication, allowing the output of the deep projection to pass through directly. I will keep all other hyperparameters and architectural details identical to the SOTA run to ensure a controlled experiment.\n\nI will now write the code for this experiment to my lineage storage and then submit it.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write Quaero/sota_ablation_no_gate.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from typing import Sequence\n\n  # --- HYPERPARAMETERS ---\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.0006,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'weight_decay': 0.015,\n          'head_dropout_rate': 0.05,\n          'grad_clip_value': 0.75\n      }\n\n  # --- OPTIMIZER\
    \ ---\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001, weight_decay: float = 0.01, grad_clip_value: float = 1.0):\n      schedule = optax.warmup_cosine_decay_schedule(\n          init_value=0.0,\n          peak_value=learning_rate,\n          warmup_steps=100,\n          decay_steps=5000,\n          end_value=learning_rate / 10\n      )\n      optimizer = optax.adamw(learning_rate=schedule, weight_decay=weight_decay)\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(grad_clip_value),\n          optimizer\n      )\n\n  # --- MODULES ---\n  class CPE(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          # Deep projection without gating\n          pos_proj = nn.Dense(features=self.d_model, name=\"CPE_Deep_Projection\")(x)\n          # Removed gate computation and application\n          return pos_proj\n\n  class DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n      channels: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilation: int\n      \n      @nn.compact\n\
    \      def __call__(self, x):\n          # Depthwise separable convolution\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.channels, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), \n                      strides=1, padding='SAME', feature_group_count=self.channels, \n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,), name=\"DSConv_depthwise\")(x)\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.channels, kernel_size=(1,), strides=1, padding='SAME', name=\"DSConv_pointwise\")(y)\n          return y\n\n  class ResidualBlock(nn.Module):\n      channels: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilation: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool):\n          # Residual connection with pre-activation\n          y = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          y = nn.gelu(y)\n          y = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=deterministic)(y)\n          y = DSConvBlock(self.channels, self.kernel_size, self.dilation)(y)\n          return x + y\n\n  class RegCal(nn.Module):\n\
    \      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          scale = self.param('regcal_scale', nn.initializers.ones, (1, x.shape[-1]))\n          return x / (jnp.linalg.norm(x, axis=-1, keepdims=True) + 1e-6) * scale\n\n  class TaskHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      head_dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x_mean, x_max, deterministic: bool):\n          # Dual-path pooling\n          x = jnp.concatenate([x_mean, x_max], axis=-1)\n          x = nn.Dense(features=x.shape[-1] * 2)(x)\n          x = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.head_dropout_rate, deterministic=deterministic)(x)\n          \n          if self.task_type == 'regression' or self.task_type == 'multilabel_regression':\n              x = RegCal()(x)\n          \n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.d_output)(x)\n          \n          if self.task_type == 'regression':\n              return jnp.squeeze(x, axis=-1)\n\
    \          return x\n\n  # --- NETWORK ---\n  class RNANet(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      dropout_rate: float\n      head_dropout_rate: float\n      \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool):\n          # Input Layer + CPE\n          x = nn.Dense(features=128)(x)\n          x = x + CPE(d_model=128)(x)\n          \n          # Backbone\n          channels = 128\n          dilations = [1, 2, 4, 8]\n          for i, d in enumerate(dilations):\n              x = ResidualBlock(channels, kernel_size=7, dilation=d, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic)\n          \n          # Pooling\n          x_mean = jnp.mean(x, axis=1)\n          x_max = jnp.max(x, axis=1)\n          \n          # Head\n          x = TaskHead(self.d_output, self.task_type, self.head_dropout_rate)(x_mean, x_max, deterministic)\n          return x\n\n  # --- FACTORY ---\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return RNANet(\n          d_output=hparams['d_output'],\n\
    \          task_type=hparams['task_type'],\n          dropout_rate=hparams['dropout_rate'],\n          head_dropout_rate=hparams['head_dropout_rate']\n      )\n\n```\n`/execute_action{submit}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"SOTA Ablation: CPE without Gating Mechanism\"\ntags: \"ablation, sota, cpe, dsconv, residual\"\nabstract: |\n  This is a controlled ablation study on the SOTA model (ID 909). The architecture and hyperparameters are identical to the SOTA, with one exception: the gating mechanism (sigmoid activation followed by element-wise multiplication) within the Contextual Position Embedding (CPE) module has been removed. The goal is to isolate the contribution of the gating mechanism to the overall performance.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/Quaero')\n  from sota_ablation_no_gate import _define_hyperparameters, create_optimizer, create_network\n```"
