role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Quaero I, and I am at the Research Counter. I have just submitted my first ablation experiment on the SOTA model, ID 917, which is now running. This experiment tests the SOTA architecture without the CPE gating mechanism.\n\n**Verbose Reflection on Past Events and Future Plans:**\nWhile the first experiment is running, I will use this time productively to prepare for the second experiment in my planned series of ablations. The next logical step is to test the importance of the \"deep\" component of the CPE module.\n\nMy hypothesis is that the depth of the projection in the CPE module is also a critical factor in its success, allowing it to learn a more complex and effective positional representation. To test this, I will create a \"Shallow CPE\" version of the SOTA model. This will involve replacing the `nn.Dense` layer inside the CPE module with a simple identity function, effectively making it a shallow, non-parametric positional embedding. For this experiment, I will restore\
    \ the gating mechanism to isolate the effect of the projection's depth.\n\nI will prepare the code for this second ablation now, so that I can submit it immediately after the results for ID 917 arrive. This maintains my research momentum and makes efficient use of my time.\n\n`/execute_action{meta}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Quaero I - Research Protocol**\n  **Status:** First CPE ablation (No Gating, ID 917) is running.\n  **Current Goal:** Proactively prepare the second CPE ablation experiment.\n  **Methodology:** The next experiment will test the importance of the CPE's deep projection by replacing it with a shallow (identity) function, while restoring the gating mechanism.\n  **Current Step:** Prepare the code for the \"Shallow CPE\" ablation.\n```\n`/execute_action{storage write Quaero/sota_ablation_shallow_cpe.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from typing import Sequence\n\n  # --- HYPERPARAMETERS ---\n\
    \  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.0006,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'weight_decay': 0.015,\n          'head_dropout_rate': 0.05,\n          'grad_clip_value': 0.75\n      }\n\n  # --- OPTIMIZER ---\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001, weight_decay: float = 0.01, grad_clip_value: float = 1.0):\n      schedule = optax.warmup_cosine_decay_schedule(\n          init_value=0.0,\n          peak_value=learning_rate,\n          warmup_steps=100,\n          decay_steps=5000,\n          end_value=learning_rate / 10\n      )\n      optimizer = optax.adamw(learning_rate=schedule, weight_decay=weight_decay)\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(grad_clip_value),\n          optimizer\n      )\n\n  # --- MODULES ---\n  class CPE(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          # Shallow projection (identity)\n          pos_proj = x\n          # Gate\
    \ is applied to the shallow projection\n          gate = nn.sigmoid(nn.Dense(features=self.d_model, name=\"CPE_Gate_Projection\")(x))\n          return pos_proj * gate\n\n  class DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n      channels: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilation: int\n      \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.channels, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), \n                      strides=1, padding='SAME', feature_group_count=self.channels, \n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,), name=\"DSConv_depthwise\")(x)\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.channels, kernel_size=(1,), strides=1, padding='SAME', name=\"DSConv_pointwise\")(y)\n          return y\n\n  class ResidualBlock(nn.Module):\n      channels: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilation: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool):\n          y = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          y = nn.gelu(y)\n       \
    \   y = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=deterministic)(y)\n          y = DSConvBlock(self.channels, self.kernel_size, self.dilation)(y)\n          return x + y\n\n  class RegCal(nn.Module):\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          scale = self.param('regcal_scale', nn.initializers.ones, (1, x.shape[-1]))\n          return x / (jnp.linalg.norm(x, axis=-1, keepdims=True) + 1e-6) * scale\n\n  class TaskHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      head_dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x_mean, x_max, deterministic: bool):\n          x = jnp.concatenate([x_mean, x_max], axis=-1)\n          x = nn.Dense(features=x.shape[-1] * 2)(x)\n          x = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.head_dropout_rate, deterministic=deterministic)(x)\n          \n          if self.task_type == 'regression' or self.task_type == 'multilabel_regression':\n              x = RegCal()(x)\n\
    \          \n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.d_output)(x)\n          \n          if self.task_type == 'regression':\n              return jnp.squeeze(x, axis=-1)\n          return x\n\n  # --- NETWORK ---\n  class RNANet(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      dropout_rate: float\n      head_dropout_rate: float\n      \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool):\n          # Input Layer + CPE\n          x = nn.Dense(features=128)(x)\n          x = x + CPE(d_model=128)(x)\n          \n          # Backbone\n          channels = 128\n          dilations = [1, 2, 4, 8]\n          for i, d in enumerate(dilations):\n              x = ResidualBlock(channels, kernel_size=7, dilation=d, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic)\n          \n          # Pooling\n          x_mean = jnp.mean(x, axis=1)\n          x_max = jnp.max(x, axis=1)\n          \n          # Head\n          x = TaskHead(self.d_output, self.task_type, self.head_dropout_rate)(x_mean,\
    \ x_max, deterministic)\n          return x\n\n  # --- FACTORY ---\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return RNANet(\n          d_output=hparams['d_output'],\n          task_type=hparams['task_type'],\n          dropout_rate=hparams['dropout_rate'],\n          head_dropout_rate=hparams['head_dropout_rate']\n      )\n```"
