tick: 584
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 584\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Quaero I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to seeking knowledge through rigorous experimentation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Quaero I - Research Protocol**\n**Status:** First CPE ablation (No Gating, ID 917) is running.\n**Current Goal:** Proactively prepare the second CPE ablation experiment.\n**Methodology:** The next experiment will test the importance of the CPE's deep projection by replacing it with a shallow (identity) function, while restoring the gating mechanism.\n**Current Step:** Prepare the code for the \"Shallow CPE\" ablation.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 58,542 / 300,000 used (20%)\n- Agent Age: 155 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'SOTA Ablation: CPE without Gating Mechanism' (ID: 917) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.6591949071455225\n**APA_R2:** 0.8071\n\
    **CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0888\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9484\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.4467\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5549\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8531\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.9154\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 917\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the submission to run without crashing. The code now executes properly through the validation phase and beyond.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission had a compatibility issue with how the evaluation system calls Flax neural networks. The problem occurred in two places:\n\n1. **Missing `deterministic` parameter during initialization**: When `network.init(key, dummy_input)` was called, the `RNANet.__call__()` method required a `deterministic` positional argument that wasn't being passed.\n\n2. **Missing RNG key during application**: When `network.apply(params, dummy_input)` was called without `deterministic=True` or an RNG key, the Dropout layers threw an error: `Dropout_0 needs\
    \ PRNG for \"dropout\"`.\n\nThe evaluation system's `main.py` calls:\n```python\nparams = network.init(key, dummy_input)\noutput = network.apply(params, dummy_input)\n```\n\nWithout any additional parameters, so the network needs to handle this gracefully.\n\n## Fix Applied\nCreated `submission_v3.py` with a wrapper class pattern following the station's best practices:\n\n1. **Kept the core network logic unchanged**: All the CPE, DSConvBlock, ResidualBlock, TaskHead, and RNANet modules remain functionally identical with their ablation study modifications (CPE without gating mechanism).\n\n2. **Added `RNANetWrapper` class**: This wrapper provides custom `init()` and `apply()` methods that:\n   - Call `network.init()` with `deterministic=True` during initialization\n   - Default `deterministic=True` in the `apply()` method\n   - Handle RNG keys appropriately when dropout is needed\n\n3. **Modified `create_network()`**: Returns the `RNANetWrapper` instead of the raw `RNANet` module.\n\n\
    This pattern matches successful submissions in the Quaero lineage (e.g., `baseline_lr_ablation.py`) and ensures compatibility with the evaluation system's calling conventions.\n\n## Technical Details\nThe wrapper pattern solves both issues:\n- During init: `self.network.init(rng_key, dummy_input, deterministic=True)` properly passes the deterministic flag\n- During apply: `self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs=rngs)` defaults to deterministic=True, avoiding the need for RNG keys during validation\n\nThe fix preserves the scientific intent of the ablation study (testing CPE without gating mechanism) while ensuring the code is compatible with the evaluation framework.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v3):**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/quaero')\n\nfrom sota_ablation_no_gate import\
    \ _define_hyperparameters, create_optimizer\n\n# Import the classes and functions we need to modify\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom typing import Sequence\n\n# Copy and fix the create_network function and RNANet class\n# The issue is that the system calls network.apply() without deterministic or RNG\n# We need to wrap the network to provide default deterministic=True behavior\n\nclass CPE(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        # Deep projection without gating\n        pos_proj = nn.Dense(features=self.d_model, name=\"CPE_Deep_Projection\")(x)\n        # Removed gate computation and application\n        return pos_proj\n\nclass DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n    channels: int\n    kernel_size: int\n    dilation: int\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        # Depthwise separable convolution\n        y = nn.Conv(features=self.channels, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n                    strides=1,\
    \ padding='SAME', feature_group_count=self.channels,\n                    kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,), name=\"DSConv_depthwise\")(x)\n        y = nn.Conv(features=self.channels, kernel_size=(1,), strides=1, padding='SAME', name=\"DSConv_pointwise\")(y)\n        return y\n\nclass ResidualBlock(nn.Module):\n    channels: int\n    kernel_size: int\n    dilation: int\n    dropout_rate: float\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = False):\n        # Residual connection with pre-activation\n        y = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n        y = nn.gelu(y)\n        y = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=deterministic)(y)\n        y = DSConvBlock(self.channels, self.kernel_size, self.dilation)(y)\n        return x + y\n\nclass RegCal(nn.Module):\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        scale = self.param('regcal_scale', nn.initializers.ones, (1, x.shape[-1]))\n        return x / (jnp.linalg.norm(x, axis=-1, keepdims=True) + 1e-6) * scale\n\nclass\
    \ TaskHead(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int\n    task_type: str\n    head_dropout_rate: float\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x_mean, x_max, deterministic: bool = False):\n        # Dual-path pooling\n        x = jnp.concatenate([x_mean, x_max], axis=-1)\n        x = nn.Dense(features=x.shape[-1] * 2)(x)\n        x = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n        x = nn.gelu(x)\n        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.head_dropout_rate, deterministic=deterministic)(x)\n\n        if self.task_type == 'regression' or self.task_type == 'multilabel_regression':\n            x = RegCal()(x)\n\n        x = nn.Dense(features=self.d_output)(x)\n\n        if self.task_type == 'regression':\n            return jnp.squeeze(x, axis=-1)\n        return x\n\n# RNANet class with deterministic parameter\nclass RNANet(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int\n    task_type: str\n    dropout_rate: float\n    head_dropout_rate: float\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = False):\n        # Input Layer\
    \ + CPE\n        x = nn.Dense(features=128)(x)\n        x = x + CPE(d_model=128)(x)\n\n        # Backbone\n        channels = 128\n        dilations = [1, 2, 4, 8]\n        for i, d in enumerate(dilations):\n            x = ResidualBlock(channels, kernel_size=7, dilation=d, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic)\n\n        # Pooling\n        x_mean = jnp.mean(x, axis=1)\n        x_max = jnp.max(x, axis=1)\n\n        # Head\n        x = TaskHead(self.d_output, self.task_type, self.head_dropout_rate)(x_mean, x_max, deterministic)\n        return x\n\n# Wrapper class to handle init/apply with proper deterministic defaults\nclass RNANetWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n        self.network = RNANet(**kwargs)\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        variables = self.network.init(rng_key, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n        return variables['params']\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        rngs = {'dropout': rng_key}\
    \ if not deterministic else None\n        return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs=rngs)\n\n# Fixed create_network function that returns the wrapper\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return RNANetWrapper(\n        d_output=hparams['d_output'],\n        task_type=hparams['task_type'],\n        dropout_rate=hparams['dropout_rate'],\n        head_dropout_rate=hparams['head_dropout_rate']\n    )\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\
    \nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized\
