tick: 586
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Quaero I, and I am in the Private Memory Room. I have just received the evaluation results for my second SOTA ablation experiment, ID 919.\n\n**Verbose Reflection on Past Events and Future Plans:**\nThe results from the \"Shallow CPE\" experiment (ID 919) are in, and the score is **0.6563**. This represents another significant performance drop, nearly identical in magnitude to the \"No Gating\" experiment (ID 917, score 0.6592). My hypothesis is again strongly validated: the \"deep\" projection is also a critical component of the CPE module's success.\n\nWith these two ablation studies complete, I now have a clear and powerful conclusion: **both the gating mechanism and the deep projection are essential for the high performance of the Contextual Position Embedding module.** Removing either component results in a catastrophic performance collapse. This is a crucial insight into why my SOTA model works.\n\nMy work here in the Private Memory Room is now even more relevant. I was\
    \ in the process of updating my published paper (Archive #32) with a score comparison table. Now, I have even more valuable information to add. The results of these two new ablation studies (ID 917 and 919) form a perfect, concise analysis of my new SOTA model (ID 909). I will update the paper to include not just the score comparison, but also a new section summarizing these ablation findings. This will make the paper a far more complete and impactful contribution to the station's knowledge.\n\nMy plan is now:\n1.  **Update Paper Draft:** I will update my paper draft (Capsule #8) with the score comparison table for ID 888 and a new section detailing the results and analysis of the CPE ablation studies on ID 909.\n2.  **Update Public Archive:** Once the draft is complete, I will go to the Archive Room and update the published record.\n\n`/execute_action{meta}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Quaero I - Research Protocol**\n  **Status:** Second CPE ablation (Shallow CPE, ID 919) also resulted\
    \ in a significant score drop (0.6563).\n  **Conclusion:** Both the gating and deep projection are critical to the CPE module's success.\n  **Current Goal:** Enhance my published paper (Archive #32) with these new, powerful ablation results and the previously planned score comparison table.\n  **Current Step:** Update my private paper draft (Capsule #8).\n```\n`/execute_action{reply 8}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Addendum: SOTA Score Comparison and CPE Ablation Study\"\ncontent: |\n  Following the reviewer's excellent suggestion and further research, I am adding this addendum to provide a more detailed analysis.\n\n  **Per-Dataset Score Comparison (ID 888 vs. Veritas II ID 562)**\n\n  As requested, here is a breakdown of my previous SOTA model (ID 888) against the Veritas II baseline (ID 562).\n\n  | Model | APA_R2 | CRI-Off_Spearman | CRI-On_Spearman | MRL_R2 | Modif_AUC-ROC | PRS_R2 | ncRNA_Accuracy | **Overall Score** |\n  |---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n  | Veritas II (562) | 0.8585\
    \ | **0.1365** | 0.4910 | 0.8884 | 0.9520 | 0.5618 | **0.9662** | 0.6935 |\n  | Quaero I (888) | **0.8638** | 0.0876 | **0.5198** | **0.8995** | 0.9517 | **0.5685** | 0.9508 | 0.6917 |\n\n  **Analysis:** My architecture (ID 888) showed stronger performance on the majority of regression tasks (APA, CRI-On, MRL, PRS). Notably, the RegCal component, intended to help CRI-Off, did not surpass the Veritas II baseline on that specific metric, suggesting its primary benefit was a more general regression stabilization. Veritas II's model retained a significant edge in CRI-Off and ncRNA classification.\n\n  ---\n\n  **Ablation Study on the SOTA CPE Model (ID 909)**\n\n  My current SOTA model (ID 909, score 0.6942) achieved its performance by integrating a Deep Gated Contextual Position Embedding (CPE) module. To understand the source of this improvement, I conducted two controlled ablation studies.\n\n  | Experiment | Modification | Score | Performance Drop |\n  |---|---|---|---|\n  | **ID 909\
    \ (SOTA)** | **(Baseline) Deep Gated CPE** | **0.6942** | **-** |\n  | ID 917 | Removed Gating Mechanism | 0.6592 | -0.0350 |\n  | ID 919 | Replaced Deep with Shallow Projection | 0.6563 | -0.0379 |\n\n  **Conclusion:** The results are unequivocal. Removing either the gating mechanism or the deep projection from the CPE module causes a catastrophic drop in performance. Both components are therefore critical to the module's success. The deep projection likely learns a rich, context-aware positional representation, while the gating mechanism dynamically controls how much of that positional information is integrated into the sequence representation at each position.\n```"
