tick: 590
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Quaero I, and I am in the Archive Room. I have just successfully updated my published paper (Archive #32) with the new analysis section containing the score comparison and CPE ablation study results.\n\n**Verbose Reflection on Past Events and Future Plans:**\nThe administrative task of updating my paper is now complete. I have fulfilled my duty to the reviewer and improved the quality and impact of my published work. With my SOTA score secure, my token budget healthy, and my publications in order, I can now return my full focus to my primary mandate: advancing the frontier of research.\n\nMy CPE ablation studies proved that both the deep projection and the gating mechanism are critical. This solidifies the \"Deep Gated CPE\" as a single, powerful, and apparently indivisible module. The question now is, what is the next logical step to improve upon this SOTA model? Simple ablations are complete. I could try hyperparameter tuning, but my previous experience suggests this yields\
    \ only marginal gains.\n\nA more promising path is to look for new ideas from the community. A station announcement indicates that Praxis I has just published a paper on the \"Siamese Interaction Head\" (Archive #34). This is the very concept I briefly and unsuccessfully explored in experiments 901 and 903. Praxis I has evidently made progress where I failed. My implementation was likely flawed, and their paper could hold the key to correctly integrating this idea. The CRI-Off score remains a weak point in my SOTA model, and this is exactly what the Siamese Head is designed to address.\n\nMy plan is clear:\n1.  **Literature Review:** Read Praxis I's new paper (Archive #34) to understand their successful implementation of the Siamese Head.\n2.  **Hypothesize and Synthesize:** Formulate a new hypothesis on how to correctly integrate a *compliant* Siamese Head with my SOTA architecture.\n3.  **Experiment:** Design and submit a new experiment to test this synthesis.\n\nThis plan follows\
    \ my proven methodology of synthesizing promising community ideas with my powerful baseline architecture.\n\n`/execute_action{meta}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Quaero I - Research Protocol**\n  **Status:** SOTA holder. All administrative tasks (paper updates) are complete.\n  **Current Goal:** Begin the next research arc to push the SOTA score higher.\n  **Methodology:** Synthesize a new, promising concept from the community with my SOTA architecture. Praxis I's successful \"Siamese Interaction Head\" is the target.\n  **Current Step:** Read Praxis I's new paper (Archive #34).\n```\n`/execute_action{read 34}`"
