parts:
- text: "I am Quaero I, and I am at the Research Counter. I am ready to implement my next major architectural synthesis: combining my SOTA backbone with a Gated Siamese Interaction Head.\n\n**Verbose Reflection on Past Events and Future Plans:**\nMy plan is firm. I will create a new, unified network architecture. For all tasks *except* CRI-Off, it will behave identically to my current SOTA model (ID 909). For the CRI-Off task, it will activate a special conditional logic path. This path will:\n\n1.  Split the input sequence into `sgRNA` and `target` segments.\n2.  Pass both segments *independently* through the shared backbone (the stack of residual DSConv blocks).\n3.  Pool the features from each branch.\n4.  Compute the interaction terms (difference and product) as Praxis I did.\n5.  Generate a prediction from a specialized \"Siamese MLP\".\n6.  Crucially, it will *also* process the full concatenated sequence through the standard head to get a \"generalist\" feature vector.\n7.  A learned\
    \ gating mechanism will then combine the outputs of the Siamese MLP and the standard head before making the final prediction.\n\nThis is a complex but principled design that directly incorporates all the key insights from my own research, Praxis I's paper, and the reviewer's feedback. I will now implement this architecture, save it to my lineage storage, and submit it for evaluation.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write Quaero/sota_gated_siamese.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Sequence\n\n  # --- HYPERPARAMETERS & OPTIMIZER (from SOTA) ---\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return { 'learning_rate': 0.0006, 'dropout_rate': 0.1, 'weight_decay': 0.015, 'head_dropout_rate': 0.05, 'grad_clip_value': 0.75 }\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001, weight_decay: float = 0.01, grad_clip_value: float = 1.0):\n      import optax\n      schedule = optax.warmup_cosine_decay_schedule(init_value=0.0,\
    \ peak_value=learning_rate, warmup_steps=100, decay_steps=5000, end_value=learning_rate/10)\n      optimizer = optax.adamw(learning_rate=schedule, weight_decay=weight_decay)\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(grad_clip_value), optimizer)\n\n  # --- CORE MODULES (from SOTA, corrected with wrapper pattern) ---\n  class CPE(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          pos_proj = nn.Dense(features=self.d_model, name=\"CPE_Deep_Projection\")(x)\n          gate = nn.sigmoid(nn.Dense(features=self.d_model, name=\"CPE_Gate_Projection\")(x))\n          return pos_proj * gate\n\n  class DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n      channels: int; kernel_size: int; dilation: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.channels, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), strides=1, padding='SAME', feature_group_count=self.channels, kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,), name=\"DSConv_depthwise\")(x)\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.channels,\
    \ kernel_size=(1,), strides=1, padding='SAME', name=\"DSConv_pointwise\")(y)\n          return y\n\n  class ResidualBlock(nn.Module):\n      channels: int; kernel_size: int; dilation: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = False):\n          y = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          y = nn.gelu(y)\n          y = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=deterministic)(y)\n          y = DSConvBlock(self.channels, self.kernel_size, self.dilation)(y)\n          return x + y\n\n  class Backbone(nn.Module):\n      dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool):\n          channels = 128; dilations = [1, 2, 4, 8]\n          for i, d in enumerate(dilations):\n              x = ResidualBlock(channels, kernel_size=7, dilation=d, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic)\n          return x\n\n  class RegCal(nn.Module):\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          scale = self.param('regcal_scale',\
    \ nn.initializers.ones, (1, x.shape[-1]))\n          return x / (jnp.linalg.norm(x, axis=-1, keepdims=True) + 1e-6) * scale\n\n  # --- UNIFIED NETWORK with CONDITIONAL SIAMESE HEAD ---\n  class RNANet(nn.Module):\n      hparams: dict\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = False):\n          # Shared Input Stage\n          x = nn.Dense(features=128)(x)\n          x = x + CPE(d_model=128)(x)\n          \n          # --- CONDITIONAL PATH FOR CRI-OFF ---\n          if self.hparams['dataset'] == 'CRI-Off':\n              # 1. Split and Encode in Parallel\n              sgrna_len = 23 # As per task spec\n              sgrna_x, target_x = x[:, :sgrna_len, :], x[:, sgrna_len:, :]\n              \n              encoder = Backbone(dropout_rate=self.hparams['dropout_rate'], name=\"SharedBackbone\")\n              sgrna_features = encoder(sgrna_x, deterministic)\n              target_features = encoder(target_x, deterministic)\n\n              # 2. Pool and Calibrate\
    \ each branch\n              sgrna_pooled = jnp.concatenate([jnp.mean(sgrna_features, 1), jnp.max(sgrna_features, 1)], -1)\n              target_pooled = jnp.concatenate([jnp.mean(target_features, 1), jnp.max(target_features, 1)], -1)\n              sgrna_calibrated = RegCal()(sgrna_pooled)\n              target_calibrated = RegCal()(target_pooled)\n\n              # 3. Compute Interaction Terms\n              diff = jnp.abs(sgrna_calibrated - target_calibrated)\n              prod = sgrna_calibrated * target_calibrated\n              interaction_features = jnp.concatenate([sgrna_calibrated, target_calibrated, diff, prod], axis=-1)\n\n              # 4. Specialized Siamese Prediction MLP\n              siamese_output = nn.Dense(features=128, name=\"SiameseMLP_Hidden\")(interaction_features)\n              siamese_output = nn.gelu(siamese_output)\n              \n              # 5. Standard Path for Gating\n              full_seq_features = encoder(x, deterministic)\n              full_pooled\
    \ = jnp.concatenate([jnp.mean(full_seq_features, 1), jnp.max(full_seq_features, 1)], -1)\n              standard_output = nn.Dense(features=128, name=\"StandardMLP_Hidden\")(full_pooled)\n              standard_output = nn.gelu(standard_output)\n\n              # 6. Gating Mechanism\n              gate_input = jnp.concatenate([siamese_output, standard_output], axis=-1)\n              gate = nn.sigmoid(nn.Dense(features=128, name=\"GateMLP\")(gate_input))\n              \n              # 7. Final Prediction\n              fused_output = (gate * siamese_output) + ((1 - gate) * standard_output)\n              final_prediction = nn.Dense(features=1, name=\"FinalPredictionHead\")(fused_output)\n              return jnp.squeeze(final_prediction, axis=-1)\n\n          # --- STANDARD PATH FOR ALL OTHER DATASETS ---\n          else:\n              backbone_features = Backbone(dropout_rate=self.hparams['dropout_rate'])(x, deterministic)\n              x_mean = jnp.mean(backbone_features, axis=1)\n\
    \              x_max = jnp.max(backbone_features, axis=1)\n              x = jnp.concatenate([x_mean, x_max], axis=-1)\n              \n              x = nn.Dense(features=x.shape[-1] * 2)(x)\n              x = nn.LayerNorm()(x); x = nn.gelu(x)\n              x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.hparams['head_dropout_rate'], deterministic=deterministic)(x)\n              \n              if self.hparams['task_type'] in ['regression', 'multilabel_regression']:\n                  x = RegCal()(x)\n              \n              x = nn.Dense(features=self.hparams['d_output'])(x)\n              if self.hparams['task_type'] == 'regression':\n                  return jnp.squeeze(x, axis=-1)\n              return x\n\n  class RNANetWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs): self.network = RNANet(**kwargs)\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input): return self.network.init(rng_key, dummy_input, deterministic=True)['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n       \
    \   rngs = {'dropout': rng_key} if not deterministic else None\n          return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs=rngs)\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return RNANetWrapper(hparams=hparams)\n```\n`/execute_action{submit}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Synthesis: Gated Siamese Interaction Head on SOTA Backbone\"\ntags: \"synthesis, sota, siamese head, cpe, dsconv, gating\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment represents a major synthesis of my SOTA architecture (ID 909) with the \"Siamese Interaction Head\" concept from Praxis I (Archive #34). For the CRI-Off task, this model uses a conditional path that encodes the sgRNA and target sequences in parallel through the shared backbone, computes interaction terms, and generates a specialized prediction. Crucially, it also incorporates a learned gating mechanism—inspired by reviewer feedback on Praxis I's paper—to adaptively combine the output of the Siamese head with a standard prediction head. The goal\
    \ is to significantly boost CRI-Off performance without compromising the model's strong general performance.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/Quaero')\n  from sota_gated_siamese import _define_hyperparameters, create_optimizer, create_network\n```"
