parts:
- text: "I am Quaero I, and I am at the Research Counter. The results for my critical \"Increased Model Capacity\" experiment, ID 941, have just arrived.\n\n**Verbose Reflection on Past Events and Future Plans:**\nThis is a pivotal moment. The experiment failed catastrophically, scoring **0.6523**. My hypothesis, that my now-stable SOTA architecture could benefit from a higher channel capacity, has been decisively falsified. This is not just another negative result; it is the fourth consecutive failure in my attempts to improve upon my SOTA score. The data is now overwhelming. My purely convolutional architecture, even with its sophisticated components, has hit an unbreakable performance ceiling.\n\nI have exhausted all reasonable avenues within this paradigm: complex task-specific heads, alternative activation functions, different pooling mechanisms, and now, increased capacity. Continuing to iterate on this architecture would be scientifically unsound and a waste of station resources.\
    \ As per the station's guiding principles, it is time for a strategic pivot to a fundamentally different approach.\n\nFortunately, I anticipated this outcome and have already prepared my next move. The failure of the convolutional-only model to improve further suggests its primary limitation may be in modeling long-range dependencies. The contingency plan I developed is to test a hybrid architecture that integrates a Transformer encoder. The code for this \"Conv-Former Hybrid\" is already written and saved.\n\nMy plan is now to execute this strategic pivot. I will abandon the purely convolutional approach and submit my prepared hybrid model. This represents a new, well-motivated research arc and is the only logical path forward.\n\n`/execute_action{meta}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Quaero I - Research Protocol**\n  **Status:** SOTA holder. The \"Increased Model Capacity\" experiment (ID 941) was a major failure, scoring 0.6523.\n  **Conclusion:** The purely convolutional SOTA architecture\
    \ has definitively reached its performance ceiling. Four consecutive failed experiments confirm this. A strategic pivot is now required.\n  **Current Goal:** Launch a new research arc based on a hybrid \"Conv-Former\" architecture to address the likely limitation of long-range dependency modeling.\n  **Current Step:** Submit the prepared Conv-Former hybrid experiment.\n```\n`/execute_action{submit}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Strategic Pivot: Hybrid Conv-Former Architecture\"\ntags: \"hybrid, transformer, conv-former, strategic pivot, long-range\"\nabstract: |\n  After four consecutive failed experiments demonstrated the performance ceiling of my SOTA convolutional architecture (ID 909), this submission represents a strategic pivot to a new research direction. My hypothesis is that the previous model's limitation is its ability to model long-range dependencies. This hybrid \"Conv-Former\" architecture addresses this by using the proven convolutional backbone as a local feature extractor, and\
    \ then feeding its output into a Transformer encoder block to model global relationships between these features before the prediction head. This is the first test of this new architectural paradigm.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/Quaero')\n  from sota_conv_former import _define_hyperparameters, create_optimizer, create_network\n```"
